<p class=3DNormal1 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Plaintiffs
State Farm Mutual Automobile Insurance Company and State Farm Fire and Casu=
alty
Insurance Company (collectively, &quot;State Farm&quot;) provide automobile
insurance coverage in New York and are required under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5CT3-11P1-6RDJ-84H4-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>New York's
Comprehensive Motor Vehicle Insurance Reparations Act (&quot;No-Fault
Act&quot;)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-farea=
st-font-family:
Times;color:black'> to reimburse covered individuals injured in automobile
accidents for necessary health expenses, without regard to fault. <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See</i> </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5CT3-11P1-6RDJ-84H4-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>N.Y. Ins. Law
&sect;&sect; 5101-5109</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. Insureds can assign their No-F=
ault
benefits to health care providers, who can then seek reimbursement directly
from State Farm for treatment provided to the insureds. In this case, State
Farm alleges that Defendants, who are health care providers and related
individuals and entities that treat automobile accident victims, engaged in=
 a
massive scheme to fraudulently obtain No-Fault benefits by providing medica=
lly
unnecessary treatment and services pursuant to illegal &quot;pay-to-play&qu=
ot;
financial arrangements, seeking reimbursement of such claims from State Far=
m,
and then bringing thousands of baseless arbitrations&nbsp;[**4]&nbsp; and
state-court proceedings when State Farm denied the claims.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal1 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>State
Farm accordingly brought this lawsuit in the United States District Court f=
or
the Eastern District of New York, asserting claims under the </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Racketeer
Influenced and Corrupt Organizations Act (&quot;RICO&quot;), 18 U.S.C. &sec=
t;
1961 </span></i></a><a
