<p class=3DNormal1 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>I. New York's No-Fault Insurance
Regime</span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal1 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>New
York's No-Fault Act requires insurers to compensate victims of automobile
accidents for their injuries regardless of fault. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font=
-style:
normal'>See</i> </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5CT3-11P1-6RDJ-84H4-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>N.Y. Ins. Law
&sect;&sect; 5101-5109</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. The No-Fault regime aims &quot=
;to
ensure prompt compensation for losses incurred by accident victims without
regard to fault or negligence, to reduce the burden on the courts and to
provide substantial premium savings to New York motorists.&quot; </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:49TT-9NW0-0039-403G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Med. Soc'y of=
 New
York v. Serio</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:49TT-9NW0-0039-403G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 100 N.Y.2d =
854,
860, 800 N.E.2d 728, 768 N.Y.S.2d 423 (2003)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
The No-Fault Act provides compensation for &quot;basic economic loss,&quot;
which covers, as relevant here, &quot;necessary&quot; health expenses up to
$50,000 per person. </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6JXH-MP93-S445-X000-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>N.Y. Ins. Law
&sect; 5102(a)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal1 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
Act's implementing regulations allow covered individuals to assign their
statutory benefits to licensed health care providers in exchange for servic=
es,
and the providers in turn can submit claims directly to the
insurance&nbsp;[**6]&nbsp; companies for medically necessary expenses. </sp=
an><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dadministrative-cod=
es&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5WYW-NFF1-F1WF-M0WW-00009-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>N.Y. Comp. Co=
des
R. &amp; Regs. tit. 11, &sect; 65-3.11(a)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font=
-family:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (&quot;An insurer
shall pay benefits . . . directly to the applicant or . . . upon assignment=
 by
the applicant[,] . . . shall pay benefits directly to providers of health c=
are
services . . . .&quot;). Providers, however, are ineligible to receive reim=
bursement
of No-Fault benefits in a number of circumstances, including if they
&quot;fail[] to meet any applicable New York State or local licensing
requirement . . . or meet any applicable licensing requirement necessary . =
. .
in any other state.&quot; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i> <=
/span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dadministrative-cod=
es&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5WYW-NFM1-JT99-23X4-00009-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect;
65-3.16(a)(12)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'>. For example, a medical services corporation may be
operated only by a licensed professional, such as a physician. <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See, e.g.</i>, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:660H-HWB3-GXF6-82V4-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>N.Y. Bus. Cor=
p.
Law &sect;&sect; 1503(b)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",s=
erif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:660H-J1T3-CGX8-04DW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>1507</span></=
i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:69VM-0HM3-RRV0-D20P-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>1508(a)</span=
></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Providers are also prohibited from paying or receiving kickbacks in exchange
for patient referrals or in connection with the performance of professional
services. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See, e.g.</i>, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6HW8-4MX3-SFMT-F0NX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>N.Y. Educ. Law
&sect; 6530(11)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6HW8-4MX3-SFMT-F0NX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>(18)-(19)</sp=
an></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>; </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dadministrative-cod=
es&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5WYW-NFV1-JC0G-61KY-00009-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>N.Y. Comp. Co=
des
R. &amp; Regs. tit. 8, &sect; 29.1(b)(3)-(4)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal1 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
the event of a dispute regarding an insurer's obligation to pay No-Fault
benefits, the No-Fault Act specifies that &quot;[e]very insurer shall provi=
de a
claimant with the option of submitting any dispute involving the insurer's
