if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>State Farm I<=
/span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:65GY-NT51-JKB3-X3RN-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 2022 U.S. D=
ist.
LEXIS 91241, 2022 WL 1606523, at *20-22</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-f=
amily:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. Defendants
undoubtedly face some hardship as relatively small companies or individual
medical providers. But State Farm raises serious and substantial allegations
that demonstrate actual and imminent irreparable harm absent an injunction,
whereas Defendants' alleged hardships of economic impact can be remedied by
monetary damages should they later prevail. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style=
:normal'>See
</i></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:467J-2RN0-0038-X36R-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Kamerling</sp=
an></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:467J-2RN0-0038-X36R-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 295 F.3d at=
 214</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Accordingly, Defendants' arguments evince plausible disagreement with the
