k'>&nbsp;[*36]&nbsp;
<span style=3D'font-variant:small-caps'>Debra Ann Livingston</span>, <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Chief Judge</i>:</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
this case we consider whether the securities fraud claims of minority
shareholders who&nbsp;[**3]&nbsp; allege that they were fraudulently induce=
d to
tender their shares in a freeze-out merger (the &quot;Freeze-Out Merger&quo=
t;
or &quot;Merger&quot;), thereby forfeiting their appraisal rights, were
properly dismissed.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Shanda
Games Limited (&quot;Shanda&quot;) was a video games business registered in=
 the
Cayman Islands with American Depository Shares (&quot;ADS&quot;) listed on =
the
NASDAQ. Its premier asset was the right to market Mir II, a massively
multiplayer online computer game, in China. By 2013, Shanda had begun
developing a mobile version of Mir II (&quot;MIIM&quot; or &quot;Mir II
Mobile&quot;) to access the expanding mobile game market. Mere months before
MIIM launched, Shanda authorized the Freeze-Out Merger, a conflicted
transaction in which members of the Board of Directors of Shanda (the
&quot;Board&quot;), including the CEO, were part of the group of buyers (the
&quot;Buyer Group&quot;). The Merger occurred three and a half months after=
 the
launch of MIIM.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>As
part of the Merger, Shanda issued two proxy statements (the
&quot;Proxies&quot;). Although the minority shareholders lacked the power to
stop the Merger, they could object to the Merger and exercise their apprais=
al
rights. The shareholders relied on the Proxies to evaluate whether to do so.
The Proxies represented&nbsp;[**4]&nbsp; that the Merger was fair to the
shareholders and came to this conclusion based on a fairness opinion that
relied on projections produced, in part, by Shanda's CEO. But the &nbsp;[*3=
7]&nbsp;
minority shareholders (now former ADS holders) in this putative class action
(&quot;Plaintiffs&quot;) allege that the Freeze-Out Merger was not fair. The
projections significantly underestimated Shanda's financial prospects, and =
an
appraisal suit (the &quot;Appraisal Action&quot;) later determined that the
Freeze-Out Merger price was a mere 55 percent of the fair value of Shanda's
shares.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Plaintiffs
brought this putative securities fraud class action on behalf of themselves=
 and
other similarly situated investors pursuant to </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8S9D-W4W2-8T6X-700R-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect;&sect;
10(b)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-fo=
nt-family:
Times;color:black'>, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8S9D-W4W2-8T6X-7020-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>20A</span></i=
></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
and </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8S9D-W4W2-8T6X-701Y-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>20(a) of the
Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (&quot;Exchange Act&quot;)</span></i></a><s=
pan
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
David Monk was appointed lead plaintiff shortly thereafter. Plaintiffs alle=
ge
that Shanda; its former CEO, Yingfeng Zhang (&quot;Zhang&quot;); former CFO=
 Li
Yao; and five directors: Lijun Lin, Heng Wing Chan, Yong Gui, Shaolin Liang
(&quot;Liang&quot;), and Danian Chen (together with Zhang, the &quot;Indivi=
dual
Defendants&quot;) made material misstatements and failed to disclose materi=
al
information between May 5, 2015 and November 18, 2015 in an effort to conce=
al
that the Freeze-Out Merger price did not reflect the fair value of Shanda's=
&nbsp;[**5]&nbsp;
shares and thereby discourage the exercise of appraisal rights. As a result,
Plaintiffs claim, they suffered financial loss through failure to exercise
their appraisal rights and receive the appraisal value of their shares.</sp=
an></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST128T4G60020000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_II08GTF069SW003RS0V2005NX"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST128T4G60040000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The United States District Court=
 for
the Southern District of New York (Carter, <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:=
normal'>J.</i>)
dismissed the claims against Shanda and the securities claims against the
Individual Defendants for failure to state a claim. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST128T4G60010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:6549-HF11-JG02-S078-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>In re Shanda
Games Ltd. Sec. Litig.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:6549-HF11-JG02-S078-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
