<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>A. Statements Concerning the
Preparation of Projections</span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>1.
Game Revenue Estimates</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Monk
first contends that Shanda's statements that the Projections provided in the
Proxies were based on &quot;projected revenues for each new
game,&quot;&nbsp;[**22]&nbsp; App'x 769, &para; 187; App'x 775, &para; 215,=
 and
that the Projections &quot;were reasonably prepared on bases reflecting the
best available estimates and good faith judgments of the management of the
Company,&quot; App'x 773, &para; 201; App'x 776, &para; 219, were materially
misleading. Monk argues that these statements, taken together, are actionab=
le
because &quot;[a] reasonable investor interpreting these statements would
understand them to mean that the projections reflected game-specific revenue
forecasts based on the best available estimates for the revenue of each
game&quot; and that Shanda did not, in fact, perform a game-specific analys=
is.
Appellant's Br. at 50. We disagree.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc8_1"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST62SF8RX001=
0000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST62SF8RX0030000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Assuming that the statement that=
 the
Projections were &quot;reasonably prepared&quot; based, <i style=3D'mso-bid=
i-font-style:
normal'>inter alia</i>, on &quot;projected revenues for each new game&quot;
reflects an opinion, such a statement is actionable if &quot;the statement
omits information whose omission conveys false facts about the speaker's ba=
sis
for holding that view and makes the opinion statement misleading to a
reasonable investor.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST62N1RRR0050000=
400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:690Y-7JH1-F5DR-23KK-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>New England
Carpenters</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:690Y-7JH1-F5DR-23KK-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 80 F.4th at=
 171</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
But the statement is actionable only if a reasonable investor would believe
that the statement implies those facts. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST62SF8RX0020000400"></a><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-st=
yle:
normal'>Abramson, 965 F.3d at 175</i>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Monk
has not adequately alleged that the opinion statements&nbsp;[**23]&nbsp; on
which he relies would lead a reasonable investor to expect projections base=
d on
&quot;game specific revenue forecasts&quot; as opposed to some other
methodology for projecting revenues for each new game. Indeed, the Complaint
explains that &quot;Shanda's management forecasted the expected revenue of =
each
game slated for release.&quot; App'x 759, &para; 163. But Shanda did so by
categorizing games into three different types and then using that
categorization to predict revenue. Shanda thus calculated each game's
revenue&#8212;such that the statement in the Proxies is literally
correct&#8212;but did so using a methodology that the Complaint alleges was=
 a
&quot;simplistic method of generating projections.&quot; <i style=3D'mso-bi=
di-font-style:
normal'>Id.</i></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
