a &quot;portion&quot; of the financial projections&nbsp;[**31]&nbsp; afford=
ed
to Merrill Lynch and to the Buyer Group. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST82SF8SJ0050000400"></a>Appellee's Br. at 40. Shanda
points to our discussion of the definition of &quot;summarize&quot; in </sp=
an><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST82SF8SJ0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5DHS-P8N1-F04K-J0PF-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>In re Bank of
America Corporation Securities, Derivatives &amp; Employment Retirement Inc=
ome
Securities Act (ERISA) Litigation</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5DHS-P8N1-F04K-J0PF-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 772 F.3d 125
(2d Cir. 2014)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'>. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST82SF8SJ0050000400_2"></a>Bu=
t that
very case defines summary as &quot;constituting or containing a summing up =
of
points: covering main points concisely: summarizing very briefly.&quot; </s=
pan><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST82SF8SJ0040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5DHS-P8N1-F04K-J0PF-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5DHS-P8N1-F04K-J0PF-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> at 133 n.5</=
span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(quoting <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Webster's Third New
International Dictionary Unabridged</i> (2014)). The question is thus not
whether it is misleading to describe the reduction of some amount of
information in a condensed presentation as a summary, but whether it is
misleading to describe the exclusion of one-fifth of the relevant data unde=
rlying
a projection as a summary. As to this latter question, we conclude that it =
is.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Shanda
next argues that it was entitled to &quot;exercise its judgment in deciding
whether the 2020 data was important enough to include.&quot; Appellee's Br.=
 at
41. But the statement is not misleading simply because Shanda excluded a ye=
ar's
worth of relevant data from the Proxies. Shanda <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-s=
tyle:
normal'>could</i> exercise its judgment in deciding what to include in the
Proxies and what information to provide to Merrill Lynch and the Buyer Grou=
p.
Once Shanda had provided information to Merrill Lynch and the Buyer Group,
however, it&nbsp;[**32]&nbsp; could not thereafter mislead investors as to =
what
information had been provided. And this is the crux of the misleading state=
ment
alleged by Monk.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[*48]&nbsp;
<a name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST828T4J60020000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST928T4JC0010000400"></a>Shanda finally argues that t=
he
excluded data was not material. <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc12_0"></a>A
statement is material if there is &quot;'a substantial likelihood that the
disclosure of the omitted fact would have been viewed by the reasonable
investor as having significantly altered the total mix of information made
available.'&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST828T4J60010000400"></a>=
<a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:417N-8MK0-0038-X1BP-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Ganino v.
Citizens Utils. Co.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:417N-8MK0-0038-X1BP-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 228 F.3d 15=
4,
162 (2d Cir. 2000)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (quoting </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST828T4J60030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-FKK0-003B-409H-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Basic Inc. v.
Levinson</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-FKK0-003B-409H-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 485 U.S. 22=
4,
231-32, 108 S. Ct. 978, 99 L. Ed. 2d 194 (1988)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>).
But on a </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6CHH-WBV3-SCV7-1000-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Rule 12(b)(6)=
</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
motion, &quot;a complaint may not properly be dismissed . . . on the ground
that the alleged misstatements or omissions are not material unless they ar=
e so
obviously unimportant to a reasonable investor that reasonable minds could =
not
differ on the question of their importance.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29ST828T4J60050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5254-JR11-652R-01XX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Litwin v.
Blackstone Grp., L.P.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5254-JR11-652R-01XX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 634 F.3d 70=
6,
717 (2d Cir. 2011)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (internal quotation marks and
citation omitted). To be sure, the 2020 data show significantly lower reven=
ue
growth than the 2016 to 2019 data. But there is still revenue growth of 5.4
percent, which Monk alleges constitutes &quot;significant and positive
information about the Company and its value.&quot; App'x 743, &para; 120. T=
his
information may turn out to be immaterial. But reasonable minds could disag=
ree
on this question and that is all that is required at the
