5,
385, 90 S. Ct. 616, 24 L. Ed. 2d 593 (1970)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Such a link is forged when authorization of a proposed merger requires the
affirmative vote of at least some minority shareholders; that is because a
proxy statement provided to minority shareholders may persuade them to prov=
ide
necessary support for merger approval. <u>See id.</u> (ruling that the
causation requirement is satisfied where a majority shareholder owned 54% o=
f a
corporation's shares, but the proposed merger required a two-thirds affirma=
