<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>I
worry that (at least in the freeze-out merger context) minority shareholders
who fail to exercise their&nbsp;[**85]&nbsp; individual right to appraisal
under state law in the first instance will now have a second-chance claim v=
ia a
class action under the federal securities law. Appraisal actions can be
expensive and chancy: the &quot;fair value&quot; could be less than the mer=
ger
price. The majority opinion alters the calculus by recasting individual
appraisal actions as securities fraud claims, hollowing out </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8S9D-W4W2-8T6X-700R-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
