if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>section 10(b)=
</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>'s
reliance requirement. <u>Cf. </u></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6F29STV2SF7PD0010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-5PF0-003B-S1BD-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Marine Bank v.
Weaver</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-5PF0-003B-S1BD-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 455 U.S. 55=
1,
556, 102 S. Ct. 1220, 71 L. Ed. 2d 409 (1982)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(&quot;Congress, in enacting the securities laws, did not intend to provide=
 a
broad federal remedy for all fraud.&quot;). Instead, these allegations at b=
est
would have entitled Monk to an appraisal of the fair value of his shares un=
der
Cayman Islands law, a remedy that he, unlike others similarly situated, did=
 not
