<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
first certified question we are called upon to answer raises a question of
proximate cause, namely, whether the chain of causation linking defendants'
alleged wrongdoing to plaintiffs' alleged injuries is too remote to permit
recovery as a matter of law. We begin by analyzing this subject in the cont=
ext
of plaintiffs' RICO claims.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>I
Proximate Cause as an Element of Standing Under RICO</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4F8XMV10K1MND4PP0000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4F8XMV10K1MND4PS0000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The RICO provision for civil act=
ions
states</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-botto=
m:0in;
margin-left:20.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:15.=
0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4F8XMV10K1MND4PS0000400_2"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4F8XMV10K1MND4PP0000400_2"></a><span style=3D'font-family=
:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Any person injured in his busine=
ss
or property by reason of a violation&nbsp;[**13]&nbsp; of section 1962 of t=
his
chapter may sue therefor in any appropriate United States district court and
shall recover threefold the damages he sustains and the cost of the suit,
including a reasonable attorney's fee.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4F8XMV10K1MND4PS0000400_3"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4F8XMV10K1MND4PP0000400_3"></a><span style=3D'font-family=
:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span><a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc1_4=
"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
1964(c) (1994)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'>. In </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4F8XMV10K1MND4PN0000400=
"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Holmes</span>=
</i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 503 U.S. at=
 268</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
the Supreme Court stated that <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc2_4"></a>a
plaintiff's standing to sue under RICO requires &quot;a showing that the
defendant's violation not only was a 'but for' cause of his injury, but was=
 the
proximate cause as well.&quot; To determine in a given case whether proxima=
te
cause is present, common law principles are applied. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-f=
ont-style:
normal'>See </i></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4F8XMV10K1MND4PR0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>id</span></i>=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>. at 267-68</=
span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(explaining that statutory standing under RICO encompasses common law
