This language tells us that to plead a direct injury is a key element for
establishing proximate causation, independent of and in addition to other
traditional elements of proximate cause. Thus, the other traditional rules
requiring that defendant's acts were a substantial cause of the injury, and
that plaintiff's injury was reasonably foreseeable, are <i style=3D'mso-bid=
i-font-style:
normal'>additional elements</i>, not substitutes &nbsp;[*236]&nbsp; for
alleging (and ultimately, showing) a direct injury.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
