rif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>In considering whether
summary&nbsp;[**17]&nbsp; judgment on the issue is appropriate, we must bea=
r in
mind that the underlying objective facts, which will often be free from
dispute, are merely the starting point for the ultimate determination of ma=
teriality.
<a name=3D"Bookmark_I4FDVMMS0K1MNJ3YT0000400"></a>The determination requires
delicate assessments of the inferences a &quot;reasonable [prospective
purchaser or seller]&quot; would draw from a given set of facts and the
significance of those inferences to him, and these assessments are peculiar=
ly
ones for the trier of fact.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal6 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
