rif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>in any private action arising un=
der
this&nbsp;[**14]&nbsp; chapter in which the plaintiff may recover money dam=
ages
only on proof that the defendant acted with a particular state of mind, the
complaint shall, with respect to each act or omission alleged to violate th=
is
chapter, <u>state with particularity </u>&nbsp;[*307]&nbsp; <u>facts giving
rise to a strong inference that the defendant acted with the required state=
 of
mind</u>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal8 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
