style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>). <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2N1RS50010000400_2"></a>As examples of other possi=
ble
causes, Empire mentioned bootlegging from states with even lower taxes or
retailers responding to changing customers' tastes&nbsp;[**18]&nbsp; by
offering product not subject to Empire's exclusive distributorship. </span>=
<a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2D6NDV0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5T4K-YBH1-F2MB-S4B9-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id</span></i>=
</a><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.</span></i></p>

<p class=3DNormal9 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Here,
by contrast, the loss to AlixPartners and the other large advising firms is
plausibly alleged to flow directly from McKinsey's fraud on the Bankruptcy
&nbsp;[*206]&nbsp; Court. If the thirteen assignments had not been awarded =
to
McKinsey, it is entirely plausible that they would have been awarded to oth=
er
advising firms, and the large advising firms would, following past practice,
have received 75% of these assignments and resulting revenue (and that
AlixPartners would have received a 24% share of these assignments and resul=
ting
revenue). And, of course, none of these prior cases involved allegations of
fraud on a court whose operations we superintend.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal9 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2N1RS50030000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Although we hold that Alix
sufficiently alleges proximate cause with respect to the thirteen bankruptc=
ies,
proximate cause is especially conspicuous in the case of <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2N1RS50020000400"></a><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-st=
yle:
normal'>GenOn</i>. Specifically, Alix plausibly alleges that had McKinsey f=
iled
proper disclosure statements, GenOn would not have hired McKinsey and, even=
 if
it had, the bankruptcy court would not have approved McKinsey's retention.
Moreover, Alix plausibly alleges that had McKinsey been disqualified,
AlixPartners would have been&nbsp;[**19]&nbsp; hired.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal9 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2N1RS50050000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>According to the amended complai=
nt,
McKinsey, prior to and at the time of the filing of the <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2N1RS50040000400"></a><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-st=
yle:
normal'>GenOn</i> bankruptcy, had extensive connections to NRG Energy, GenO=
n's
parent company and a current or former McKinsey client. Prior to its
bankruptcy, GenOn had a multi-million-dollar fraudulent transfer claim agai=
nst
NRG Energy. Had McKinsey made truthful disclosures, Alix alleges, GenOn wou=
ld
not have hired McKinsey RTS to investigate GenOn's fraudulent transfer claim
against NRG Energy, McKinsey's own client. Nor would it have hired McKinsey=
 to
negotiate GenOn's separation from NRG Energy during bankruptcy proceedings.
Alix further alleges that, in addition to failing to disclose its connectio=
n to
NRG Energy, McKinsey also concealed at least 53 other known conflicts and
connections, some of which would have revealed that multiple McKinsey clien=
ts
were GenOn's creditors. Alix further alleges that in order to avoid being
listed as a creditor of the estate, McKinsey received avoidable preference
payments from GenOn and intentionally concealed an interest adverse to the
estate.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal9 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Based
on these alleged facts, it is implausible to conclude that GenOn would have
retained McKinsey with knowledge of these&nbsp;[**20]&nbsp; serious conflic=
ts
of interests. We are even more hard-pressed to conclude that the Bankruptcy
Court, given these facts, could or would have found that McKinsey was
&quot;disinterested&quot; and did not &quot;hold or represent an interest
adverse to the estate.&quot; </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8S8T-0CK2-8T6X-73HH-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>11 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
327(a)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-f=
ont-family:
Times;color:black'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal9 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2HM63Y0020000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>McKinsey contends that the causal
chains in these thirteen bankruptcies are too tenuous to meet the proximate
cause standard because debtors do not have to hire a bankruptcy consultant =
at
all or may hire more than one. In its view, this discretion makes any causal
relationship too speculative. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2HM63Y0040000400"=
></a>We
disagree. <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc8_7"></a>As the Supreme Court has
explained, proximate cause is a &quot;flexible concept&quot; that is
&quot;generally not amenable to bright-line rules.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2HM63Y0010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4SPS-PSH0-TXFX-12X7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Bridge</span>=
</i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4SPS-PSH0-TXFX-12X7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 553 U.S. at
654, 659</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast=
-font-family:
Times;color:black'>. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2HM63Y0040000400_2"></a>Al=
though
the existence of an intervening decision-maker &quot;may in some cases tend=
 to
show that an injury was not sufficiently direct to satisfy [the]
proximate-cause requirement, . . . it is not in and of itself
dispositive.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2HM63Y0030000400"></a=
><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4SPS-PSH0-TXFX-12X7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Bridge</span>=
</i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4SPS-PSH0-TXFX-12X7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 553 U.S. at=
 659</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
On our review of a </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6CHH-WBV3-SCV7-1000-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Rule 12(b)(6)=
</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
dismissal, which requires us to draw all reasonable inferences in Alix's fa=
vor,
we see nothing implausible or speculative about the conclusion that
AlixPartners and the other competitors would have secured additional
engagements absent McKinsey's alleged misconduct.&nbsp;[**21]&nbsp;</span><=
/p>

<p class=3DNormal9 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2N1RS60010000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Although proximate cause is most
clearly alleged with respect to <a name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2HM63Y005000040=
0"></a><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>GenOn</i>, the remaining twelve engage=
ments
also meet the proximate cause requirement. This is because, &nbsp;[*207]&nb=
sp;
as we have noted (<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>see</i> pp. 13-18=
),
Alix plausibly alleges that Alix Partners and the other two firms that comp=
ete
for assignments in large bankruptcies would have been in direct competition=
 for
the other twelve bankruptcies if McKinsey had not submitted allegedly
fraudulent statements to the Bankruptcy Court. Then, plausibly, the firms w=
ould
have received assignments roughly in accordance with their historical market
shares. Moreover, fraud on the Bankruptcy Court committed in the manner all=
eged
by Alix causes direct harm to litigants who are entitled to a level playing
field and calls into play our unique supervisory responsibilities.</span></=
p>

<p class=3DNormal9 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I40FW3M9816000058KM00009"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I40FW3M9DJ3000058KM0000B"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I40FW3M8K6M000058KM00005"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2N1RS60030000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The congruence of these concerns=
 has
not been at play in any of the authorities cited by the parties&#8212;</spa=
n><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2N1RS60020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4SPS-PSH0-TXFX-12X7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Bridge</span>=
</i></a><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, </span></i><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT2N1RS60040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4K41-DS80-004C-200J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Anza</span></=
i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
or </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT28T3WK0010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5T4K-YBH1-F2MB-S4B9-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Empire Mercha=
nts</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&#8212;or,
for that matter, in any other relevant authority. But the fact that this ca=
se
is a &quot;one off&quot; does not reduce our responsibility to superintend =
the
integrity of bankruptcy processes. Of course, proximate cause is merely one
hurdle. McKinsey might well prevail on summary judgment&nbsp;[**22]&nbsp; o=
r at
trial, and to be sure, uncertainties at those stages might exist. But in li=
ght
of our supervisory responsibilities, we remand in order for a more complete
record to be developed: one that will disclose more about who did what, whe=
n,
and with what reasonably likely consequences.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal9 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT28T3WK0040000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>For the guidance of the parties =
on
remand, we note that uncertainty on how to calculate damages should not be
confused with proximate cause because they are distinct concepts. <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See </i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT28T3WK0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4K41-DS80-004C-200J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Anza</span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4K41-DS80-004C-200J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 547 U.S. at=
 466</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(&quot;Proximate cause and certainty of damages, while both related to the
plaintiff's responsibility to prove that the amount of damages he seeks is
fairly attributable to the defendant, are distinct requirements.&quot;)</sp=
an></p>

<p class=3DNormal9 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Alix
alleges that if McKinsey had disclosed what it was required to disclose,
McKinsey would have been disqualified and the thirteen assignments would ha=
ve
been added to the pool available to Alix Partners and McKinsey's other
competitors. McKinsey's three largest competitors would have received 75% of
these assignments (and revenue), just as they historically received 75% of
assignments and revenue.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal9 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Of
course, we cannot tell which particular assignments would have been within
AlixPartners' 24% and therefore cannot determine&nbsp;[**23]&nbsp; exactly =
its
losses. <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc9_7"></a>But certainty as to the am=
ount
of damages is not required at the pleading stage. And whatever uncertainty
exists does not undermine the fact that Alix plausibly alleged that McKinse=
y's
fraud caused Alix some damage.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal9 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT28T3WM0010000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT28T3WM0030000400"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFc=
lscc10_7"></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
law is well-settled that uncertainty as to amount of damages is not a reaso=
n to
deny a plaintiff some recovery. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT28T3WK0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-DH60-003B-755V-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Story Parchme=
nt
Co. v. Paterson Parchment Co.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-DH60-003B-755V-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 282 U.S. 55=
5,
51 S. Ct. 248, 251-52, 75 L. Ed. 544 (1931)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
There the Court said that &quot;[t]he wrongdoer is not entitled to complain
that [damages] cannot be measured with the exactness and precision that wou=
ld
be possible if the case, which he alone is responsible for making, were
otherwise...the risk of the uncertainty should be thrown upon the wrongdoer
instead of upon the injured party.&quot; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'>Id.;
see also </i></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT28T3WM0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-G520-003B-74J4-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Eastman Kodak=
 Co.
of New York v. S. Photo Materials Co.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-G520-003B-74J4-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 273 U.S. 35=
9,
379, 47 S. Ct. 400, 71 L. Ed. 684 (1927)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-=
family:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal9 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT28T3WM0050000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GV2D6NF10020000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Uncertainty as to the amount of
damages can arise in a somewhat analogous context where wrongdoing has inju=
red
one member of a group, but it is not known which one. The Seventh Circuit h=
as
offered the example of several job applicants who were passed over on racial
grounds for one &nbsp;[*208]&nbsp; promotion. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc11_6"></a>&quot;If four people competing for o=
ne
position lost an equal chance to get it, then each should receive 25% of the
benefits available.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GT28T3WM00400004=
00"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4D64-7JB0-0038-X038-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Biondo v. Cit=
y of
Chicago</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4D64-7JB0-0038-X038-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 382 F.3d 68=
0,
688 (7th Cir. 2004)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-styl=
e:
normal'>See </i></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GV2D6NF10010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:52FW-1VM1-F04K-R033-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>BCS Services,
Inc. v. Heartwood 88, LLC</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:52FW-1VM1-F04K-R033-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 637 F.3d 75=
0,
758 (7th Cir. 2011)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal9 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GV2D6NF10040000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GV2HM6450010000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Finally, McKinsey has not
demonstrated that anyone else is &quot;better&nbsp;[**24]&nbsp; situated to
sue&quot; than Alix. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See </i></span=
><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I64KM5GV2D6NF10030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5T4K-YBH1-F2MB-S4B9-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Empire Mercha=
nts</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5T4K-YBH1-F2MB-S4B9-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
