k'>.
Here, Shields does not allege that defendants owned stock, but rather that
defendants made fraudulent statements intending to inflate the stock price =
so
that they &quot;could protect their executive positions and the compensation
and prestige they enjoy thereby.&quot; Following <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-=
style:
normal'>Goldman</i>, we require of Shields more specific factual allegations
before we will infer from defendants' positions as executives that incorrect
predictions were made with fraudulent intent.</span></p>

