:contentItem:3YDK-P8F0-0038-X3H0-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 201 F.3d 94=
, 97
(2d Cir. 2000)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'> (&quot;The nonmoving party must have had the opportunit=
y to
discover information that is essential to [its] opposition to the motion for
summary judgment. Only in the rarest of cases may summary judgment be grant=
ed
against a plaintiff who has not been afforded the opportunity to conduct
discovery.&nbsp;[**29]&nbsp; &quot; (internal quotation marks and citation
