time
of the complaint without any opportunity for discovery. We do not think the
Standing Order can possibly be intended to impose such an obligation.</span=
></p>

<p class=3DNormal11 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4F54HVJ0K1MND1BD0000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The district court might also ha=
ve
understood the entry of judgment as a sanction imposed by reason of the
plaintiff's violation of a court order. We have observed that <a
