k'>.
As the Supreme Court explained in <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>R=
eves</i>:</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal12 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bott=
om:0in;
margin-left:20.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:15.=
0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Once
we understand the word &quot;conduct&quot; to require some degree of direct=
ion
and the word &quot;participate&quot; to require some part in that direction,
the meaning of </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
comes into focus. In order to &quot;participate, directly or indirectly, in=
 the
conduct of such enterprise's affairs,&quot; one must have some part in
directing those affairs. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I75075MNY29000D07DC0002W"></a>=
<a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4F0WVM10K1MND1180000400"></a>Of course, the word
&quot;participate&quot; makes clear that RICO liability is not limited to t=
hose
with primary responsibility for the enterprise's affairs, just as the phrase
&quot;directly or indirectly&quot; makes clear that RICO liability is not l=
imited
to those with a formal position in the enterprise, but some part in directi=
ng
the enterprise's affairs is required. The &quot;operation or management&quo=
t;
test expresses this requirement in a formulation that is easy to apply.</sp=
an></p>

