f;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal14 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4F3M5JX0K1MND1BP0000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Gallina demonstrated his
discretionary authority and direction of the enterprise by recruiting finan=
cing
for the enterprise, obtaining bonds and insurance coverage, issuing false
insurance certificates, concealing Raycon's deceptive payroll practices, and
representing the Rubinos in meetings with Baisch. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4F3M5JX0K1MND1D10000400"></a>Therefore, Baisch has standi=
ng to
bring his RICO claims against Gallina under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
We also note that <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc14_7"></a>the requirement=
s for
RICO's conspiracy charges under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(d=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
are less demanding: A &quot;conspirator must intend to further an endeavor
which, if completed, would satisfy all of the elements of a substantive
criminal offense, but it suffices that he adopt the goal of&nbsp;[*377]&nbs=
p;
furthering or facilitating the criminal endeavor.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4F3M5JX0K1MND1BN0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RHK-1090-004C-300F-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Salinas v.</s=
pan></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RHK-1090-004C-300F-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> </span></i><=
/a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RHK-1090-004C-300F-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RHK-1090-004C-300F-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 522 U.S. 52,
65, 139 L. Ed. 2d 352, 118 S. Ct. 469 (1997)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4F3M5JX0K1MND1D10000400_2"></a>In the civil context, a
plaintiff must allege that the defendant &quot;knew about and agreed to
facilitate the scheme.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4F3M5JX0K1MND1D000=
00400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RHK-1090-004C-300F-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id</span></i>=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RHK-1090-004C-300F-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>. at 66</span=
></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Baisch has presented a genuine question as to Gallina's knowledge of the
racketeering enterprise and his willingness to promote it.
The&nbsp;[**27]&nbsp; defendants have offered no reason why Baisch has not
presented a material question as to McKinnon-Doxsee's liability, considering
that Gallina is a director and vice-president, and that Gallina acted in th=
ose
official capacities in committing these frauds. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal14 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Baisch,
however, has not contested the district court's dismissal of the federal cl=
aims
against Peter Rubino, Jr. on the ground that his debts had been discharged =
by
the bankruptcy court. Thus, we affirm the district court's dismissal of
Baisch's claims against Rubino, Jr. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal14 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><b
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",se=
rif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>III. CONCLUSION</span></b><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal14 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>For
the foregoing reasons, we AFFIRM the dismissal of claims against Rubino, Jr=
.,
and we VACATE the district court's grant of summary judgment for the other
defendants and REMAND for further proceedings consistent with this opinion.=
