<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
this case, we assess ambiguity in the disputed CDS contracts by looking to =
(i)
the terms of the three credit default swaps; (ii) the terms of the
International Swaps and Derivatives Association's (&quot;ISDA&quot; or
&quot;the Association&quot;) &quot;Master Swap Agreement,&quot; on which th=
ose
swaps are predicated, (iii) ISDA's 1999 Credit Derivatives Definitions--whi=
ch
are incorporated into the disputed contracts; and (iv) the background
&quot;customs, practices, [and] usages&quot; of the credit derivatives trad=
e, <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>id.</i> Because customs and usages mat=
ter,
and because documentation promulgated by the ISDA was used by the parties to
this dispute, we briefly review some relevant background. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
term &quot;derivatives&quot; references &quot;a vast array of privately
negotiated over-the counter . . . and exchange traded transactions,&quot;
including interest-rate swaps, currency swaps, commodity price swaps and cr=
edit
derivatives--which include credit default swaps. </span><a style=3D'mso-foo=
tnote-id:
ftn127' href=3D"#_ftn127" name=3D"_ftnref127" title=3D""><sup><span style=
=3D'font-family:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>17</span></sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> A
derivative is a bilateral contract that is typically negotiated by phone and
followed by an exchange of confirmatory faxes that constitute the contract =
but
do not specify such terms as events of default, representations and warrant=
ies,
covenants, liquidated damages, &nbsp;[**12]&nbsp; and choice of law. </span=
><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn128' href=3D"#_ftn128" name=3D"_ftnref128" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>18</span>=
</sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
These (and other) terms are typically found in a &quot;Master Swap
Agreement,&quot; which, prior to standardization efforts that began in the
mid-1980s, &quot;took the form of separate 15-to 25-page&nbsp;[*174]&nbsp;
agreements for each transaction.&quot; </span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:f=
tn129'
href=3D"#_ftn129" name=3D"_ftnref129" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-f=
amily:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>19</span></sup></a></p>

<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Documentation
of derivatives transactions has become streamlined, chiefly through industry
adherence to &quot;Master Agreements&quot; promulgated by the ISDA. In 1999,
Eternity and Morgan entered the ISDA Multicurrency-Cross Border Master
Agreement, which governs, <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>inter ali=
a</i>,
the CDS transactions disputed on appeal. Each disputed CDS also incorporates
the 1999 ISDA Credit Derivatives Definitions, the Association's first attem=
pt
at a comprehensive lexicon governing credit derivatives transactions. </spa=
n><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn130' href=3D"#_ftn130" name=3D"_ftnref130" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>20</span>=
</sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
Last year, due&nbsp;[**13]&nbsp; to the rapid evolution of &quot;ISDA
documentation for credit default swaps,&quot; the Association began market
implementation of the 2003 </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>Credit Derivatives Definitions, </s=
pan><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn131' href=3D"#_ftn131" name=3D"_ftnref131" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>21</span>=
</sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
which evidently constitutes a work in progress. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-s=
tyle:
normal'>See</i> note 28, <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>infra</i>.=
</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
