Morgan would pay Eternity par value for the obligations tendered. </span></=
p>

<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'text-align:justify;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>It
is alleged (and we therefore assume) that Eternity entered the swaps in
reliance on Morgan's representations that it would provide access to a liqu=
id
secondary market that would enable the Fund to divest the contracts prior to
termination. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
