6,
73, 623 N.E.2d 541, 603 N.Y.S.2d 414 (1993)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4F252FJ0K1MND3PM0000400"></a>But misstatements are action=
able
only if the defendant is &quot;under a duty to the plaintiff to exercise
reasonable care in giving the information, and plaintiffs' reliance upon the
information [is] foreseeable.&quot; </span><a
