<p class=3DNormal18 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[**66]&nbsp;
<a name=3D"Bookmark_I05BC9D00YV0000P4G70001B"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4JT82MC0K1MNJ2HC0000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4JT82MC0K1MNJ2HF0000400"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFc=
lscc7_15"></a>In
Connecticut, the elements of res judicata are: (1) identity of the parties =
to
the actions; (2) the same claim, demand, or cause of action at issue; (3) a
final judgment on the merits by a court of competent jurisdiction in the fi=
rst
matter; and (4) the parties had a full opportunity to litigate the matter. =
<i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See </i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4JT82MC0K1MNJ2HB0000400"></a><a
