mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> 50 Conn. App.
680, 719 A.2d 62, 65 (Conn. App. Ct. 1998)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4JT82MC0K1MNJ2HH0000400"></a>Where the elements are met, =
res
judicata raises an &quot;absolute bar to a subsequent action on the same
claim.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4JT82MC0K1MNJ2HD0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RX3-YT60-003D-8190-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Joe's Pizza, =
Inc.
v. Aetna Life and Cas. Co.,</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RX3-YT60-003D-8190-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> 236 Conn. 86=
3,
675 A.2d 441, 448 (Conn. 1996)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Ti=
mes",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. <a
