Practice Book &sect; 17-34</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> that &quot;they intend to chall=
enge
certain material allegations of WWE's counterclaims and to assert various
defenses at the damages hearing.&quot; (Letter from Michael A. Freeman to t=
he
Court 2, Jan. 19, 2006) The provisions of </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6HNX-8X93-S3HF-H161-00009-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 17-34<=
/span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
essentially give the Shenker Defendants an opportunity to re-open the defau=
lt
judgment that was entered against them. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:nor=
mal'>See</i>
</span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4JT82MC0K1MNJ2XJ0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
