name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc12_13"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",=
serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The factors the court should
consider include: (1) the assumption of jurisdiction by either court over a=
ny
res or property; (2) the inconvenience of the federal forum; (3) the
desirability of avoiding piecemeal litigation; (4) the order in which juris=
diction
was obtained by the concurrent forums; (5) whether state or federal law
supplies the rule of decision; and (6) whether the state court proceeding w=
ill
adequately protect the rights of the party seeking to invoke federal
jurisdiction. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See </i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4JT82MC0K1MNJ2Y00000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-54V0-003B-S0RY-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-54V0-003B-S0RY-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> at 19, 23-27=
</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>; <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>see also </i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4JT82MC0K1MNJ2Y20000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4DBK-S9X0-0038-Y2CD-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
