k'>.
The Connecticut court has rendered several judgments in the case and a hear=
ing
on damages is scheduled. </span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn244'
href=3D"#_ftn244" name=3D"_ftnref244" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-f=
amily:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>19</span></sup></a><span style=3D'font-famil=
y:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> &nbsp;[*513]&nbsp=
; In
the federal action, on the other hand, no discovery has occurred and the co=
urt
has not rendered any substantive judgments. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal18 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[**80]&nbsp;
<u>e. Law Which Supplies the Rule of Decision</u></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal18 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4JT82MC0K1MNJ3010000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The next factor involves
consideration of which law governs. This factor weighs heavily against
abstention because federal law supplies the rule of decision on the RICO, R=
PA,
and Sherman Act claims. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See </i></s=
pan><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4JT82MC0K1MNJ3000000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-3WR0-008H-V204-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Johnson,</spa=
n></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-3WR0-008H-V204-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> 964 F.2d at =
122</span></i></a><span
