<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",=
serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>1. UpCodes's statements regarding
integrated amendments</span></i></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGF2SF88H0010000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>ICC alleges that UpCodes's
advertisements and promotional statements imply that UpCodes's website
integrates <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>all</i> amendments adopt=
ed by
a relevant jurisdiction, but their website actually omits numerous amendmen=
ts.
The district court dismissed this claim after determining that ICC did not
adequately plead the falsity of these statements. The court held that &quot=
;[t]he
claim that UpCodes offers integrated amendments is not rendered false by the
fact that 'some but not all' amendments are posted.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGF2N1RDS0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:62CN-FF21-F4NT-X0PT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Int'l Code
Council, Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:62CN-FF21-F4NT-X0PT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 2021 U.S. D=
ist.
LEXIS 66802, 2021 WL 1236106, at *6</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-famil=
y:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. We disagree and
conclude that ICC did adequately allege that these statements were false.</=
span></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Accepting
ICC's allegations of omitted amendments as true, at least one statement is
facially false. UpCodes describes itself as the &quot;only place where <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>all the codes</i> are kept up-to-date =
<i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>with all the amendments&nbsp;[**19]&nb=
sp;
integrated</i> natively into the code.&quot; App'x 34, &para; 51 (emphasis
added). This statement&#8212;with which the district court did not
engage&#8212;unambiguously asserts that UpCodes does integrate <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>all</i> amendments for a given jurisdi=
ction.
Because the complaint plausibly alleges that UpCodes failed to incorporate
amendments made by some jurisdictions, <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:norm=
al'>see</i>
App'x 29-31, &para;&para; 38-43, ICC adequately pled the falsity of this
statement.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGF2SF88H0030000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>We further conclude that the oth=
er
relevant statements are also literally false as pled because they
&quot;necessarily and unambiguously imply a false message.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGF2SF88H0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4PCS-P8M0-TXFX-42DR-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Time Warner</=
span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4PCS-P8M0-TXFX-42DR-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 497 F.3d at=
 148</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Statements such as &quot;UpCodes hosts the adopted codes <i style=3D'mso-bi=
di-font-style:
normal'>as enacted</i> by the state or local jurisdiction&quot; and
&quot;UpCodes has integrated the local &nbsp;[*58]&nbsp; codes in jurisdict=
ion
[sic] like Pennsylvania and New York State,&quot; App'x 36-37, &para; 54
(emphasis added), seem to us to necessarily imply that UpCodes integrates <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>all</i> local amendments made in those
jurisdictions. The district court's interpretation&#8212;that these stateme=
nts
could be understood to promise only that UpCodes integrates <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>some</i> of a jurisdiction's amendment=
s (and
thus offers incomplete local codes)&#8212;is implausible when considered in
context.</span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn255' href=3D"#_ftn255"
name=3D"_ftnref255" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",seri=
f;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>5</span></sup></a><span style=3D'font-family=
:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> For these reasons, we conclude =
that
ICC adequately&nbsp;[**20]&nbsp; pled the falsity of UpCodes's statements
regarding integrated amendments.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",=
serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>2. UpCodes's statements regarding
the exclusivity of its services</span></i></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGF28T4RH0010000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>ICC alleges that UpCodes falsely
stated that it is the &quot;sole&quot; provider of codes with integrated
amendments when ICC also offered some of the same materials. In its pre-mot=
ion
letter, UpCodes argued that its &quot;representation [was] actually qualifi=
ed,&quot;
because &quot;ICC's own screenshot shows that UpCodes claims to be the only
source of integrated codes <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>only</i>=
 for
'jurisdictions [that] do not provide integrated code books.'&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGF2D6N720050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:62CN-FF21-F4NT-X0PT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Int'l Code
Council, Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:62CN-FF21-F4NT-X0PT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 2021 U.S. D=
ist.
LEXIS 66802, 2021 WL 1236106, at *8</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-famil=
y:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (emphasis added)
(quoting App'x 41, &para; 63). UpCodes urged the court to dismiss ICC's cla=
im
&quot;[b]ecause ICC d[id] not allege that the statement <i style=3D'mso-bid=
i-font-style:
normal'>as qualified</i> is false.&quot; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'>Id.</i>
(emphasis added). The district court concluded that ICC had
&quot;conceded&quot; the point &quot;[b]ecause [ICC did] not respond to this
argument&quot; in its pre-motion letter, even though ICC's letter was limit=
ed
to three pages and the court did not give ICC notice that its pre-motion le=
tter
might be converted to its response to a motion to dismiss that had not yet =
been
filed. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Given
the opportunity on appeal, ICC now responds. We conclude that it adequately
pled the falsity of UpCodes's&nbsp;[**21]&nbsp; statements regarding the
exclusivity of its services. The district court relied on only one of the
challenged statements, which appeared to be qualified, but it did not addre=
ss
other statements in which UpCodes did not limit its claims to jurisdictions
that do not otherwise provide integrated code books. For example, the compl=
aint
challenged the following statement by UpCodes on its webpage for New York
state: &quot;States and cities enact critical amendments to the base codes.=
 New
York State has made amendment [sic] to the codes. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font=
-style:
normal'>UpCodes provides the only source to view these amendments integrated
into the model codes</i>.&quot; App'x 42, &para; 64 (emphasis added). This
statement unambiguously asserts that UpCodes is the only entity that provid=
es
integrated amendments for the state of New York. ICC pled that it also prov=
ides
Custom Codes, including &quot;New York building codes showing integrated
amendments made by New York.&quot; App'x 41, &para; 64.</span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn256' href=3D"#_ftn256" name=3D"_ftnref256" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>6</span><=
/sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> We
conclude that ICC has adequately &nbsp;[*59]&nbsp; pled that UpCodes's
statements necessarily imply the false message that ICC does not offer
integrated amendments.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",=
serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>3. UpCodes's statements regarding
accuracy and its guarantees that users will completely understand relevant =
code</span></i></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[**22]&nbsp;The
district court determined that ICC sufficiently alleged the falsity of
UpCodes's statements that its codes were accurate and up-to-date and that it
provides a complete understanding of relevant material, but the court
nevertheless concluded that those statements were non-actionable puffery. We
address the accuracy statements and completeness statements separately. Fir=
st,
we agree with the district court that ICC alleged the falsity of UpCodes's
accuracy claims, but we disagree that we can, at least at this stage of the
proceedings, conclude that they are puffery. Second, the district court
correctly determined that UpCodes's statements regarding completeness are
non-actionable puffery, but as explained in section B.3.b. below, we disagr=
ee
with the district court's reasons for reaching that conclusion.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>a. <b
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Claims of accuracy</b></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>ICC
adequately alleges that UpCodes made false statements about the accuracy and
comprehensiveness of its products. These statements include claims such as
&quot;[a]lways up to date&quot; and &quot;never work from outdated code,&qu=
ot;
and implications that the website contained &quot;all [relevant] code.&quot;
App'x 33-34, &para; 50; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>id.</i> at =
35,
&para; 52. In another statement made on Twitter, UpCodes&nbsp;[**23]&nbsp;
doubled down: &quot;ICC says 'UpCodes cannot guarantee that it has the <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>most accurate</i>, <i style=3D'mso-bid=
i-font-style:
normal'>up-to-date</i> information on its website'. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGF28T4RH0030000400"></a>How does that make any sense=
? We
are only [sic] place where <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>all the =
codes
are kept up-to-date</i> with all the amendments integrated natively into the
code.&quot; App'x 34, &para; 51 (emphasis added). We need not decide whether
these statements are rendered false by minor, superficial errors; by averri=
ng
that its codes are completely up-to-date and comprehensive, at the very lea=
st,
UpCodes &quot;necessarily impl[ies] [the] false message&quot; that its
materials are not missing entire sections of code or erroneously publishing
material that it had not been enacted as law. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGF28T4RH0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4PCS-P8M0-TXFX-42DR-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Time Warner</=
span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4PCS-P8M0-TXFX-42DR-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 497 F.3d at=
 158</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Therefore&#8212;accepting the truth of ICC's plausible allegations of UpCod=
es's
errors&#8212;ICC has properly pled that UpCodes's statements regarding accu=
racy
are false.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGF28T4RH0050000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>We disagree with the district co=
urt
that, at this early stage, these accuracy-related statements can be deemed
puffery, which would render them non-actionable under the </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:61XJ-43W3-GXJ9-33DV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Lanham Act</s=
pan></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See </i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGF28T4RH0040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-9PW0-001T-D0TG-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Lipton v. Nat=
ure
Co.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-9PW0-001T-D0TG-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 71 F.3d 464,
474 (2d Cir. 1995)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. Determining whether each of th=
em
is puffery requires a factual inquiry into how users interpreted UpCodes's
claims, and we therefore conclude that the district court erred in dismissi=
ng
this&nbsp;[**24]&nbsp; portion of ICC's false advertising claim.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGF2SF88R0020000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGF2HM5WF0010000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGG28T4RS0020000400"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFc=
lscc7_16"></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>We
have recognized two forms of puffery: The first encompasses &quot;[s]ubject=
ive
