en
false&#8212;then courts treat them as non-actionable puffery as a matter of
law. A plaintiff cannot state a false advertising claim based on such a
statement because, by&nbsp;[**25]&nbsp; definition, it cannot be proven fal=
se. <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See </i></span><a
