<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGM2HM5XD0040000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc10_16"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",=
serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>As we have noted, a statement is
nonactionable puffery if it makes &quot;[s]ubjective claims about products,
which cannot be proven either true or false.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGM2HM5XD0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4PCS-P8M0-TXFX-42DR-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Time Warner</=
span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4PCS-P8M0-TXFX-42DR-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 497 F.3d at=
 159</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(quoting </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGM2HM5XD0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-9PW0-001T-D0TG-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Lipton</span>=
</i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-9PW0-001T-D0TG-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 71 F.3d at =
474</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>).
Whether users could glean a &quot;complete understanding of relevant
material&quot; from UpCodes's website is immeasurable and subjective. App'x
34-35, &para; 52. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGM2D6N8B0030000400"></a>That is=
, even
if UpCodes provided entirely accurate materials, whether any individual cou=
ld
&quot;[u]nderstand all code relevant to [her] project&quot; depends on the
cognitive abilities of the user and the nature of the project. App'x 35, &p=
ara;
52. These statements, which are &quot;expressed in broad, vague, and
commendatory language,&quot; should be &quot;understood as an expression of=
 the
seller's&nbsp;[**33]&nbsp; opinion only.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGM2D6N8B0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4PCS-P8M0-TXFX-42DR-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Time Warner</=
span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4PCS-P8M0-TXFX-42DR-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 497 F.3d at=
 159</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(quoting <a name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGM2D6N8B0040000400"></a><i style=3D'mso-=
bidi-font-style:
normal'>Pennzoil Co., 987 F.2d at 945</i>). False advertising claims
challenging this type of puffery are appropriately resolved at the pleadings
stage. We therefore affirm the dismissal of ICC's claims challenging this
limited set of statements.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>C. <u>Materiality</u></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
district court did not address whether UpCodes's allegedly false statements
were material. Now that the issue has been fully briefed by the parties on
appeal, we conclude that ICC adequately alleges materiality.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGM2D6N8C0020000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGM2D6N8C0040000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc11_15"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",=
serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>In addition to pleading falsity,=
 ICC
must also plausibly allege &quot;that the false or misleading representation
involved an inherent or material quality of the product.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGM2D6N8C0010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5JSS-8501-F04K-J00R-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Apotex Inc.</=
span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5JSS-8501-F04K-J00R-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 823 F.3d at=
 63</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(internal quotation marks omitted). <a name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGN2HM5XM00100=
00400"></a>In
other words, the allegedly false statement must be &quot;likely to influence
purchasing decisions.&quot; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i>
(quoting </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGM2D6N8C0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RV0-0VD0-00B1-D4D2-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Nat'l Basketb=
all
Ass'n v. Motorola, Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RV0-0VD0-00B1-D4D2-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 105 F.3d 84=
1,
855 (2d Cir. 1997)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>). We &nbsp;[*64]&nbsp; have
declared that plaintiffs &quot;should be given the opportunity to develop t=
heir
evidence&quot; to demonstrate materiality. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGN2HM5XM0010000400_2"></a><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-=
style:
normal'>See </i></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I662SCGM2D6N8C0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-0G10-001B-K1KW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Nat'l Ass'n of
Pharm. Mfrs., Inc. v. Ayerst Lab'ys</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-0G10-001B-K1KW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 850 F.2d 90=
4,
917 (2d Cir. 1988)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. And we have explained that the
question of &quot;whether or not [consumers] construed&quot; a statement as
material generally &quot;cannot be determined on consideration of a motion =
to
dismiss.&quot; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i> </span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn260' href=3D"#_ftn260" name=3D"_ftnref260" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>10</span>=
</sup></a></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>ICC's
allegations that UpCodes's false statements were &quot;likely to influence
purchasing&nbsp;[**34]&nbsp; decisions&quot; are plausible, App'x 44, &para;
75, particularly because nearly all the challenged statements either assure=
 the
accuracy of complex legal codes, promote a central feature of UpCodes's
business (i.e., the integration of local amendments), or imply that ICC off=
ers
inferior services. Therefore, we conclude that ICC pled sufficient facts to
demonstrate materiality for the purpose of surviving a motion to dismiss.</=
span></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>CONCLUSION</span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Although
we decide that the district court erred by <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:=
normal'>sua
sponte</i> and without notice construing the parties' pre-motion letters as
briefing on a motion to dismiss and granting that motion, in light of the
unusual circumstances of this appeal, we are able to reach the merits of the
motion to dismiss based on the appellate briefing. We conclude that the
district court erred by granting the defendants' motion to dismiss in its
entirety: ICC adequately pled falsity as to all of the challenged statements
except those suggesting that users will obtain a &quot;full&quot; or
&quot;complete understanding&quot; of relevant code from UpCodes's website.=
 The
statements claiming completeness are nonactionable puffery and therefore we
affirm the dismissal of ICC's claims to the extent they are
premised&nbsp;[**35]&nbsp; on them. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I662J8F62HM5XF00100=
00400"></a>ICC's
complaint sufficiently alleges, for the purpose of surviving a motion to
dismiss, that the remaining challenged statements are material.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal19 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>We
have considered the defendants' remaining arguments on appeal and conclude =
that
they are without merit. For the reasons explained above, we AFFIRM IN PART =
and
REVERSE IN PART the district court's decision and order and REMAND for furt=
her
proceedings consistent with this opinion.</span></p>

