<p class=3DNormal21 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[****29]&nbsp;
On the contrary, these statements are in full accord with the proposition
&nbsp;[***260]&nbsp; that <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc8_17"></a>RICO is
equally applicable to a criminal enterprise that has no legitimate dimensio=
n or
has yet to acquire one.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Accep=
ting
that the primary purpose of RICO is to cope with the infiltration of legiti=
mate
businesses, applying the statute in accordance with its terms, so as to rea=
ch
criminal enterprises, would seek to deal with the problem at its very
source.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Supporters of the bill
recognized that organized crime uses its primary sources of revenue and pow=
er
-- illegal gambling, loan sharking and illicit drug distribution -- as a
springboard into the sphere of legitimate enterprise.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Hearings on S. 30, <i style=3D'mso=
-bidi-font-style:
normal'>supra</i>, at 1-2.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The
Senate Report stated:</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal21 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&quot;What
is needed here, the committee believes, are new approaches that will deal n=
ot
only with individuals, but also with the economic base through which those
individuals &nbsp;[*592]&nbsp; constitute such a serious threat to the econ=
omic
well-being of the Nation.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>In =
short,
an attack must be made on <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>their sou=
rce of
economic power itself</i>, and the attack must take place on all available
fronts.&quot; S. Rep. No. 91-617, p. 79 (1969) (emphasis supplied). </span>=
</p>

<p class=3DNormal21 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4R64HVD0K1MNJ0330000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4R64HVD0K1MNJ0350000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4R64HVD0K1MNJ03N0000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>&nbsp;[****30]&nbsp; Senator Byrd
explained in debate on the floor, that &quot;loan sharking paves the way for
organized criminals to gain access to and eventually take over the control =
of
thousands of legitimate businesses.&quot; 116 Cong. Rec. 606 (1970).<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Senator Hruska declared that &quot=
;the
combination of criminal and civil penalties in this title offers an
extraordinary potential for striking a mortal blow against the property
interests of organized crime.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4R64HVD0K1MNJ0320000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-HMF0-003B-S491-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id</span></i>=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-HMF0-003B-S491-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>., at 602</sp=
an></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. </span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn275' href=3D"#_ftn275" name=3D"_ftnref275" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>14</span>=
</sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
Undoubtedly, the infiltration &nbsp;[*593]&nbsp; of legitimate businesses w=
as
of great concern, but the means provided to prevent that infiltration plain=
ly
included striking at the source of the problem.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>As Representative Poff, a manager =
of the
bill in the House, stated: &quot;[Title] IX . . . will deal not only with
individuals, but also with the economic base through which those individuals
constitute such a serious threat to the economic well-being of the Nation.<=
span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>In short, an attack must be made on
their source of economic power itself . . . .&quot; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-fo=
nt-style:
normal'>Id</i>., at 35193.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal21 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[****31]&nbsp;
&nbsp;[**2534]&nbsp;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN1_3"></a>[1C]As a measure to deal with the
&nbsp;[***261]&nbsp; infiltration of legitimate businesses by organized cri=
me,
RICO was both preventive and remedial. Respondent's view would ignore the
preventive function of the statute.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>If Congress had intended the more circumscribed approach espoused by=
 the
Court of Appeals, there would have been some positive sign that the law was=
 not
to reach organized criminal activities that give rise to the concerns about
infiltration. The language of the statute, however -- the most reliable
evidence of its intent -- reveals that Congress opted for a far broader
definition of the word &quot;enterprise,&quot; and we are unconvinced by
anything in the legislative history that this definition should be given le=
ss
than its full effect.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal21 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
