at
section simply qualifies SIPC as a proper party in interest in any &quot;ma=
tter
arising in a liquidation proceeding&quot; as to which it &quot;shall be dee=
med
to have intervened,&quot; and gives SIPC no independent right to sue Holmes=
 for
money damages. Pp. 275-276.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal24 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
