ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
sum, subrogation to the rights of the manipulation conspiracy's secondary
victims does, and should, run afoul of proximate-causation standards, and S=
IPC
must wait on the outcome of the trustees' suit. If they&nbsp;[****34]&nbsp;
recover from Holmes, SIPC may share according to the priority SIPA gives its
claim. See </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8S9D-W4W2-8T6X-703J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>15 U. S.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>C. &sect; 78fff-2(c)</span></i></a=
><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
