Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>&nbsp;[*282]&nbsp; Which violati=
ons
of the federal securities laws, if any, constitute a &quot;fraud in the sal=
e of
securities&quot; within the meaning of </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1961(1=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> is
a question that has generated much ink and little agreement among courts </=
span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn316' href=3D"#_ftn316" name=3D"_ftnref316" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>3</span><=
/sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[****48]&nbsp;
or commentators, </span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn317' href=3D"#_ftn31=
7"
name=3D"_ftnref317" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",seri=
f;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>4</span></sup></a><span style=3D'font-family=
:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> and one &nbsp;[*283]&nbsp; whic=
h we
need not definitively resolve here. The statute unmistakably requires that
there be fraud, sufficiently willful to constitute a criminal violation, and
that there be a sale of securities. At the same time, however, I am persuad=
ed
that Congress' use of the word &quot;sale&quot; in defining the predicate
offense does not <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>necessarily</i> di=
ctate
that a RICO plaintiff have been a party to an executed sale.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal24 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[****49]&nbsp;
</span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Section 1961(=
1)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>'s
list of racketeering offenses provides the RICO predicates for both criminal
prosecutions and civil actions. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I4FFVT6Y0K1MNJ0FN000040=
0"></a>Obviously
there is no requirement that the Government be party to a sale before it can
&nbsp;[***554]&nbsp; bring a RICO prosecution predicated on &quot;fraud in =
the
sale of securities.&quot; Accordingly, any argument that the offense itself
embodies a standing requirement must apply only to private actions. That
distinction is not tenable, however. By including a private
&nbsp;[**1326]&nbsp; right of action in RICO, Congress intended to bring
&quot;the pressure of 'private attorneys general' on a serious national pro=
blem
for which public prosecutorial resources [were] deemed inadequate.&quot; </=
span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FFVT6Y0K1MNJ0FM0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-H530-003B-44MW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Agency Holding
Corp.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-H530-003B-44MW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-H530-003B-44MW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Malley-Duff &=
amp;
Associates, Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-H530-003B-44MW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 483 U.S. 14=
3,
151, 97 L. Ed. 2d 121, 107 S. Ct. 2759 (1987)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Although not everyone can qualify as an appropriate &quot;private attorney
general,&quot; the prerequisites to the role are articulated, not in the
definition of the predicate act, but in the civil action provisions of </sp=
an><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1964(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> --
a plaintiff must allege &quot;injury in his business or property by reason
of&quot; a RICO violation.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal24 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FFVT6Y0K1MNJ0FR0000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FFVT6Y0K1MNJ0FT0000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Construing RICO's reference to
&quot;fraud in the sale&nbsp;[****50]&nbsp; of securities&quot; to limit
standing to purchasers and sellers would be &nbsp;[*284]&nbsp; in tension w=
ith
our reasoning in <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Blue Chip Stamps</=
i>. In
that case, the Court admitted that it was not &quot;able to divine from the
language of &sect; 10(b) the express 'intent of Congress' as to the contour=
s of
a private cause of action under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dadministrative-cod=
es&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:603K-8JY1-DYB7-W40R-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Rule 10b-5</s=
pan></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.&quot;
</span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4FFVT6Y0K1MNJ0FP0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-BRX0-003B-S28N-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>421 U.S. at 7=
37</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
The purchaser/seller standing limitation in </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dadministrative-cod=
es&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:603K-8JY1-DYB7-W40R-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Rule 10b-5</s=
pan></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
damages actions thus does not stem from a construction of the phrase &quot;=
in
connection with the purchase or sale of any security.&quot; Rather, it rest=
s on
the relationship between &sect; 10(b) and other provisions of the securities
laws, </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4FFVT6Y0K1MNJ0FS0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-BRX0-003B-S28N-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-BRX0-003B-S28N-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 733-736<=
/span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
and the practical difficulties in granting standing in the absence of an
