<p class=3DNormal25 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_10_1"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>A provision of the Racketeer
Influenced and Corrupt Organizations Act (RICO), </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U. S. C.
&sect; 1962(c)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'>, makes it unlawful &quot;for any person employed by or
associated with [an interstate] enterprise . . . to conduct or participate,
directly or indirectly, in the conduct of such enterprise's affairs through=
 a
pattern of racketeering activity . . . .&quot; After respondent's predecess=
or,
the accounting firm of Arthur Young and Company, engaged in certain activit=
ies
relating to valuation of a gasohol plant on the yearly audits and financial
statements of a farming cooperative, the cooperative filed for bankruptcy, =
and
the bankruptcy trustee brought suit, alleging, <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-st=
yle:
normal'>inter alia</i>, that the activities in question rendered
&nbsp;[****2]&nbsp; Arthur Young civilly liable under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> to
petitioner holders of certain of the cooperative's notes. Among other thing=
s,
the District Court applied Circuit precedent requiring, in order for such
liability to attach, &quot;some participation in the operation or managemen=
t of
the enterprise itself&quot;; ruled that Arthur Young's activities failed to
satisfy this test; and granted summary judgment in its favor on the RICO cl=
aim.
Agreeing with the lower court's analysis, the Court of Appeals affirmed in =
this
regard.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal25 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_11_2"></a><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>=
<span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Held:</span></i><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
One must participate in the operation or management of the enterprise itsel=
f in
order to be subject to </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
liability. Pp. 177-186.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal25 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_12_2"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>(a) Examination of the statutory
language in the light of pertinent dictionary definitions and the context o=
f </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
brings the section's meaning unambiguously into focus. Once it is understood
that the word &quot;conduct&quot; requires some degree of direction, and th=
at
the word &quot;participate&quot; requires some part in that direction, it is
clear that one must have <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>some</i> p=
art in
directing an enterprise's affairs in order to &quot;participate, directly or
indirectly, in the conduct of such . . . affairs.&quot; The &quot;operation=
 or
management&quot; test expresses &nbsp;[****3]&nbsp; this requirement in a
formulation that is easy to apply. Pp. 177-179.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal25 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_13_2"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>(b) The &quot;operation or
management&quot; test finds further support in </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962</=
span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>'s
legislative history. Pp. 179-183.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal25 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_14_2"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>(c) RICO's &quot;liberal
construction&quot; clause -- which specifies that the &quot;provisions of t=
his
title shall be liberally construed to effectuate its remedial purposes&quot=
; --
does not require rejection of the &quot;operation or management&quot; test.=
 The
clause obviously seeks to ensure that Congress' intent is not frustrated by=
 an
overly narrow reading of the statute, but it is not an invitation to apply =
RICO
to new purposes that Congress never intended. It is clear from the statute's
language and legislative history that Congress did not intend to extend </s=
pan><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
liability beyond those who participate in the operation or management of an
enterprise through a pattern of racketeering activity. Pp. 183-184.</span><=
/p>

<p class=3DNormal25 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_15_2"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>(d) The &quot;operation or
management&quot; test is consistent with the proposition that liability und=
er </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> is
not limited to upper management. &quot;Outsiders&quot; having no official
position with the enterprise may be liable under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> if
they are &quot;associated with&quot; the enterprise and participate in the
operation or management of the &nbsp;[****4]&nbsp; enterprise. Pp. 184-185.=
</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal25 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_16_1"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>(e) This Court will not overturn=
 the
lower courts' findings that respondent was entitled to summary judgment upon
application of the &quot;operation or management&quot; test to the facts of
this case. The failure to tell the cooperative's board that the gasohol pla=
nt
should have been valued in a particular way is an insufficient basis for
concluding that Arthur Young participated in the operation or management of=
 the
cooperative itself. Pp. 185-186.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </s=
pan></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal25 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><a
