since commission of a crime listed under title IX provides only one element=
 of
title IX's prohibitions. Unless an individual not only commits such a crime=
 but
engages in a pattern of such violations, and uses that pattern to obtain or
operate an interest in an interstate business, he is not made subject to
proceedings under title IX.&quot; 116 Cong. Rec., at 18940.</span></p>

