k'>&nbsp;[****27]&nbsp;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN1_9"></a>=
[1I] <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN9_1_2"></a>[9]The United States also argues that the
&quot;operation or management&quot; test is not consistent with </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
because it limits &nbsp;[*185]&nbsp; the liability of &quot;outsiders&quot;=
 who
have no official position within the enterprise. Brief for United States as=
 <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Amicus Curiae</i> 12 and 15. The United
States correctly points out that RICO's major purpose was to attack the
&quot;infiltration of organized crime and racketeering into legitimate
organizations,&quot; S. Rep. No. 91-617, at 76, but its argument fails on
several counts. First, it ignores the fact that </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962</=
span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc8_18"></a>has four subsections. Infiltration of
legitimate organizations by &quot;outsiders&quot; is clearly addressed in
subsections (a) and (b), and the &quot;operation or management&quot; test t=
hat
applies under subsection (c) in no way limits the application of subsections
(a) and (b) to &quot;outsiders.&quot; </span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ft=
n329'
href=3D"#_ftn329" name=3D"_ftnref329" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-f=
amily:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>10</span></sup></a><span style=3D'font-famil=
y:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> Second, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> is
limited to persons &quot;employed by or associated with&quot; an enterprise,
suggesting a more limited reach than subsections (a) and (b), which do not
contain such a restriction. Third, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc9_17"></a>cannot be interpreted to reach compl=
ete
&quot;outsiders&quot; because liability depends on showing that the defenda=
nts
conducted or participated in the conduct of the &quot;<i style=3D'mso-bidi-=
font-style:
normal'>enterprise's</i> affairs, &nbsp;[****28]&nbsp; &quot; not just thei=
r <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>own</i> affairs. Of course,
&quot;outsiders&quot; may be liable under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> if
they are &quot;associated with&quot; an enterprise and participate in the
conduct of <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>its</i> affairs -- that =
is,
participate in the operation or management of the enterprise itself -- but =
it
would be consistent with neither the language nor the legislative history o=
f </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> to
interpret it as broadly as petitioners and the United States urge.</span></=
p>

<p class=3DNormal25 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
