<p class=3DNormal25 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN10_1"></a>=
[10]Both
the District Court and the Court of Appeals applied the standard we adopt t=
oday
to the facts of this case, and both found that &nbsp;[***541]&nbsp; respond=
ent
was entitled to summary judgment. &nbsp;[*186]&nbsp; Neither petitioners nor
the United States have argued that these courts misapplied the &quot;operat=
ion
or management&quot; test. The &nbsp;[****29]&nbsp; dissent argues that by
creating the Co-Op's financial statements Arthur Young participated in the
management of the Co-Op because &quot;'financial statements are management's
responsibility.'&quot; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Post</i>, at=
 190,
quoting 1 CCH AICPA Professional &nbsp;[**1174]&nbsp; Standards, SAS No. 1,
&sect; 110.02 (1982). Although the professional standards adopted by the
accounting profession may be relevant, they do not define what constitutes
management of an enterprise for the purposes of </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal25 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN2_2_1"></a=
>[2B]In
this case, it is undisputed that Arthur Young relied upon existing Co-Op
records in preparing the 1981 and 1982 audit reports. The AICPA's professio=
nal
standards state that an auditor may draft financial statements in whole or =
in
part based on information from management's accounting system. See <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>ibid</i>. It is also undisputed that A=
rthur
Young's audit reports revealed to the Co-Op's board that the value of the
gasohol plant had been calculated based on the Co-Op's investment in the pl=
ant.
See App. in No. 87-1726 (CA8), pp. 250-251, 272-273. Thus, we only could
conclude that Arthur Young participated in the operation or management of t=
he
Co-Op itself if Arthur Young's failure &nbsp;[****30]&nbsp; to tell the Co-=
Op's
board that the plant should have been given its fair market value constitut=
ed
such participation. We think that Arthur Young's failure in this respect is=
 not
sufficient to give rise to liability under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal25 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
judgment of the Court of Appeals is affirmed.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal25 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>It is so ordered</span></i><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span></p>

