not regulated by State Law,&quot; </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8S9D-W4W2-8T6X-714X-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1012(b=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
and &sect; 3(b) provides that nothing in the McCarran-Ferguson Act &quot;sh=
all
render the . . . Sherman Act inapplicable to any agreement to boycott, coer=
ce,
or intimidate, or act of boycott, coercion, or intimidation,&quot; </span><a
