jurisdiction over foreign conduct (or, as JUSTICE SCALIA would put it, may
conclude by the employment of comity analysis in the first instance that th=
ere
is no jurisdiction), international comity would not counsel against exercis=
ing
jurisdiction in the circumstances alleged here. </span></p>

