mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>e</span></i><=
/a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. </span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn356' href=3D"#_ftn356" name=3D"_ftnref356" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>25</span>=
</sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
Since the London reinsurers &nbsp;[**2911]&nbsp; do not argue that British =
law
requires them to act in some fashion prohibited by the law of the United
States, see Reply Brief for Petitioners Merrett Underwriting Agency Managem=
ent
Ltd. et al. in No. 91-1128, pp. 7-8, or claim that their compliance with the
laws of both countries is otherwise impossible, &nbsp;[***641]&nbsp; we see=
 no
conflict with British law. See </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Danalytical-materia=
ls&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:42GD-0NW0-00YF-J022-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Restatement
(Third) Foreign Relations Law &sect; 403, Comment </span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Danalytical-materia=
ls&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:42GD-0NW0-00YF-J022-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>e</span></i><=
/a><span
