insurers to &quot;prompt&quot; reinsurers not to deal with the insurers'
competitors -- <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>whether or not</i> t=
hat
refusal to deal is a boycott. That feeling is certainly understandable, sin=
ce
under the normal application of the Sherman Act the reinsurers' concerted
refusal to deal would be an unlawful conspiracy, and the insurers'
&quot;prompting&quot; could make them part of that conspiracy. The
McCarran-Ferguson &nbsp;[*810]&nbsp; Act, however, makes that conspiracy la=
wful
(assuming reinsurance is state regulated), unless the refusal to deal is a
&quot;boycott.&quot; </span></p>

