Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Application of common-law princi=
ples
of proximate causation beyond the directness requirement likewise supports a
finding that causation was sufficiently pleaded in this case.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Though the <i style=3D'mso-bidi-fo=
nt-style:
normal'>Holmes</i> Court noted that directness was &quot;one of [the] centr=
al
elements&quot; it had considered in evaluating causation, it recognized that
proximate causation took &quot;many shapes&quot; at common law. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4K76R6C0K1MNJ1DG0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
