style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>intended</i> consequences of the defen=
dant's
unlawful behavior.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>A defendan=
t may
do so simply by concocting a scheme under which a further, lawful and
&nbsp;[*471]&nbsp; intentional step <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'=
>by
the defendant</i> is required to inflict the injury.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Such a rule precludes recovery for
injuries for which the defendant is plainly morally responsible and which a=
re
suffered by easily identifiable plaintiffs.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>There is no basis in the RICO stat=
ute,
in common-law tort, or in <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Holmes</i=
> for
