if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3WNV-2M50-004C-2006-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3WNV-2M50-004C-2006-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 527 U.S. 1,
24-25, 119 S. Ct. 1827, 144 L. Ed. 2d 35 (1999)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>;
Prosser &amp; Keeton &sect; 105, at 728.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&n=
bsp;
</span>But RICO does not confer on private plaintiffs a right to sue defend=
ants
who engage in any act of common-law fraud; instead, racketeering activity
