<p class=3DNormal31 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_10_3"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>&nbsp;[1353]&nbsp;&nbsp;[*635]&n=
bsp;&nbsp;[**1863]&nbsp;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Respondents filed a state-court su=
it
alleging that petitioner had violated state and federal law in connection w=
ith
a patent dispute.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>After remov=
ing
the case to Federal District Court under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5HW2-D6RV-H0JF-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>28 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
1441(c)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>, which allows removal if the case includes at least one
claim over which the federal court has original jurisdiction, petitioner mo=
ved
to dismiss the suit's only&nbsp;[**1864]&nbsp; federal claim, which arose u=
nder
the Racketeer Influenced and Corrupt Organizations Act (RICO).<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Agreeing that respondents had fail=
ed to
state a RICO claim upon which relief could be granted, the District Court
dismissed the claim; declined to exercise supplemental jurisdiction over the
remaining state-law claims under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5HW2-D6RV-H0HC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1367(c=
)(3)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
which allows such a course if the court &quot;has dismissed all claims over
which it has original jurisdiction&quot;; and remanded the case to state
court.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The Federal Circuit
dismissed petitioner's appeal, &nbsp;[1354]&nbsp; finding that the remand o=
rder
could be colorably characterized as based on a &quot;lack of subject matter
jurisdiction&quot; over the state-law claims, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5HW2-D6RV-H0JP-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1447(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
and was therefore &quot;not reviewable &nbsp;[****2]&nbsp;on appeal,&quot; =
</span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5HW2-D6RV-H0JP-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1447(d=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal31 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_11_5"></a><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>=
<span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Held:</span></i><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> A
district court's order remanding a case to state court after declining to
exercise supplemental jurisdiction over state-law claims is not a remand for
lack of subject-matter jurisdiction for which appellate review is barred by=
 </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5HW2-D6RV-H0JP-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect;&sect;
1447(c)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'> and </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5HW2-D6RV-H0JP-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>(d)</span></i=
></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>With respect to supplemental
jurisdiction, a federal court has subject-matter jurisdiction over specified
state-law claims, see </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5HW2-D6RV-H0HC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect;&sect;
1367(a)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5HW2-D6RV-H0HC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>(c)</span></i=
></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
and its decision whether to exercise that jurisdiction after dismissing eve=
ry
claim over which it had original jurisdiction is purely discretionary, see,=
 <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>e.g., </i></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4MW8-SG00-004B-Y04G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Osborn</span>=
</i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4MW8-SG00-004B-Y04G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4MW8-SG00-004B-Y04G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Haley</span><=
/i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4MW8-SG00-004B-Y04G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 549 U.S. 22=
5,
245, 127 S. Ct. 881, 166 L. Ed. 2d 819</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-fa=
mily:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>It is undisputed that when this ca=
se was
removed, the District Court had original jurisdiction over the federal RICO
claim under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5HW2-D6RV-H0G3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1331</=
span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
and supplemental jurisdiction over the state-law claims, which were &quot;so
related to claims . . . within such original jurisdiction that they form[ed]
part of the same case or controversy,&quot; </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5HW2-D6RV-H0HC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1367(a=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>On dismissing the RICO claim, the =
court
retained its statutory supplemental jurisdiction over the state-law
claims.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Its decision not to
exercise that statutory authority was not based on a jurisdictional defect,
&nbsp;[***847]&nbsp;but on its &nbsp;[*636]&nbsp; discretionary choice.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>See &nbsp;[****3]&nbsp;</span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RKS-5JC0-004C-300N-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Chicago</span=
></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RKS-5JC0-004C-300N-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RKS-5JC0-004C-300N-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>International
College of Surgeons</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RKS-5JC0-004C-300N-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 522 U.S. 15=
6,
173, 118 S. Ct. 523, 139 L. Ed. 2d 525</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-fa=
mily:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. Pp. 638-641.</sp=
an></p>

