k'>
--which requires particularity when pleading &quot;fraud or mistake&quot; b=
ut
allows &quot;other conditions of a person's mind [to] be alleged
generally&quot;--does not require courts to credit a complaint's conclusory
statements without &nbsp;[****8]&nbsp;reference to its factual context.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5GYC-1WP1-6N19-F0YN-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Rule 9</span>=
</i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
merely excuses a party from pleading discriminatory intent under an elevated
pleading standard.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>It does no=
t give
him license to evade </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5GYC-1WP1-6N19-F0YK-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
