<p class=3DNormal32 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4FR0000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4FT0000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>To survive a motion to dismiss, a
complaint must contain sufficient factual matter, accepted as true, to
&quot;state a claim to relief that is plausible on its face.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4FP0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NSN-8840-004C-002M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NSN-8840-004C-002M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 570, 127=
 S.
Ct. 1955, 167 L. Ed. 2d 929</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times=
",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>A claim has facial plausibility wh=
en the
plaintiff pleads factual content that allows the court to draw the reasonab=
le
inference that the defendant is liable for the misconduct alleged.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4FS0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NSN-8840-004C-002M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NSN-8840-004C-002M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 556, 127=
 S.
Ct. 1955, 167 L. Ed. 2d 929</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times=
",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4GD0000400"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>The plausibility standard is not ak=
in to
a &quot;probability requirement,&quot; but it asks for more than a sheer
possibility that a defendant has acted unlawfully.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'>Ibid.</i><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Where a complaint pleads facts tha=
t are
&quot;merely consistent with&quot; a defendant's liability, it &quot;stops
short of the line between possibility and plausibility of 'entitlement to
relief.'&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4FV0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NSN-8840-004C-002M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NSN-8840-004C-002M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 557, 127=
 S.
Ct. 1955, 167 L. Ed. 2d 929</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times=
",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (brackets omitted). </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal32 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Two
working principles underlie our decision in <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style=
:normal'>Twombly.</i><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_II08C29RM5PM003RS46200CGC"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4GG0000400"></a>First, <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc11_20"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN11_1_2"></=
a>[11]
the tenet that a court must accept as true all of the allegations contained=
 in
a complaint is inapplicable to legal conclusions.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Threadbare recitals of the element=
s of a
cause of action, supported by mere conclusory statements, do not suffice.<s=
pan
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4GF0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NSN-8840-004C-002M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NSN-8840-004C-002M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 555, 127=
 S.
Ct. 1955, 167 L. Ed. 2d 929</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times=
",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (Although for the purposes of a
motion &nbsp;[****30]&nbsp;to dismiss we must take all of the factual
allegations in the complaint as true, we&nbsp;[**1950]&nbsp; &quot;are not
bound to accept as true a legal conclusion couched as a factual allegation&=
quot;
(internal quotation marks omitted)). <a name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4GJ0=
000400"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5GYC-1WP1-6N19-F0YK-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Rule 8</span>=
</i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
marks a notable and generous departure from the hypertechnical, code-pleadi=
ng
regime of a prior era, but it does not unlock the doors of discovery for
&nbsp;[*679]&nbsp; a plaintiff armed with nothing more than conclusions. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4JC0000400"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>Second, <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc12_18"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN12_1_2"></=
a>[12]
only a complaint that states a plausible claim for relief survives a motion=
 to
dismiss.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4GH0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NSN-8840-004C-002M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NSN-8840-004C-002M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 556, 127=
 S.
Ct. 1955, 167 L. Ed. 2d 929</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times=
",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4JC0000400_2"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>Determining whether a complaint sta=
tes a
plausible claim for relief will, as the Court of Appeals observed, be a
context-specific task that requires the reviewing court to draw on its judi=
cial
experience and common sense.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>=
</span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4JB0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NYV-G060-0038-X36S-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>490 F.3d at
157-158</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>But wher=
e the
well-pleaded facts do not permit the court to infer more than the mere
possibility of misconduct, the complaint has alleged--but it has not
&quot;show[n]&quot;--&quot;that the pleader is entitled to relief.&quot;<sp=
an
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5GYC-1WP1-6N19-F0YK-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
