here.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>In <i style=3D'mso-bidi=
-font-style:
normal'>Twombly</i>, the complaint alleged general wrongdoing that extended
over a &nbsp;[****38]&nbsp;period of years, </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4MK0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NSN-8840-004C-002M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>id.,</span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NSN-8840-004C-002M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> at 551, 127 =
S.
Ct. 1955, 167 L. Ed. 2d 929</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times=
",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, whereas here the complaint all=
eges
discrete wrongs--for instance, beatings--by lower level Government actors.<=
span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The allegations here, if true, and=
 if
condoned by petitioners, could be the basis for some inference of wrongful
intent on petitioners' part.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>Despite these distinctions, respondent's pleadings do not suffice to
state a claim.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Unlike in <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Twombly</i>, where the doctrine of <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>respondeat superior</i> could bind the
corporate defendant, here, as we have noted, petitioners cannot be held lia=
ble
unless they themselves acted on account of a constitutionally protected
characteristic.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Yet responden=
t's
complaint does not contain any factual allegation sufficient to plausibly
suggest petitioners' discriminatory state of mind.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>His pleadings thus do not meet the
standard necessary to comply with </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5GYC-1WP1-6N19-F0YK-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Rule 8</span>=
</i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal32 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[*684]&nbsp;
It is important to note, however, that we express no opinion concerning the
sufficiency of respondent's complaint against the defendants who are not be=
fore
us.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Respondent's account of h=
is prison
ordeal alleges serious official misconduct that we need not address here.<s=
pan
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Our decision is limited to the
determination that respondent's complaint does not entitle him to relief
&nbsp;[****39]&nbsp;from petitioners. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal32 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>C </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal32 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Respondent
offers three arguments that bear on our disposition of his case, but none is
persuasive. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal32 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>1&nbsp;[**1953]&nbsp;
</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal32 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Respondent
first says that our decision in <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Two=
mbly</i>
should be limited to pleadings made in the context of an antitrust dispute.=
 <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4MW0000400"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>Iqbal Brief 37-38.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>This argument is not supported by =
<i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Twombly</i> and is incompatible with t=
he
Federal Rules of Civil Procedure.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>Though <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Twombly</i> determine=
d the
sufficiency of a complaint sounding in antitrust, the decision was based on=
 our
interpretation and application of </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5GYC-1WP1-6N19-F0YK-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Rule 8</span>=
</i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4MV0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NSN-8840-004C-002M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>550 U.S., at =
554,
127 S. Ct. 1955, 167 L. Ed. 2d 929</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family=
:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WGBBPY0K1MNJ4MY0000400"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span><a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc14_=
12"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN14_1_1"></a>[14] That Rule in turn governs the pleadi=
ng
standard &quot;in all civil actions and proceedings in the United States
district courts.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span=
><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8JD7-3YB2-8T6X-706W-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
