<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1CB0000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>In instructing the jury on the
meaning of a RICO &quot;enterprise,&quot; the District Court relied largely=
 on
language in </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1C90000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Turkette</spa=
n></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 452 U.S. 57=
6,
101 S. Ct. 2524, 69 L. Ed. 2d 246 (1981)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-=
family:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The court told the jurors that, in=
 order
to establish the existence of such an enterprise, the Government had to pro=
ve
that:<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>&quot;(1) There [was] an
ongoing organization with some sort of framework, formal or informal, for
carrying out its objectives; and (2) the various members and associates of =
the
association function[ed] as a continuing unit to achieve a common
purpose.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>App. 112.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Over petitioner's objection, the c=
ourt
also told the jury that it could &quot;find an enterprise where an associat=
ion
of individuals, without structural hierarchy, form[ed] solely for the purpo=
se
of carrying out a pattern of racketeering acts&quot; and that &quot;[c]ommon
sense suggests that the existence of an association-in-fact is oftentimes m=
ore
readily proven by what is [sic] does, rather than by abstract analysis
&nbsp;[****9]&nbsp;of its structure.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=
&nbsp;
</span><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i>, at 111-112.</span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn409' href=3D"#_ftn409" name=3D"_ftnref409" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>1</span><=
/sup></a></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[*943]&nbsp;
Petitioner requested an instruction &nbsp;[***1274]&nbsp;that the Government
was required to prove that the enterprise &quot;had an ongoing organization=
, a
core membership that functioned as a continuing unit, and an ascertainable =
structural
hierarchy distinct from the charged predicate acts.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'>Id.</i>,
at 95.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The District Court ref=
used
to give that instruction. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1CD0000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1DX0000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Petitioner was convicted on 11 of
the 12 counts against him, including the RICO counts, and was sentenced to =
151
months' imprisonment.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>In a su=
mmary
order, the Court of Appeals for the Second Circuit affirmed his
&nbsp;[****11]&nbsp;conviction but vacated the sentence on a ground not
relevant to the issues before us.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </=
span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1CC0000400"></a><a
