<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>A </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc2_32"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN2_1_8"></a>=
<span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>[2]<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>RICO makes it &quot;unlawful for a=
ny
person employed by or <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>associated wi=
th any
enterprise</i> engaged in, or the activities of which affect, interstate or
foreign commerce, to conduct or participate, directly or indirectly, in the
conduct of such enterprise's affairs through a pattern of racketeering acti=
vity
&nbsp;[*944]&nbsp; or collection of unlawful debt.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
1962(c)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'> (emphasis added). </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1F00000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1F20000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1GX0000400"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFc=
lscc3_32"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN3_1_8"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>[3]<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The statute does not specifically =
define
the outer boundaries of the &quot;enterprise&quot; concept but states that =
the
term &quot;includes any individual, partnership, corporation, association, =
or
other legal entity, and any union or group of individuals associated in fact
although not a legal entity.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; <=
/span></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1961(4=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.</span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn410' href=3D"#_ftn410" name=3D"_ftnref410" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>2</span><=
/sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>This enumeration of included enter=
prises
is obviously broad, &nbsp;[***1275]&nbsp;encompassing
&nbsp;[****12]&nbsp;&quot;<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>any</i> .=
 . .
group of individuals associated in fact.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'>Ibid.</i>
(emphasis added).<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The term
&quot;any&quot; ensures that the definition has a wide reach, see, <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>e.g., </i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1DY0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4RN5-0G70-TXFX-12B7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Ali</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4RN5-0G70-TXFX-12B7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4RN5-0G70-TXFX-12B7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Federal Burea=
u of
Prisons</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4RN5-0G70-TXFX-12B7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 552 U.S. 21=
4,
218-219, 128 S. Ct. 831, 169 L. Ed. 2d 680 (2008)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
and the very concept of an association in fact is expansive.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>In addition, <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc4_32"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN4_1_8"></a>=
[4] the
RICO statute provides that its terms are to be &quot;liberally construed to
effectuate its remedial purposes.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nb=
sp;
</span>&sect; 904(a), 84 Stat. 947, note following </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
1961</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-fon=
t-family:
Times;color:black'>; see also, <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>e.g.=
,</i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1F10000400"></a><a
