</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-40C0-003B-S1ST-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 464 U.S. 16,
21, 104 S. Ct. 296, 78 L. Ed. 2d 17 (1983)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(noting &quot;the pattern of the RICO statute in utilizing terms and concep=
ts
of breadth&quot;). </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1H00000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1H20000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>In light of these statutory
features, we explained in <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Turkette<=
/i>
that <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc7_26"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN7_1=
_7"></a>[7]
&quot;an enterprise includes any union or group of individuals associated in
fact&quot; and that RICO reaches &quot;a group of persons associated togeth=
er
for a common purpose of engaging in a course of conduct.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1GY0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>452 U.S., at =
580,
583, 101 S. Ct. 2524, 69 L. Ed. 2d 246</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-fa=
mily:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Such &nbsp;[*945]&nbsp; an enterpr=
ise,
we said, &quot;is proved by evidence of an ongoing organization, formal or
informal, and by evidence that the various associates function as a continu=
ing
unit.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1H10000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id</span></i>=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>., at 583, 10=
1 S.
Ct. 2524, 69 L. Ed. 2d 246</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I500PFN70K1MNJ2BF0000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Notwithstanding these precedents,
the dissent asserts that the definition of a RICO enterprise is limited to
&quot;businesslike entities.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>See </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I500PFN70K1MNJ2BD0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4WGD-3S70-TXFX-12BB-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>post</span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4WGD-3S70-TXFX-12BB-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 952, 173=
 L.
Ed. 2d, at 1279-1282</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (opinion of Stevens, J.).<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>We see no basis to impose such an
extratextual requirement.</span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn411'
href=3D"#_ftn411" name=3D"_ftnref411" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-f=
amily:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>3</span></sup></a></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[**2244]&nbsp;B
</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>As
noted, the specific question on which we granted certiorari is whether an
association-in-fact enterprise must have &quot;an ascertainable structure
beyond that inherent in the pattern of racketeering activity in which it
engages.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Pet. for Cert.
i.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>We will break this questio=
n into
three parts.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>First, must an
association-in-fact enterprise have a &quot;structure&quot;?<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Second, must the structure be
&quot;ascertainable&quot;?<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Th=
ird,
must the &quot;structure&quot; go &quot;beyond that inherent in the pattern=
 of racketeering
activity&quot; in which its &nbsp;[****15]&nbsp;members engage? </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>&quot;Structure.&quot;</span></i=
><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>We agree with petitioner that <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc9_24"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN9_1_7"></a>=
[9] an
association-in-fact enterprise must have a structure.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>In the sense relevant here, the te=
rm
&quot;structure&quot; means &quot;[t]he way in which parts are arranged or =
put
together to &nbsp;[***1276]&nbsp;form a whole&quot; &nbsp;[*946]&nbsp; and
&quot;[t]he interrelation or arrangement of parts in a complex
entity.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>American Herita=
ge
Dictionary 1718 (4th ed. 2000); see also Random House Dictionary of the Eng=
lish
Language 1410 (1967) (defining structure to mean, among other things, &quot=
;the
pattern of relationships, as of status or friendship, existing among the
members of a group or society&quot;). </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I7W5WWXXDS0000BT00M00038"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1JD0000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc10_23"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN10_1_4"></=
a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>[10]<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>From the terms of RICO, it is appa=
rent
that an association-in-fact enterprise must have at least three structural
features:<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>a purpose, relation=
ships
among those associated with the enterprise, and longevity sufficient to per=
mit
these associates to pursue the enterprise's purpose.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>As we succinctly put it in <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Turkette</i>, an association-in-fact
enterprise is &quot;a group of persons associated together for a common pur=
pose
of engaging in a course of conduct.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&=
nbsp;
</span></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1JC0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>452 U.S., at =
583,
101 S. Ct. 2524, 69 L. Ed. 2d 246</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:=
"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc11_21"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN11_1_3"></=
a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>[11]<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>That an &quot;enterprise&quot; mus=
t have
a purpose is apparent from the meaning of the term in ordinary usage, <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>i.e.</i>, a &quot;venture,&quot;
&quot;undertaking,&quot; or &quot;project.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>&nbsp;[****16]&nbsp;Webster's Thir=
d New
International Dictionary 757 (1976).<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>The concept of &quot;associat[ion]&quot; requires both interpersonal
relationships and a common interest.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>See <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>id.</i>, at 132 (defining
&quot;association&quot; as &quot;an organization of persons having a common
interest&quot;); Black's Law Dictionary 156 (rev. 4th ed. 1968) (defining
&quot;association&quot; as a &quot;collection of persons who have joined
together for a certain object&quot;).<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Section 1962(=
c)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
reinforces this conclusion and also shows that an &quot;enterprise&quot; mu=
st
have some longevity, since the offense proscribed by that provision demands
proof that the enterprise had &quot;affairs&quot; of sufficient duration to
permit an associate to &quot;participate&quot; in those affairs through &qu=
ot;a
pattern of racketeering activity.&quot; </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc12_19"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN12_1_3"></=
a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>[12]<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Although an association-in-fact
enterprise must have these structural features, it does not follow that a
district court must use the term &quot;structure&quot; in its jury
instructions.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc13_16"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN13_1_3"></=
a>[13] A
trial judge has considerable discretion in choosing the language of an
instruction so long as the substance of the relevant point is adequately
expressed. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[*947]&nbsp;
<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>&quot;Ascertainable.&quot;</i><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN14_1_2"></a>[14] <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc14_1=
3"></a>Whenever
a jury is told that it must find the existence of an element beyond a
reasonable doubt, that element must be &quot;ascertainable&quot;
&nbsp;[****17]&nbsp;or else the jury could not find that it was proved.
&nbsp;[**2245]&nbsp; Therefore, telling the members of the jury that they h=
ad
to ascertain the existence of an &quot;ascertainable structure&quot; would =
have
been redundant and potentially misleading. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1JG0000400"></a><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-st=
yle:
normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Ti=
mes;
color:black'>&quot;Beyond that inherent in the pattern of racketeering
activity.&quot;</span></i><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fare=
ast-font-family:
Times;color:black'><span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>This phra=
se may
be interpreted in at least two different ways, and its correctness depends =
on
the particular sense in which the phrase is used.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>If the phrase is interpreted to me=
an
that the existence of an enterprise is a separate element that must be prov=
ed,
it is of course correct.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>As we
explained in <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Turkette</i>, <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc15_11"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN15_1_2"></=
a>[15]
the existence of an enterprise is an element distinct from the pattern of
racketeering activity and &quot;proof of one does not necessarily establish=
 the
other.&quot;</span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn412' href=3D"#_ftn412"
name=3D"_ftnref412" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",seri=
f;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>4</span></sup></a><span style=3D'font-family=
:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1JF0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>452 U.S., at =
583,
101 S. Ct. 2524, 69 L. Ed. 2d 246</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:=
"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>&nbsp;[****18]&nbsp;On the other h=
and,
if the phrase is used to mean that the existence of an enterprise may never=
 be
inferred from &nbsp;[***1277]&nbsp;the evidence showing that persons associ=
ated
with the enterprise engaged in a pattern of racketeering activity, it is
incorrect.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>We recognized in <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Turkette</i> that <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc16_8"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN16_1_0"></a=
>[16]
the evidence used to prove the pattern of racketeering activity and the
evidence establishing an enterprise &quot;may in particular cases
coalesce.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Ibid.</i></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>C </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
crux of petitioner's argument is that a RICO enterprise must have structural
features in addition to those that &nbsp;[*948]&nbsp; we think can be fairly
inferred from the language of the statute.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=
&nbsp;
</span>Although petitioner concedes that an association-in-fact enterprise =
may
be an &quot;'informal'&quot; group and that &quot;not 'much'&quot; structur=
e is
needed, Reply Brief for Petitioner 24, he contends that such an enterprise =
must
have at least some additional structural attributes, such as a structural
&quot;hierarchy,&quot; &quot;role differentiation,&quot; a &quot;unique <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>modus operandi</i>,&quot; a &quot;chai=
n of
command,&quot; &quot;professionalism and sophistication of organization,&qu=
ot;
&quot;diversity and complexity of crimes,&quot; &quot;membership dues, rules
and regulations,&quot; &quot;uncharged or additional crimes aside from pred=
icate
acts,&quot; an &quot;internal &nbsp;[****19]&nbsp;discipline mechanism,&quo=
t;
&quot;regular meetings regarding enterprise affairs,&quot; an &quot;enterpr=
ise
'name,'&quot; and &quot;induction or initiation ceremonies and rituals,&quo=
t;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'>id.</i>,
at 31-35; see also Brief for Petitioner 26-28, 33; Tr. of Oral Arg. 6, 8, 1=
7. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>We
see no basis in the language of RICO for the structural requirements that
petitioner asks us to recognize.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </s=
pan>As
we said in <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Turkette</i>, <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc17_8"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN17_1_0"></a=
>[17] an
association-in-fact enterprise is simply a continuing unit that functions w=
ith
a common purpose.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Such a grou=
p need
not have a hierarchical structure or a &quot;chain of command&quot;; decisi=
ons
may be made on an ad hoc basis and by any number of methods--by majority vo=
te,
consensus, a show of strength, etc.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>Members of the group need not have fixed roles; different members may
perform different roles at different times.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The group need not have a name, re=
gular
meetings, dues, established rules and regulations, disciplinary procedures,=
 or
induction or initiation ceremonies.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>While the group must function as a continuing unit and remain in
existence long enough to pursue a course of conduct, nothing in RICO exempt=
s an
enterprise whose associates engage in spurts of activity punctuated by peri=
ods
of quiescence.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Nor is the sta=
tute
limited &nbsp;[****20]&nbsp;to groups whose crimes are sophisticated,
diverse,&nbsp;[**2246]&nbsp; complex, or unique; for example, a group that =
does
nothing but engage in extortion through old-fashioned, unsophisticated, and
brutal means may fall squarely within the statute's reach. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[*949]&nbsp;
The breadth of the &quot;enterprise&quot; concept in RICO is highlighted by
comparing the statute with other federal statutes that target organized
criminal groups.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>For example,=
 </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PJ-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
1955(b)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>, which was enacted together with RICO as part of the
Organized Crime Control Act of 1970, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5CD7-HSC0-01XN-S17Y-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>Pub. L. 91-452, 84 Stat. 922</span>=
</i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
defines an &quot;illegal gambling business&quot; as one that &quot;involves
five or more persons who conduct, finance, manage, supervise, direct, or own
all or part of such business.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>A &quot;continuing criminal enterprise,&quot; as defined in </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SDD-0C82-8T6X-73J4-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>21 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
848(c)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-f=
ont-family:
Times;color:black'>, must involve more than five persons who act in concert=
 and
must have an &quot;organizer,&quot; supervisor, or other manager.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Congress included
&nbsp;[***1278]&nbsp;no such requirements in RICO. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>III
</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
