<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[*952]&nbsp;
Justice <b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Stevens,</b> with whom Jus=
tice <b
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Breyer</b> joins, dissenting. </span>=
</p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
my view, Congress intended the term &quot;enterprise&quot; as it is used in=
 the
Racketeer Influenced and Corrupt Organizations Act (RICO), </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
1961 </span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>et seq.</span=
></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
to refer only to businesslike entities that have an existence apart from the
predicate acts committed by their employees or associates.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The trial judge in this case commi=
tted
two significant errors relating to the meaning of that term.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>First, he instructed the jury that
&quot;an association of individuals, without structural hierarchy, form[ed]
solely for the purpose of carrying out a pattern of racketeering acts&quot;=
 can
constitute an enterprise.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>App.
112.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>And he&nbsp;[**2248]&nbs=
p;
allowed the jury to find that element satisfied by evidence showing a group=
 of
criminals with no existence beyond its intermittent commission of racketeer=
ing
acts and related offenses.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Be=
cause
&nbsp;[***1280]&nbsp;the Court's decision affirming petitioner's conviction=
 is
inconsistent with the statutory meaning of the term enterprise and serves to
expand RICO liability far beyond the bounds Congress intended, I respectful=
ly
dissent. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>I </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>RICO
makes it &quot;unlawful for any person employed &nbsp;[****26]&nbsp;by or
associated with any enterprise engaged in, or the activities of which affec=
t,
interstate or foreign commerce, to conduct or participate, directly or
indirectly, in the conduct of such enterprise's affairs through a pattern of
racketeering activity.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>=
</span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The statute defines
&quot;enterprise&quot; to include &quot;any individual, partnership,
corporation, association, or other legal entity, and any union or group of
individuals associated in fact although not a legal entity.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1961(4=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I500PFN70K1MNJ2BN0000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>It is clear from the statute and=
 our
earlier decisions construing the term that Congress used &quot;enterprise&q=
uot;
in these provisions in the sense of &quot;a business organization,&quot;
Webster's Third New International Dictionary 757 (1976), rather than &quot;a
'venture,' 'undertaking,' or 'project,'&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I500PFN70K1MNJ2BM0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4WGD-3S70-TXFX-12BB-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>ante</span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4WGD-3S70-TXFX-12BB-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 946, 173=
 L.
Ed. 2d, at 1276</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> &nbsp;[*953]&nbsp; (quoting
Webster's Third New International Dictionary, at 757).<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>First, the terms &quot;individual,
partnership, corporation, association, or other legal entity&quot; describe
entities with formal legal structures most commonly established for business
purposes.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1961(4=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>In context, the subsequent referen=
ce to
any &quot;union or group of individuals associated in fact <i style=3D'mso-=
bidi-font-style:
normal'>although not a legal entity</i>&quot; reflects an intended commonal=
ity
&nbsp;[****27]&nbsp;between the legal and nonlegal entities included in the
provision. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I7W5WWY207P000BT00M0003P"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1MX0000400"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:nor=
mal'>Ibid.</i>
(emphasis added).<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>&quot;The
juxtaposition of the two phrases suggests that 'associated in fact' just me=
ans
structured without the aid of legally defined structural forms such as the
business corporation.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><=
/span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1MW0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4S68-N4N0-TXFX-92HR-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Limestone
Development Corp.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4S68-N4N0-TXFX-92HR-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4S68-N4N0-TXFX-92HR-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
