name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1PY0000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I7TF82HKH9100008MKR0068C"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1R10000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>That an enterprise must have
businesslike characteristics is confirmed by the text of </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
and our decision in </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1PX0000400"></=
a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S70-NFC0-003B-R50T-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Reves</span><=
/i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S70-NFC0-003B-R50T-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S70-NFC0-003B-R50T-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Ernst &amp; Y=
oung</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S70-NFC0-003B-R50T-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 507 U.S. 17=
0,
113 S. Ct. 1163, 122 L. Ed. 2d 525 (1993)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font=
-family:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I7TF82HKJXD00008MKR0068D"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1R30000400"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Section 1962(=
c)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
creates liability for &quot;conduct[ing] or participat[ing] . . . in the
conduct of [an] enterprise's affairs through a pattern of racketeering
activity.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>In <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Reves,</i> we examined that provision's
meaning and held that, &quot;[i]n order to 'participate, directly or
indirectly, in the conduct of such enterprise's affairs,' one must have some
part in directing those affairs.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbs=
p;
</span></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1R00000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S70-NFC0-003B-R50T-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S70-NFC0-003B-R50T-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 179, 113=
 S.
Ct. 1163, 122 L. Ed. 2d 525</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times=
",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (quoting </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>).<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>It is not enough for a defendant to
&nbsp;[*954]&nbsp; &quot;carry on&quot; or &quot;participate in&quot; an
enterprise's affairs &nbsp;[***1281]&nbsp;&nbsp;[**2249]&nbsp;through a pat=
tern
of racketeering activity; instead, evidence that he operated, managed, or
directed those affairs is required. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1R30000400_2"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>See </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1R20000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S70-NFC0-003B-R50T-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S70-NFC0-003B-R50T-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 177-179,=
 113
S. Ct. 1163, 122 L. Ed. 2d 525</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Ti=
mes",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>This requirement confirms that the
enterprise element demands evidence of a certain quantum of businesslike
organization--<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>i.e.</i>, a system of
processes, dealings, &nbsp;[****29]&nbsp;or other affairs that can be
&quot;directed.&quot; </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I7W5WWY56TD000BT00M00043"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1R50000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Our cases also make clear that an
enterprise &quot;is an entity separate and apart from the pattern of activi=
ty
in which it engages.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></=
span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1R40000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Turkette</spa=
n></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 452 U.S. 57=
6,
583, 101 S. Ct. 2524, 69 L. Ed. 2d 246 (1981)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>As with the requirement that an
enterprise have businesslike characteristics, that an enterprise must have a
separate existence is confirmed by </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
and <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Reves.</i><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>If an entity's existence consisted
solely of its members' performance of a pattern of racketeering acts, the
&quot;enterprise's affairs&quot; would be synonymous with the &quot;pattern=
 of
racketeering activity.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>=
</span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Section 1962(=
c)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
would then prohibit an individual from conducting or participating in &quot=
;the
conduct of [a pattern of racketeering activity] through a pattern of
racketeering activity&quot;--a reading that is unbearably redundant,
particularly in a case like this one in which a single pattern of activity =
is
alleged.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The only way to avoi=
d that
result is to require that an &quot;enterprise's affairs&quot; be something
other than the pattern of racketeering activity undertaken by its members.<=
/span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn415' href=3D"#_ftn415" name=3D"_ftnref415" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>2</span><=
/sup></a></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[*955]&nbsp;
<a name=3D"Bookmark_I7W5WWY6D00000BT00M00047"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1RJ0000400"></a>Recognizing an enterprise's
businesslike nature and its distinctness from the pattern of predicate
&nbsp;[****31]&nbsp;acts, however, does not answer the question of what pro=
of
each element requires. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I7TF82HM06700008MKR0050J"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1RM0000400"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>In cases involving a legal entity, =
the
matter of proving the enterprise element is straightforward, as the entity's
legal existence will always be something apart from the pattern of activity
performed by the defendant or his associates.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Cf. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1RH0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:437X-B220-004C-0032-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Cedric Kushner
Promotions, Ltd.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:437X-B220-004C-0032-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:437X-B220-004C-0032-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>King</span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:437X-B220-004C-0032-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 533 U.S. 15=
8,
163, 121 S. Ct. 2087, 150 L. Ed. 2d 198 (2001)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1RM0000400_2"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>But in the case of an association-i=
n-fact
enterprise, the Government must adduce other evidence of the entity's
&quot;separate&quot; existence and &quot;ongoing organization.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4WN1JSN0K1MNJ1RK0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Turkette</spa=
n></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 452 U.S., at
583, 101 S. Ct. 2524, 69 L. Ed. 2d 246</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-fa=
mily:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>There may be cases in which a jury=
 can
infer that existence and continuity from the evidence used to establish the
pattern of racketeering activity.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </=
span><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Ibid.</i><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>But that will be true only when the
pattern of activity is so complex that it could not be performed in the abs=
ence
of structures or processes for planning or concealing the illegal conduct
beyond those inherent in performing the predicate
&nbsp;[***1282]&nbsp;acts.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Mo=
re
often, proof of an enterprise's separate existence will require different
evidence from that used to establish the pattern of predicate acts. </span>=
</p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Precisely
what proof is required in each case is a more difficult question,
&nbsp;[****32]&nbsp;largely&nbsp;[**2250]&nbsp; due to the abundant variety=
 of
RICO predicates and enterprises.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>Because covered enterprises are necessarily businesslike in nature,
however, proof of an association-in-fact enterprise's separate existence wi=
ll
generally require evidence of rules, routines, or processes through which t=
he
entity maintains its continuing operations and seeks to conceal its illegal
acts.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>As petitioner suggests,=
 this
requirement will usually be satisfied by evidence that &nbsp;[*956]&nbsp; t=
he
association has an &quot;ascertainable structure beyond that inherent in the
pattern of racketeering activity in which it engages.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Pet. for Cert. i.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Examples of such structure include=
 an
organizational hierarchy, a &quot;framework for making decisions,&quot; an
&quot;internal discipline mechanism,&quot; &quot;regular meetings,&quot; or=
 a
practice of &quot;reinvest[ing] . . . proceeds to promote and expand the
enterprise.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Reply Brief=
 for
Petitioner 31-34.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>In other ca=
ses,
the enterprise's existence might be established through evidence that it
provides goods or services to third parties, as such an undertaking will
require organizational elements more comprehensive than those necessary to
perform a pattern of predicate acts.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>Thus, the evidence needed to establish an enterprise
&nbsp;[****33]&nbsp;will vary from case to case, but in every case the
Government must carry its burden of proving that an alleged enterprise has =
an
existence separate from the pattern of racketeering activity undertaken by =
its
constituents. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>II </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I500PFN70K1MNJ2BR0000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>In some respects, my reading of =
the
statute is not very different from that adopted by the Court.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>We agree that &quot;an
association-in-fact enterprise must have at least three structural features=
:<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>a purpose, relationships among tho=
se
associated with the enterprise, and longevity sufficient to permit these
associates to pursue the enterprise's purpose.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I500PFN70K1MNJ2BP0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4WGD-3S70-TXFX-12BB-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Ante</span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4WGD-3S70-TXFX-12BB-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 946, 173=
 L.
Ed. 2d, at 1276</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>But the Court stops short of giving
content to that requirement.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>=
It
states only that RICO &quot;demands proof that the enterprise had 'affairs'=
 of
sufficient duration to permit an associate to 'participate' in those affairs
through 'a pattern of racketeering activity,'&quot; before concluding that
&quot;[a] trial judge has considerable discretion in choosing the language =
of
an instruction&quot; and need not use the term &quot;structure.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'>Ibid</i>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>While I agree the word
&quot;structure&quot; is not talismanic, I would hold that the instructions
must convey the requirement that the alleged enterprise have an existence a=
part
from the alleged pattern &nbsp;[****34]&nbsp;of predicate acts.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>&nbsp;[*957]&nbsp; The Court's dec=
ision,
by contrast, will allow juries to infer the existence of an enterprise in e=
very
case involving a pattern of racketeering activity undertaken by two or more
associates. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>By
permitting the Government to prove both elements with the same evidence, the
Court renders the enterprise requirement essentially meaningless in
association-in-fact cases. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I500PFN70K1MNJ2BW0000400"></=
a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>It also threatens to make that cate=
gory
of </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
offenses indistinguishable from conspiracies to commit predicate acts, see =
</span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5032-D6RV-H544-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 371</s=
pan></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
as the only remaining difference is </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>'s
pattern requirement.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The Court
resists this criticism, arguing that </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
&quot;demands much more&quot; than the inchoate &nbsp;[***1283]&nbsp;offense
defined in </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5032-D6RV-H544-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 371</s=
pan></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I500PFN70K1MNJ2BV0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4WGD-3S70-TXFX-12BB-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Ante</span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4WGD-3S70-TXFX-12BB-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 950, 173=
 L.
Ed. 2d, at 1278</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>It states that the latter &quot;ma=
y be
completed in the brief period needed for the formation of the agreement and=
 the
commission of a single overt act in furtherance of the conspiracy,&quot;
whereas the former requires the creation of &quot;a group with a common pur=
pose
and course of conduct--and the actual commission of a pattern of predicate
offenses.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Ibid.</i><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Given that it is also unlawful to
conspire to violate </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
see </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(d=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
this comment provides no assurance that </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5032-D6RV-H544-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>RICO and &sec=
t;
371</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font=
-family:
Times;color:black'> &nbsp;[****35]&nbsp;offenses remain distinct.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Only if proof of the enterprise
element--the &quot;group with a common purpose&nbsp;[**2251]&nbsp; and cour=
se
of conduct&quot;--requires evidence of activity or organization beyond that
inherent in the pattern of predicate acts will RICO offenses retain an iden=
tity
distinct from </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5032-D6RV-H544-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 371</s=
pan></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
offenses. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I500PFN70K1MNJ2G10000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>This case illustrates these
concerns.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The trial judge
instructed the jury that an enterprise need have only the degree of
organization necessary &quot;for carrying out its objectives&quot; and that=
 it
could &quot;find an enterprise where an association of individuals, without
structural hierarchy, forms solely for the purpose of carrying out a patter=
n of
racketeering acts.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>App.=
 112.</span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn416' href=3D"#_ftn416" name=3D"_ftnref416" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>3</span><=
/sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>These instructions were plainly
deficient, as they did not require the Government to prove that
&nbsp;[*958]&nbsp; the alleged enterprise had an existence apart from the
pattern of predicate acts.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>In=
stead,
they permitted the Government's proof of the enterprise's structure and
continuing nature--requirements on which all agree--to consist only of evid=
ence
that petitioner and his associates performed a pattern of racketeering
activity. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Petitioner's
requested &nbsp;[****36]&nbsp;instruction would have required the jury to f=
ind
that the alleged enterprise &quot;had an ongoing organization, a core
membership that functioned as a continuing unit, and an ascertainable
structural hierarchy distinct from the charged predicate acts.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'>Id.</i>,
at 95.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>That instruction does =
not
precisely track my understanding of the statute; although evidence of
&quot;structural hierarchy&quot; can evidence an enterprise, it is not
necessary to establish that element.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>Nevertheless, the proposed instruction would have better directed the
jury to consider whether the alleged enterprise possessed the separate
existence necessary to expose petitioner to liability under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
and the trial judge should have considered an instruction along those lines=
. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
trial judge also erred in finding the Government's evidence in this case
sufficient to support petitioner's RICO convictions.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Petitioner was alleged to have
participated and conspired to participate in the conduct of an enterprise's
affairs through a pattern of racketeering activity consisting of one act of
bank robbery and three acts of interstate transportation of stolen funds.<s=
pan
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'>Id.</i>,
at 15-19.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The &quot;primary
goals&quot; of the alleged enterprise &quot;included
&nbsp;[****37]&nbsp;generating money for its members and associates through=
 the
commission of criminal activity, including bank robberies, bank burglaries =
and
interstate transportation of stolen money.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'>Id.</i>,
at 14.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>And its <i style=3D'ms=
o-bidi-font-style:
normal'>modus operandi</i> was to congregate periodically when an associate=
 had
a lead on a night-deposit box that the group could break into.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Whoever among the associates was
available would bring screwdrivers, crowbars, &nbsp;[***1284]&nbsp;and
walkie-talkies to the location.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>Some acted as lookouts, while others retrieved the money.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>When the endeavor was successful, =
the
participants &nbsp;[*959]&nbsp; would split the proceeds.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Thus, the group's purpose and
activities, and petitioner's participation therein, were limited to sporadic
acts of taking money from bank deposit boxes.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>There is no evidence in RICO's tex=
t or
history that Congress intended it to reach such ad hoc associations of thie=
ves.
</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>III
</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal33 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Because
the instructions and evidence in this case did not satisfy the requirement =
that
an alleged enterprise have an existence separate and apart from the pattern=
 of
activity in which it engages, I respectfully dissent. </span></p>

