<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_10_6"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>&nbsp;[*1]&nbsp;&nbsp;[***946]&n=
bsp;&nbsp;[**984]&nbsp;
Respondent New York City taxes the possession of cigarettes.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Petitioner Hemi Group, based in New
Mexico, sells cigarettes online to residents of the City.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Neither state nor city law requires
out-of-state sellers such as Hemi to charge, collect, or remit the City's t=
ax;
instead, the City must recover its tax on out-of-state sales directly from =
the
purchasers.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>But the Jenkins A=
ct, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:61XJ-4HH3-GXJ9-33PC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>15 U.S.C.
&sect;&sect; 375-378</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, requires out-of-state sellers =
to
submit customer information to the States into which they ship cigarettes, =
and
New York State has agreed to forward that information to the City.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>That information helps the City tr=
ack
down cigarette purchasers who do not pay their taxes.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Against that backdrop, the City fi=
led
this lawsuit under the Racketeer Influenced and Corrupt Organizations Act
(RICO), alleging that Hemi's failure to file the Jenkins Act reports with t=
he
State constituted mail and wire fraud, which are defined as &quot;racketeer=
ing
activit[ies],&quot; </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
1961(1)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>, subject to enforcement under civil </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>RICO, &sect;
1964(c)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The Dist=
rict
Court dismissed the claims, but the Second &nbsp;[****2]&nbsp;Circuit vacat=
ed
the judgment and remanded.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Am=
ong
other things, the Court of Appeals held that the City's asserted injury--lo=
st
tax revenue--came about &quot;by reason of&quot; the predicate mail and wire
frauds.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>It accordingly determ=
ined
that the City had stated a valid RICO claim. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_11_8"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>&nbsp;[*2]&nbsp; <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Held:</i> The judgment is reversed, an=
d the
case is remanded. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_12_8"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4TCJ-FMR0-TXFX-4226-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>541 F.3d 425<=
/span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
reversed and remanded. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_13_7"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Chief Justice Roberts delivered =
the
opinion of the Court in part, concluding that because the City cannot show =
that
it lost tax revenue &quot;by reason of&quot; the alleged RICO violation, it
cannot state a RICO claim.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></=
span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:7XMP-8RB0-YB0V-912G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Pp. ____ - __=
__,
175 L. Ed. 2d, at 950-956</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",=
serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_14_7"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>(a) To establish that an injury =
came
about &quot;by reason of&quot; a RICO violation, a plaintiff must show that=
 a
predicate offense &quot;not only was a 'but for' cause of his injury, but w=
as
the proximate cause as well.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; <=
/span></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Holmes</span>=
</i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Securities
Investor Protection Corporation</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 503 U.S. 25=
8,
268, 112 S. Ct. 1311, 117 L. Ed. 2d 532</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-f=
amily:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Proximate cause for RICO purposes =
should
be evaluated&nbsp;[**985]&nbsp; in light of its common-law foundations; it =
thus
requires &quot;some direct relation between the injury asserted and the
injurious conduct alleged.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </s=
pan><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Ibid.</i><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>A link that is &quot;too remote,&q=
uot;
&quot;purely contingent,&quot; or &quot;indirec[t]&quot; is insufficient.<s=
pan
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 271, 274,
112 S. Ct. 1311, 117 L. Ed. 2d 532</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family=
:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_15_6"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The City's causal theory cannot
&nbsp;[****3]&nbsp;satisfy RICO's direct relationship requirement.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Indeed, the causal link here is fa=
r more
attenuated than the one the Court rejected as &quot;purely contingent&quot;=
 and
&quot;too remote&quot; in <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Holmes</i=
>. </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 271, 112=
 S.
Ct. 1311, 117 L. Ed. 2d 532</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times=
",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>According to the City, Hemi commit=
ted
fraud by selling cigarettes to city residents and failing to submit the
required customer information to the State.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Without the reports from Hemi, the=
 State
could not pass on the information to the City, even if it had been so
inclined.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Some of the custome=
rs
legally obligated to pay the cigarette tax to the City failed to do so.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Because the City did not receive t=
he
customer information, it could not determine which customers had failed to =
pay
the tax.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The City thus could =
not
pursue those customers for payment.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>The City thereby was injured in the amount of the portion of back ta=
xes
that were never collected.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>As=
 the
Court reiterated in <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Holmes</i>,
&quot;[t]he general tendency of the law, in regard &nbsp;[***947]&nbsp;to
damages at least, is not to go beyond the first step,&quot; </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>id.,</span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> at 271-272, =
112
S. Ct. 1311, 117 L. Ed. 2d 532</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Ti=
mes",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, and that &quot;general
tendency&quot; applies with full force to proximate cause inquiries under R=
ICO,
<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>e.g., ibid.</i><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Because the City's causation theory
requires the Court to move well beyond the first step, &nbsp;[****4]&nbsp;t=
hat
theory cannot satisfy RICO's direct relationship requirement. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_clspara_16_5"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The City's claim suffers from the
same defect as the RICO claim rejected in </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4K41-DS80-004C-200J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Anza</span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4K41-DS80-004C-200J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4K41-DS80-004C-200J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Ideal Steel
Supply Corp.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4K41-DS80-004C-200J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 547 U.S. 45=
1,
458-461, 126 S. Ct. 1991, 164 L. Ed. 2d 720</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
where the conduct directly causing the harm was distinct from the conduct
giving rise to the fraud, see </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4K41-DS80-004C-200J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>id</span></i>=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4K41-DS80-004C-200J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>., at 458, 12=
6 S.
Ct. 1991, 164 L. Ed. 2d 720</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times=
",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Indeed, the disconnect between the
asserted injury and the alleged fraud in this case is even sharper.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>In <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style=
:normal'>Anza,</i>
the same party had both engaged in the harmful conduct and committed the
fraudulent act.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Here, the Cit=
y's
theory of liability rests not just on separate <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-st=
yle:
normal'>actions</i>, but separate actions carried out by
separate&nbsp;[*3]&nbsp; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>parties.</=
i><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The City's theory thus requires th=
at the
Court extend RICO liability to situations where the defendant's fraud on the
third party (the State) has made it easier for a <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-=
style:
normal'>fourth</i> party (the taxpayer) to cause harm to the plaintiff (the
City).<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Indeed, the fourth-par=
ty
taxpayers here only caused harm to the City in the first place if they deci=
ded
not to pay taxes they were legally obligated to pay.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Put simply, Hemi's obligation was =
to
file Jenkins Act reports with the State, not the City, and the City's harm =
was
directly caused by the customers, not Hemi.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The &nbsp;[****5]&nbsp;Court has n=
ever
before stretched the causal chain of a RICO violation so far, and declines =
to
do so today.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>See, <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>e.g., </i></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4K41-DS80-004C-200J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>id.,</span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
