n.
Code &sect; 11-1302(a) (2008)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Tim=
es",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>; see also Record A1016.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>When purchasers buy cigarettes from
in-state vendors, the seller is responsible for charging, collecting, and
remitting the tax.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6873-NR53-CGX8-02K3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>N. Y. Tax Law
Ann. &sect; 471(2) (West Supp. 2009)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-fami=
ly:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Out-of-state vendors, however, are
not.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i style=3D'mso-bidi-fon=
t-style:
normal'>Ibid.</i>; see </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3RF0000400"=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4TCJ-FMR0-TXFX-4226-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>City of New Y=
ork</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4TCJ-FMR0-TXFX-4226-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4TCJ-FMR0-TXFX-4226-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Smokes-Spirit=
s.com,
Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4TCJ-FMR0-TXFX-4226-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 541 F.3d 42=
5,
432-433 (CA2 2008)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Instead, the City is responsible f=
or
recovering, directly from the customers, use taxes on cigarettes sold outsi=
de
New York.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>That can be difficu=
lt,
&nbsp;[***949]&nbsp;as those customers are often reluctant to pay and tough=
 to
track down.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>One way the City =
can
gather information that would assist it in collecting the back taxes is thr=
ough
<a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc1_33"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN1_1_9"><=
/a>[1]
the Jenkins Act, ch. 699, 63 Stat. 884, as amended by 69 Stat. 627.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>That Act requires out-of-state cig=
arette
sellers to register and to file a report with state tobacco tax administrat=
ors
listing the name, address, and quantity of cigarettes purchased by state
residents.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>&nbsp;[****9]&nbsp=
;</span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:61XJ-4HH3-GXJ9-33PC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>15 U.S.C.
&sect;&sect; 375-378</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>New
York State and the City have executed an agreement under which both parties
undertake to &quot;cooperate fully with&nbsp;[*6]&nbsp; each other and keep
each other fully and promptly informed with reference to any person or
transaction subject to both State and City cigarette taxes including
[i]nformation obtained which may result in additional cigarette tax revenue=
 to
the State or City provided that the disclosure of that information is
permissible under existing laws and agreements.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Record A1003.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The City asserts that under that
agreement, the State forwards Jenkins Act information to the City.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'>Id.,</i>
at A998; Second Amended Compl. P 54.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>That information helps the City track down purchasers who do not pay
their taxes.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i style=3D'mso-=
bidi-font-style:
normal'>Id.</i>, PP 58-59. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Hemi
Group is a New Mexico company that sells cigarettes online.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Hemi, however, does not file Jenki=
ns Act
information with the State.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>T=
he
City alleges that this failure has cost it &quot;tens if not hundreds of
millions of dollars a year in cigarette excise tax revenue.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Record A996.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Based on Hemi's failure to file the
information with the State, the City filed this federal RICO claim. </span>=
</p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>B </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc2_33"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN2_1_9"></a>=
<span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>[2]<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>RICO provides a private cause of a=
ction
for &quot;[a]ny person injured in his &nbsp;[****10]&nbsp;business or prope=
rty
by reason of a violation of </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>section 1962<=
/span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> of
this chapter.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
1964(c)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Section 1962<=
/span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
in turn, contains RICO's criminal provisions.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Specifically, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
which the City invokes here, makes it &quot;unlawful for any person employe=
d by
or associated with any enterprise engaged in, or the activities of which
affect, interstate . . . commerce, to conduct or participate, directly or
indirectly, in the conduct of such enterprise's affairs through a pattern of
racketeering activity.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>&quot;[R]acketeering activity&quot; is defined to include a number of
so-called predicate acts, including the two at issue in this case--mail and
wire fraud.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>See </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1961(1=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
City alleges that Hemi's &quot;interstate sale of cigarettes and the failur=
e to
file Jenkins Act reports identifying those sales&quot; constitute the RICO
predicate offenses of mail and&nbsp;[*7]&nbsp; wire fraud in violation of <=
/span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
for which </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1964(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
provides a private cause of action.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>Record A980.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Invoking =
that
private cause of action, the&nbsp;[**988]&nbsp; City asserts that it has
suffered injury in the form of lost tax revenue--its &quot;business or
property&quot; in RICO terms--&quot;by reason of&quot; Hemi's fraud. </span=
></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Hemi
does not contest the City's characterization &nbsp;[****11]&nbsp;of the Jen=
kins
Act violations as predicate offenses actionable under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1964(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>(We therefore assume, without deci=
ding,
that failure to file Jenkins Act material can serve as a RICO predicate
offense.)<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Instead, Hemi argue=
s that
the City's asserted injury--lost tax revenue--is not &quot;business or
property&quot; under RICO, and that the City cannot show that it suffered a=
ny
injury &quot;by reason of&quot; the failure to file Jenkins Act reports. </=
span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6T28539VFP00002D6700017"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3SX0000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3T00000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>&nbsp;[***950]&nbsp;The District
Court dismissed the City's RICO claims, determining that Hemi owner and off=
icer
Kai Gachupin did not have an individual duty to file Jenkins Act reports, a=
nd
thus could not have committed the alleged predicate acts.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3RH0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4JGS-B9C0-TVW3-P2B5-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>City of New Y=
ork</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4JGS-B9C0-TVW3-P2B5-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4JGS-B9C0-TVW3-P2B5-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Nexicon, Inc.=
</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4JGS-B9C0-TVW3-P2B5-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, No. 03 CV 3=
83
(DAB), 2006 U.S. Dist. LEXIS 10295, 2006 WL 647716, *7-*8 (SDNY, Mar. 15, 2=
006)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The District Court therefore held =
that
the City could not establish that Hemi and Gachupin formed an
&quot;enterprise&quot; as required to establish RICO liability.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3SY0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4JGS-B9C0-TVW3-P2B5-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>2006 U.S. Dis=
t.
LEXIS 10295, [WL] at *7-*10</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times=
",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Because it dismissed on that groun=
d, the
District Court did not address whether the City's loss of tax revenue
constitutes an injury to its &quot;business or property&quot; under </span>=
<a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1964</=
span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
or whether that injury was caused &quot;by reason of&quot; Hemi's failure to
file the Jenkins Act reports. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3T20000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The &nbsp;[****12]&nbsp;Second
Circuit vacated the District Court's judgment and remanded for further
proceedings. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3TG0000400"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>The Court of Appeals held that the =
City
had established that Gachupin and Hemi operated as an &quot;enterprise&quot;
and that the enterprise committed the predicate RICO acts of mail and wire
fraud, based on the failure to file the Jenkins Act material with the
State.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3T10000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4TCJ-FMR0-TXFX-4226-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>541 F.3d at
447-448</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3TG0000400_2"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3TJ0000400"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>The court also determined that the =
City's
asserted injury, lost tax revenue, was &quot;business&nbsp;[*8]&nbsp; or
property&quot; under RICO.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></=
span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3TF0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4TCJ-FMR0-TXFX-4226-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id</span></i>=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4TCJ-FMR0-TXFX-4226-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>., at 444-445=
</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3TJ0000400_2"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>And that injury, the court conclude=
d,
came about &quot;by reason of&quot; the predicate mail and wire frauds.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3TH0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4TCJ-FMR0-TXFX-4226-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id</span></i>=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4TCJ-FMR0-TXFX-4226-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>., at 440-444=
</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3V00000400"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>The City thus had stated a viable R=
ICO
claim.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Judge Winter dissented=
 on
the ground that the alleged RICO violation was not the proximate cause of t=
he
