name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3WJ0000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>We explained that, <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc3_33"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN3_1_9"></a>=
[3] to
state a claim under civil RICO, the plaintiff is required to show that a RI=
CO
predicate offense &quot;not only was a 'but for' cause of his injury, but w=
as
the proximate cause as well.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; <=
/span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3W80000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
