",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Proximate cause for RICO purposes,=
 we
made clear, should be evaluated in light of its common-law foundations;
proximate cause thus requires &quot;some direct relation between the injury
asserted and the injurious conduct alleged.&quot;<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'>Ibid.</i><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>A link that is &quot;too remote,&q=
uot;
&quot;purely contingent,&quot; or &quot;indirec[t]&quot; is insufficient.<s=
pan
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ3WH0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id</span></i>=
