name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ48R0000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>It bears remembering what this c=
ase
is &nbsp;[****29]&nbsp;about.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span=
>It is
about the RICO liability of a company for lost taxes it had no obligation to
collect, remit, or pay, which harmed a party to whom it owed no duty.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>It is about imposing such liabilit=
y to
substitute for or complement a governing body's uncertain ability or desire=
 to
collect taxes directly from those who owe them.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>And it is about the fact that the
liability comes with treble damages and attorney's fees attached.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc7_=
27"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LEDHN7_1_8"></a>[7] This Court has interpreted RICO broadl=
y,
consistent with its terms, but we have also held that its reach is limited =
by
the &quot;requirement&nbsp;[*18]&nbsp; of a direct causal connection&quot;
between the predicate wrong and the harm.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&=
nbsp;
</span></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ48P0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4K41-DS80-004C-200J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Anza</span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4K41-DS80-004C-200J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 547 U.S., at
460, 126 S. Ct. 1991, 164 L. Ed. 2d 720</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-f=
amily:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The City's injuries here were not =
caused
directly by the alleged fraud, and thus were not caused &quot;by reason
of&quot; it.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The City, theref=
ore,
has no RICO claim. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
judgment of the Court of Appeals for the Second Circuit is reversed, and the
case is remanded for further proceedings consistent with this opinion. </sp=
an></p>

