k'>&nbsp;[*21]&nbsp;
B </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
case arises as a result of the District Court's dismissal of New York
City's&nbsp;[**996]&nbsp; RICO complaint. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6T2853DNP000002D6700035"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ4BB0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6CHH-WBV3-SCV7-1000-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Fed. Rule Civ.
Proc. 12(b)(6)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'>.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Hence we=
 must
answer the question in light of the facts alleged, taking as true the facts
pleaded in the complaint (along with the &quot;RICO statement&quot; submitt=
ed
pursuant to the District Court's rule).<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nb=
sp;
</span></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ4B90000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4SPS-PSH0-TXFX-12X7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Bridge</span>=
</i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4SPS-PSH0-TXFX-12X7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4SPS-PSH0-TXFX-12X7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Phoenix Bond
&amp; Indem. Co.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4SPS-PSH0-TXFX-12X7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 553 U.S. 63=
9,
642, n. 1, 128 S. Ct. 2131, 2135, 170 L. Ed. 2d 1012, 1017 (2008)</span></i=
></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>).<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Those facts (as I interpret them)
include the following: </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>1.
New York State (or State) and New York City (or City) both impose tobacco t=
axes
on New York cigarette buyers.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>Second Am. Compl. P 37. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>2.
Both City and State normally collect the taxes from in-state cigarette sell=
ers,
who, in turn, charge retail customers.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbs=
p;
</span><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.,</i> PP 4, 6. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>3.
Hemi, an out-of-state company, sells cigarettes over the Internet to in-sta=
te
buyers at prices that are lower than in-state cigarette prices.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>The difference in price is almost
entirely attributable to the fact that Hemi's prices do not include any cha=
rge
for New York taxes.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Hemi adve=
rtises
its cigarettes as &quot;tax free&quot; &nbsp;[***959]&nbsp;and often
&nbsp;[****35]&nbsp;adds that it &quot;does not report any sales activity to
any State taxing authority.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </=
span><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.,</i> PP 2, 6, 108b (internal quota=
tion
marks omitted; emphasis deleted). </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>4.
New York State normally receives Jenkins Act reports from out-of-state
sellers.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>It is contractually
obliged to pass the information on to New York City (and I assume it normal=
ly
does so).<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i style=3D'mso-bid=
i-font-style:
normal'>Id.,</i> PP 8-9, 11, 54-57. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>5.
When it receives Jenkins-Act-type information, New York City writes letters=
 to
resident customers asking them to pay the tobacco tax they owe.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>As a result, New York City collects
about 40% of the tax due.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>(By=
 doing
so, in 2005 the City obtained $400,000 out of $1 million owed.)<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'>Id.,</i>
PP 58-59. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal34 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>6.
Hemi has consistently and intentionally failed to file Jenkins Act reports =
in
order to prevent both State and&nbsp;[*22]&nbsp; City from collecting the
tobacco taxes that Hemi's in-state customers owe and which otherwise many of
those customers would pay.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.,</i> PP 13, 24, 58. </span></p>

