:contentItem:4SPS-PSH0-TXFX-12X7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 553 U.S., at
655-657, 128 S. Ct. 2131, 170 L. Ed. 2d 1012</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>But
where so much basic common law argues in favor of such a finding, how can t=
he
Court avoid that conclusion here? </span></p>

