5 L.
Ed. 2d, at 952</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'>.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>But how =
could
that be so?<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>New York State si=
gned a
contract promising to relay relevant information to the City.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>In respect to that relevant inform=
ation,
the State is a conduit, indeed roughly analogous to a postal employee.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>This Court has recognized specific=
ally
that &quot;under&nbsp;[**999]&nbsp; the common law a fraud may be establish=
ed
when the defendant has made use of a third party to reach the target of the
fraud.&quot;<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4YD38400K1MNJ4CH0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-H630-003B-44TP-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
