k'>
(FHA or Act). The FHA prohibits, among other things, racial discrimination =
in
connection with real-estate transactions, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SHT-0722-D6RV-H1F9-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>42 U. S. C.
&sect;&sect;3604(b)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SHT-0722-D6RV-H1FB-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>3605(a)</span=
></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
and permits any &#8220;aggrieved person&#8221; to file a civil damages acti=
on
for a violation of the Act, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SHT-0722-D6RV-H1FN-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect;&sect;3=
613(a)(1)(A)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SHT-0722-D6RV-H1FN-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>(c)(1)</span>=
</i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
The City's complaints charge that the Banks intentionally targeted predatory
practices at African-American and Latino neighborhoods and residents, lendi=
ng
to minority borrowers on worse terms than equally creditworthy nonminority
borrowers and inducing defaults by failing to extend refinancing and loan
modifications to minority borrowers on fair terms. The City alleges that the
Banks' discriminatory conduct led to a disproportionate number of foreclosu=
res
and vacancies in majority-minority neighborhoods, which impaired the City's
effort to assure racial integration, diminished the City's property-tax
revenue, and increased demand for police, fire, and other municipal service=
s.
The District Court dismissed the complaints on the grounds&nbsp;[***2]&nbsp=
; that
(1) the harms alleged fell outside the zone of interests the FHA protects a=
nd
(2) the complaints failed to show a sufficient causal connection between the
City's injuries and the Banks' discriminatory conduct. The Eleventh Circuit
reversed.</span></p>

