<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc1_36"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",s=
erif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Racketeer
Influenced and Corrupt Organizations Act (RICO)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
creates a cause of action for &#8220;[a]ny person injured in his business or
property.&#8221; </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U. S. C.
&sect;1964(c)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fa=
reast-font-family:
Times;color:black'>. We must decide whether the statute, by implicitly deny=
ing
a remedy for <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>personal</i> injuries,=
 also
denies a remedy for business and property loss that derives from a personal
injury. It does not.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;
color:black'>&nbsp;[*597]&nbsp; I</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>A</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
2012, Douglas Horn was working as a commercial truck driver when he crashed=
 his
truck and injured his back and shoulder. Months later, he was still sufferi=
ng
from chronic pain, and neither physical therapy nor traditional medicine
provided relief. While searching for a natural alternative, Horn came across
&#8220;Dixie X,&#8221; a tincture infused with cannabidiol&#8212;more commo=
nly
known as CBD&#8212;sold &nbsp;[***482]&nbsp; by Medical Marijuana, Inc. </s=
pan><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn424' href=3D"#_ftn424" name=3D"_ftnref424" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>1</span><=
/sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
CBD, like its cannabis &#8220;cousin&#8221; tetrahydrocannabinol (THC), is a
naturally occurring chemical compound found in the cannabis plant. Only THC,
however, has the mind-altering properties associated with marijuana. </span=
><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn425' href=3D"#_ftn425" name=3D"_ftnref425" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>2</span><=
/sup></a></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Because
a positive drug test could cost him his job, Horn was wary of any product t=
hat
might contain THC. But Dixie X seemed safe. It was described as a
&#8220;CBD-rich,&#8221; non-psychoactive medicine that is &#8220;0% THC.&#8=
221;
App. 19. Medical Marijuana&#8217;s online FAQ page&nbsp;[****8]&nbsp; promi=
sed
that Dixie X was &#8220;legal to consume both here in the U.S. and in many
countries abroad.&#8221; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i>, a=
t 40.
Additional research, including a call to a customer-service representative,
reinforced those representations. Satisfied that &nbsp;[**937]&nbsp; Dixie X
was THC-free, Horn bought a bottle and gave it a try.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>A
few weeks later, Horn&#8217;s employer selected him for a random drug
screening. To his surprise, the test detected THC in his system. After Horn
refused to complete a substance-abuse program&#8212;in his view, doing so w=
ould
constitute &#8220;an admission to doing drugs,&#8221; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-=
font-style:
normal'>id.</i>, at 91-92&#8212;his employer fired &nbsp;[*598]&nbsp; him. =
Horn
then ordered another bottle of Dixie X and sent it to a third-party lab for
testing. This test also came back positive for THC. In fact, the lab refuse=
d to
mail the sample back to him, fearing that doing so would violate federal la=
w.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF82D6P140020000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Horn sued Medical Marijuana in
Federal District Court, raising a civil RICO claim (as well as a host of
state-law claims not relevant here). See </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U. S. C.
&sect;1964(c)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fa=
reast-font-family:
Times;color:black'>. He alleged that Medical Marijuana was a RICO
&#8220;&#8216;enterprise&#8217;&#8221; engaged in marketing, distributing, =
and
selling Dixie X. </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect;1961(4)=
</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>;
see </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF82D6P140010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Turkette</spa=
n></i></a><a
