<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF82D6P140040000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF92D6P190010000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The District Court granted summa=
ry
judgment to Medical Marijuana&nbsp;[****9]&nbsp; on the RICO claim. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF92D6P190030000400"></a>According to the court,
Horn&#8217;s lost employment &#8220;flow[ed] from, and [was] derivative of,=
 a
personal injury he suffered&#8221;&#8212;the introduction of THC &#8220;into
his system through the ingestion of Dixie X.&#8221; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF82D6P140030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:63M3-2N21-F27X-6549-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>2021 U.S. Dis=
t.
LEXIS 174740, 2021 WL 4173195, *2, *5 (WDNY, Sept. 14, 2021)</span></i></a>=
<span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Yet RICO&#8217;s civil cause of action, the court stressed, is available on=
ly
to a &#8220;&#8216;person injured in his <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'>business</i>
or <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>property</i>.&#8217;&#8221; </sp=
an><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF82D6P140050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:63M3-2N21-F27X-6549-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>2021 U.S. Dis=
t.
LEXIS 174740, [WL], at *2</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",=
serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (emphasis added). <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF92D6P190030000400_2"></a>Because a plaintiff cannot
recover for a <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>personal</i> injury, =
it
reasoned, neither can he recover for a business or property harm that resul=
ts
from a personal injury. </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF92D6P190020000400=
"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:63M3-2N21-F27X-6549-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>2021 U.S. Dis=
t.
LEXIS 174740, [WL], at *5</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",=
serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. So for Horn, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect;1964(c)=
</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
offered no path to relief.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[***483]&nbsp;
<a name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF92D6P190050000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF92SF7SC0020000400"></a>The Second Circuit reversed.=
 </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF92D6P190040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:690H-9651-JXNB-60B0-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>80 F. 4th 130
(2023)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-f=
ont-family:
Times;color:black'>. It began by analyzing an issue that neither the Distri=
ct
Court nor the parties had addressed: whether the term &#8220;business&#8221=
; in
</span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect;1964(c)=
</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
encompasses not only a &#8220;&#8216;commercial or industrial establishment=
 or
enterprise,&#8217;&#8221; but also an individual&#8217;s &nbsp;[*599]&nbsp;
&#8220;&#8216;employment.&#8217;&#8221; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF92SF7SC0010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:690H-9651-JXNB-60B0-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:690H-9651-JXNB-60B0-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 135-136<=
/span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Adopting the broad definition, the Second Circuit concluded that Horn had b=
een
&#8220;&#8216;injured in his business&#8217;&#8221; when he lost his job. <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Ibid</i>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF92SF7SC0040000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF92SF7SD0010000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>It then turned to the District
Court&#8217;s holding that a plaintiff like Horn cannot recover for a busin=
ess
or property harm that flows from an &#8220;antecedent personal injury.&#822=
1; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF92SF7SC0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:690H-9651-JXNB-60B0-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
