if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:690H-9651-JXNB-60B0-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 137</spa=
n></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF92SF7SD0030000400"></a>Horn insisted that any
personal-injury bar was inapplicable&nbsp;[****10]&nbsp; because the court =
had
mischaracterized his &#8220;unwitting ingestion of THC&#8221; as a
&#8220;personal injury&#8221; from which his lost employment derived. </spa=
n><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYF92SF7SC0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:690H-9651-JXNB-60B0-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
