mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Alvarez-Macha=
in</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4CRG-3TY0-004C-000F-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 542 U. S. 6=
92,
711, n. 9, 124 S. Ct. 2739, 159 L. Ed. 2d 718 (2004)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>).
According to Medical Marijuana, &#8220;damage[s]&#8221; refers to the
&#8220;loss, hurt or harm&#8221; resulting from the RICO violation.
Ballentine&#8217;s Law Dictionary, at 303. So &#8220;injured&#8221; must me=
an
something else&#8212;namely, &#8220;having suffered an invasion of a legal
right.&#8221; See Brief for Petitioners 15.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFC2N1RM50050000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Once again, Medical Marijuana ed=
its
the statute to make its point. Much as it treats &#8220;injured&#8221; as
interchangeable with &#8220;injury,&#8221; it treats &#8220;damages&#8221; =
as
interchangeable with &nbsp;[*604]&nbsp; &#8220;damage.&#8221; Yet the
distinction matters, because <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc6_31"></a>&#82=
20;damages&#8221;
has a specialized legal meaning referring&nbsp;[****15]&nbsp; to monetary
redress. See Ballentine&#8217;s Law Dictionary, at 303; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFC2N1RM50040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-JVV0-003B-S0YJ-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>American
Stevedores, Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-JVV0-003B-S0YJ-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-JVV0-003B-S0YJ-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Porello</span=
></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-JVV0-003B-S0YJ-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 330 U. S. 4=
46,
450, n. 6, 67 S. Ct. 847, 91 L. Ed. 1011 (1947)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Section 1964(=
c)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> is
best read as using &#8220;damages&#8221; in precisely this way. By allowing=
 a
plaintiff to recover &#8220;threefold the damages he sustains,&#8221; the
statute allows a plaintiff to recover triple the amount that makes him whol=
e. </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect;1964(c)=
</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
And if &#8220;damages&#8221; refers to &#8220;monetary redress,&#8221; it
obviously means something different from &#8220;hurt or harmed.&#8221; Givi=
ng
&#8220;injured&#8221; its ordinary meaning, therefore, is perfectly consist=
ent
with the meaningful-variation canon. Besides, Medical Marijuana&#8217;s
preferred definition of &#8220;damages&#8221; is untenable. Under it, the
statute would allow a plaintiff to recover &#8220;threefold the loss, hurt,=
 or
harm he sustains.&#8221; That makes little sense.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
