mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 327 Conn. 5=
40,
564-568, 175 A. 3d 1, 15-17 (2018)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family=
:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. Does disclosure implicate a
privacy interest? If so, does violating that interest constitute a
&#8220;personal injury&#8221;? Or does disclosure implicate a property inte=
rest
in one&#8217;s medical information?</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFH2D6MTD0050000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Relying on state law would also
create choice-of-law questions. Many &nbsp;[***491]&nbsp; RICO enterprises
transcend the boundaries of a single jurisdiction. See </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PY-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U. S. C.
&sect;1965(a)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fa=
reast-font-family:
Times;color:black'> (establishing venue in &#8220;any district&#8221; in wh=
ich
the defendant &#8220;resides, is found, has an agent, or transacts his
affairs&#8221;); see also </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFH2D6MTD00400004=
00"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-H530-003B-44MW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Agency Holding
Corp.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-H530-003B-44MW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-H530-003B-44MW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Malley-Duff &=
amp;
Associates, Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-H530-003B-44MW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 483 U. S. 1=
43,
154, 107 S. Ct. 2759, 97 L. Ed. 2d 121 (1987)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(&#8220;[P]redicate acts will often occur in several States&#8221;). Which
jurisdiction must supply the necessary tort-law analogue? Is it where the
plaintiff felt her injury? Where the defendant engaged in the racketeering
&nbsp;[**945]&nbsp; activity? Where the majority of the enterprise resides?=
</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFH2HM63F0020000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The third source on Medical
Marijuana&#8217;s list&#8212;general tort law&#8212;avoids the choice-of-law
concern but has&nbsp;[****22]&nbsp; theoretical problems of its own. For on=
e,
like state tort law, general tort law does not always clearly distinguish
between &#8220;business,&#8221; &#8220;personal,&#8221; and
&#8220;property&#8221; torts. For another, general tort law is neither stat=
ic
nor uniform. See </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFH2HM63F0010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5VNW-V971-JKPJ-G4DY-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Air &amp; Liq=
uid
Systems Corp.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5VNW-V971-JKPJ-G4DY-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> v. </span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5VNW-V971-JKPJ-G4DY-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>DeVries</span=
></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5VNW-V971-JKPJ-G4DY-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 586 U. S. 4=
46,
453, 139 S. Ct. 986, 203 L. Ed. 2d 373 (2019)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(observing that &#8220;the federal and state courts ha[d] not reached conse=
nsus
on how to apply&#8221; a particular principle of &nbsp;[*612]&nbsp; general
tort law). When a majority rule does not exist, when the law is unsettled, =
or
when there is no analogous tort, deferring to general tort principles is
difficult, to say the least.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>***</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Medical
Marijuana tries valiantly to engineer a rule that yields its preferred
outcomes. (Civil RICO should permit suit against Tony Soprano, but not agai=
nst
an ordinary tortfeasor.) But its textual hook&#8212;the word
&#8220;injured&#8221;&#8212;does not give it enough to go on. When all is s=
aid
and done, Medical Marijuana is left fighting the most natural interpretatio=
n of
the text&#8212;that &#8220;injured&#8221; means &#8220;harmed&#8221;&#8212;=
with
no plausible alternative in hand. That is a battle it cannot win.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>III</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFH2HM63F0040000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Medical Marijuana, together with=
 the
principal dissent, warn that the Second Circuit&#8217;s rule will eviscerate
RICO&#8217;s &#8220;business or property&#8221; limitation. See <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFH2HM63F0030000400"></a><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-st=
yle:
normal'>post</i>, at 635 (opinion of <span style=3D'font-variant:small-caps=
'>Kavanaugh,
J.&nbsp;[****23]&nbsp;</span>). In their view, a plaintiff can characterize=
 any
economic harm flowing from a personal injury as a harm to his business or
property. Hence, they say, plaintiffs can easily transform garden-variety
personal-injury claims into RICO suits for treble damages. While we underst=
and
the concern, Medical Marijuana and the dissent understate other constraints=
 on
civil RICO claims.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFH2N1RNF0010000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFH2N1RNF0030000400"></a><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-st=
yle:
normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Ti=
mes;
color:black'>First</span></i><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'> and foremost is RICO&#8217;s direct-relationship
requirement. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFH2N1RNF0050000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc8_27"></a>Time and again, we have reiterated t=
hat </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect;1964(c)=
</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&#8217;s
&#8220;by reason of &#8221; language demands &#8220;some direct relation
between the injury asserted and the injurious conduct alleged.&#8221; </spa=
n><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFH2HM63F0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Holmes</span>=
</i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 503 U. S., =
at
268, 112 S. Ct. 1311, 117 L. Ed. 2d 532</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-f=
amily:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. The key word is
&#8220;direct&#8221;; foreseeability does not cut it. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFH2N1RNF0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:7XMP-8RB0-YB0V-912G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Hemi Group</s=
pan></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:7XMP-8RB0-YB0V-912G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 559 U. S., =
at
12, 130 S. Ct. 983, 175 L. Ed. 2d 943</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-fam=
ily:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFH2N1RNF0050000400_2"></a>Rather, whenever the plain=
tiff
&#8217;s theory of causation requires moving &#8220;well beyond the first
step,&#8221; it &#8220;cannot meet RICO&#8217;s direct relationship
requirement.&#8221; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFH2N1RNF0040000400"></=
a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:7XMP-8RB0-YB0V-912G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
