<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_II08GRN6YPH8003RRRM1000V1"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFN2N1RP20010000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Moreover, it is
not&nbsp;[****32]&nbsp; clear to me that Medical Marijuana is even entitled=
 to
argue that Horn suffered a personal injury. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_II08GRN6YPH8003RRRM1000VK"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFN2N1RP20030000400"></a>The rule of judicial estoppel
&#8220;&#8216;generally prevents a party from prevailing in one phase of a =
case
on an argument and then relying on a contradictory argument to prevail in
another phase.&#8217;&#8221; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFM2D6MV300500=
00400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4354-R7T0-004B-Y04P-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>New Hampshire=
</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4354-R7T0-004B-Y04P-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
