<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
question presented is also bound up with a related question&#8212;that is, =
the
definition of the phrase &nbsp;[***497]&nbsp; &#8220;injured in his busines=
s or
property&#8221; in civil RICO. </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect;1964(c)=
</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
To understand whether Horn&#8217;s civil RICO claim is based on an
&#8220;injur[y] in his business or property,&#8221; it would be helpful to
understand the meaning of that phrase in the civil RICO statute. <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Ibid.</i> But, I would not decide that
weighty question here because the court below did not do so, and neither pa=
rty
offers a complete definition of the phrase.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_II08GRN6YPH8003RRRM1000V0"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFN2N1RP20050000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_II08GRN6YPH8003RRRM1000TY"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFN28T42F0020000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The Second Circuit did not decide
the meaning of &#8220;injured in his business or property.&#8221; <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Ibid.</i> In its view, &#8220;[b]y usi=
ng the
disjunctive &#8216;or&#8217; to separate &#8216;business&#8217; from
&#8216;property,&#8217; &nbsp;[*621]&nbsp; Congress&nbsp;[****34]&nbsp; made
clear that &#8216;business&#8217; was not intended to modify &#8216;propert=
y,&#8217;
nor was &#8216;property&#8217; intended to modify
&#8216;business.&#8217;&#8221; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFN2N1RP20040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:690H-9651-JXNB-60B0-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>80 F. 4th, at
135-136</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>. Thus, the Second Circuit evaluated the meaning of
&#8220;business&#8221; without considering the meaning of
&#8220;property.&#8221; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFN28T42F0010000400=
"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:690H-9651-JXNB-60B0-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:690H-9651-JXNB-60B0-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, at 136</spa=
n></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Similarly,
neither party offers a complete definition of &#8220;injured in his busines=
s or
property.&#8221; </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect;1964(c)=
</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Horn argues that an injury to &#8220;business&#8221; is any harm to one&#82=
17;s
employment, and employment, in Horn&#8217;s view, &#8220;embraces everything
about which a person can be employed.&#8221; Brief for Respondent 12 (inter=
nal
quotation marks omitted). But, Horn says little about what it means to be
&#8220;injured in his . . . property.&#8221; </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect;1964(c)=
</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Medical Marijuana, for its part, argues that an injury to business or prope=
rty
is the invasion of a legal right that one holds in his business or property.
Brief for Petitioners 11. But, nowhere does Medical Marijuana tell us exact=
ly
how it would define those legal rights. At times it has suggested that cour=
ts
should look to state tort law, but, it says little about how courts should
assess whether the plaintiff has suffered a qualifying tort. Given the stat=
e of
the briefing on this matter, we are not well positioned to decide the meani=
ng
of &#8220;injured in his business or property&#8221; in this case. </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect;1964(c)=
</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_II08GRN6YPH8003RRRM1000TX"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFN28T42F0040000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_II08GRN6YPH8003RRRM1000TW"></a><a
