<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>What
constitutes injury as a matter of traditional tort law?&nbsp;[****43]&nbsp;=
 For
tort-law purposes, injury is the infringement of a legal right&#8212;&#8220=
;the
invasion of any legally protected interest of another.&#8221; <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Restatement (Second) of Torts &sect;7(=
1)</i>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_II08GRN6YPH8003RRRM1000W8"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFS2SF7WM0050000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>And with injury so defined,
Congress&#8217;s &#8220;cabining RICO&#8217;s private cause of action to
particular kinds of &nbsp;[***502]&nbsp; injury&#8221;&#8212;business or
property injuries, not personal injuries&#8212;makes perfect sense. </span>=
<a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6FGFYFS2SF7WM0040000400"></a><a
