:contentItem:5K27-42B1-F04K-F1B2-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 579 U. S. 3=
25,
350, 136 S. Ct. 2090, 195 L. Ed. 2d 476 (2016)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
That is because tort law has long categorized different kinds of legal inju=
ries
along precisely those lines.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Personal
injury includes &#8220;acts constituting a tort because intended or likely =
to
cause bodily harm or emotional distress.&#8221; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-s=
tyle:
normal'>Restatement (Second) of Torts &sect;924, Comment a</i> (1977); see =
<i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>id.</i>, <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-sty=
le:normal'>ch.
2, Introductory Note, at 22</i>; Ballentine&#8217;s Law Dictionary 941 (3d =
ed.
1969). Typical personal-injury &nbsp;[*629]&nbsp; claims may involve, for
example, car accidents or defective products.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal37 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
