<p class=3DNormal38 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>I. <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Stating a Claim -- the Governing Law</=
i></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal38 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>A.
Required Allegations and the Standard of Review</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal38 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J4X0030000400"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFc=
lscc1_37"></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
Federal Rules of Civil Procedure require that a claim for relief contain
&quot;a short and plain statement of the claim showing that the pleader is
entitled to relief.&quot; </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5GYC-1WP1-6N19-F0YK-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Fed. R. Civ. =
P.
8(a)(2)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J4X0050000400"></a>A
complaint may be dismissed to the extent that it &quot;fail[s] to state a c=
laim
upon which relief can be granted.&quot; </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6CHH-WBV3-SCV7-1000-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Fed. R. Civ. =
P.
12(b)(6)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast=
-font-family:
Times;color:black'>. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J4Y0040000400"></a>This=
 Court
reviews such a dismissal <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>de novo. S=
ee </i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J4X0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-2X90-006F-M37T-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Bernheim v. L=
itt</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-2X90-006F-M37T-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 79 F.3d 318,
321 (2d Cir. 1996)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (citation omitted). <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J4Y0040000400_2"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J4X0050000400_2"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J500030000400"></a>In doing so, we are constrai=
ned to
&quot;'accept[] &nbsp;[*111]&nbsp; all factual allegations as true, and dra=
w[]
all reasonable inferences in the plaintiff's favor.'&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J4X0040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4X0G-STX0-TXFX-41XG-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Shomo v. City=
 of
New York</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4X0G-STX0-TXFX-41XG-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 579 F.3d 17=
6,
183 (2d Cir. 2009)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (quoting </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J4Y0010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:456H-9WR0-0038-X4H7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Chambers v. T=
ime
Warner, Inc</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:456H-9WR0-0038-X4H7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>., 282 F.3d 1=
47,
152 (2d Cir. 2002))</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J500030000400_2"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J500050000400"></a>We are also constrained, how=
ever,
to ascertain that the complaint &quot;contain sufficient factual matter,
&nbsp;[**16]&nbsp;accepted as true, to 'state a claim to relief that is
plausible on its face.'&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J4Y0030=
000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4W9Y-4KS0-TXFX-1325-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Ashcroft v. I=
qbal</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4W9Y-4KS0-TXFX-1325-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 129 S. Ct.
1937, 1949, 173 L. Ed. 2d 868 (2009)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-fami=
ly:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (quoting </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J4Y0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NSN-8840-004C-002M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Bell Atl. Cor=
p.
v. Twombly</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4NSN-8840-004C-002M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 550 U.S. 54=
4,
570, 127 S. Ct. 1955, 167 L. Ed. 2d 929 (2007))</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J500050000400_2"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J500030000400_3"></a>In other words, a complain=
t is
not required to have &quot;detailed factual allegations, but it demands more
than an unadorned, the defendant-unlawfully-harmed-me accusation.&quot; </s=
pan><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J500020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4W9Y-4KS0-TXFX-1325-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id</span></i>=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4W9Y-4KS0-TXFX-1325-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>. at 1949</sp=
an></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(internal quotation marks omitted). In its formulation of the <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Twombly-Iqbal</i> requirements for a
statement of claim, the Supreme Court has established the following order t=
o be
followed in determining whether the pleading is adequate: &quot;When there =
are
well-pleaded factual allegations, a court should assume their veracity and =
<i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>then</i> determine whether they plausi=
bly
give rise to an entitlement to relief.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J500040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4W9Y-4KS0-TXFX-1325-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id</span></i>=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4W9Y-4KS0-TXFX-1325-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>. at 1950</sp=
an></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(emphasis supplied).</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal38 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>B.
Consideration of Matters Extraneous to the Complaint</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal38 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3M0K9J510020000400"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFc=
lscc2_37"></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
considering a motion to dismiss for failure to state a claim pursuant to </=
span><a
