<p class=3DNormal38 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>DiFolco's
complaint on its face clearly alleges a breach of her employment contract w=
ith
MSNBC. In brief, she alleges that she was subjected to intolerable working
conditions and that she was fired when she complained about the conditions.=
 <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3N0K9J540020000400"></a>She also asserts that defend=
ants
improperly interpreted certain of her e-mails as notices of resignation. The
District Court referred to e-mails from DiFolco that were said to be
incorporated by reference in the complaint in concluding that &nbsp;[**18]&=
nbsp;DiFolco
did indeed repudiate her contract by resignation and therefore that the
complaint failed to state a claim upon which relief could be granted. The
District Court referred to those e-mails dated August 23 and August 31 in
arriving at a conclusion that &quot;[b]oth of these e-mails from Plaintiff
constituted repudiation of the Contract and relieved MSNBC of future
obligations.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I51BFP3N0K9J540010000400"></a=
><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4ND7-5XY0-TVW3-P2DM-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>DiFolco</span=
></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4ND7-5XY0-TVW3-P2DM-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 2007 U.S. D=
ist.
LEXIS 23440, 2007 WL 959085, at *3</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family=
:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal38 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
