:contentItem:3S4X-0560-008H-V1D7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
 v.
Crockett</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-0560-008H-V1D7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 979 F.2d 12=
04,
1209 (7th Cir. 1992)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (quoting </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG780N0BD40050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-H480-008H-V1HX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Glecier</span=
></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-H480-008H-V1HX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 923 F.2d at=
 501</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>)).</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal39 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I82R1BM8CN1000077XR0000G"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I82R1BM8HC7000077XR0000H"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BD50030000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I82R1BM8SV8000077XR0000K"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I82R1BM8Y9Y000077XR0000M"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I82R1BM934G000077XR0000N"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I82R1BM9BGS000077XR0000R"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I82R1BM96TP000077XR0000P"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I82R1BM8N3P000077XR0000J"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BD60020000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc11_23"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",=
serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Because a RICO conspiracy charge
need not specify the predicate or racketeering acts that the defendants agr=
eed
would be committed, </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BD50020000400"></=
a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RHK-1090-004C-300F-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Salinas</span=
></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RHK-1090-004C-300F-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 522 U.S. at=
 64</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(&quot;The RICO conspiracy statute broadened conspiracy coverage by omitting
&nbsp;[**60]&nbsp;the requirement of an overt act.&quot; (internal citation
omitted)); </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BD50040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4TCG-2PS0-TX4N-G13C-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Yannotti</spa=
n></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4TCG-2PS0-TX4N-G13C-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 541 F.3d at=
 129</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(stating that &quot;to secure [defendant's] conviction for RICO conspiracy,=
 the
government was not required to prove the <u>actual</u> commission of a sing=
le
predicate act by [defendant] or any other conspirator&quot; (emphasis in
original)), it is sufficient to allege and prove that the defendants agreed=
 to
the commission of multiple violations of a specific statutory provision tha=
t qualifies
as RICO racketeering activity. <u>See </u></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BD60010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-H480-008H-V1HX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Glecier</span=
></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-H480-008H-V1HX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 923 F.2d at
499-500</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>; <u>see also </u></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BD60030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-0560-008H-V1D7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Crockett</spa=
n></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-0560-008H-V1D7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 979 F.2d at
1209 n.3</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast=
-font-family:
Times;color:black'> (concluding that the indictment contained sufficient
information to fall well within the boundary for RICO conspiracy where that
indictment &quot;alleged acts of violence carried out during a specific per=
iod
of time for specific purposes in furtherance of the delineated activities o=
f a
RICO enterprise&quot;) (citing </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BD60050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CDV0-003B-51C8-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
 v.
Phillips</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CDV0-003B-51C8-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 874 F.2d 12=
3,
130 (3d Cir. 1989)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (holding that where RICO conspi=
racy
count generally identified racketeering acts as acts of bribery and extorti=
on,
the government &quot;can rely on any act of bribery and extortion, so long =
as
that act occurred within the time frame of the conspiracy and was establish=
ed
&nbsp;[**61]&nbsp;by proof[] at the trial&quot;); </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BD70020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4W-YR10-0039-W3BD-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
