href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dadministrative-cod=
es&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:4NS7-4070-006W-83X3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Amendments to=
 the
Sentencing Guidelines for United States Courts, 72 Fed. Reg. 28571-28573</s=
pan></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
The Sentencing Commission later designated the crack-cocaine amendment as o=
ne
that may be applied retroactively, effective March 3, 2008. U.S.S.G. Supp. =
to
App. C, amend. 713 (2009); </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6FVK-4P43-S3SM-S1J2-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>U.S.S.G. &sec=
t;
1B1.10(c)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareas=
t-font-family:
Times;color:black'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal39 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BDG0020000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>In this case, Gregory Thomas was
convicted and sentenced for an offense involving crack-cocaine. The parties
submitted their sentencing memoranda to the district court, and the district
court sentenced Thomas, prior to the amendments and prior to the Supreme
Court's decision &nbsp;[**66]&nbsp;in </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BDG0010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4RB0-9510-TXFX-12KY-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Kimbrough v.
United States</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4RB0-9510-TXFX-12KY-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 552 U.S. 85,
128 S. Ct. 558, 169 L. Ed. 2d 481 (2007)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-=
family:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, in which the Cou=
rt
held that a sentencing judge may consider the disparity between the
Guidelines's treatment of crack- and powder-cocaine offenses. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BDG0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4RB0-9510-TXFX-12KY-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>128 S. Ct. at=
 575</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal39 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
record demonstrates that Thomas has preserved his claim that the applicatio=
n of
the Sentencing Guidelines's powder-crack disparity would result in a senten=
ce
greater than necessary to achieve the sentencing objectives in </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8TV4-SKM2-8T6X-72T1-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 3553(a=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
In his April 23, 2007 sentencing memorandum submitted to the district court,
Thomas specifically argued, inter alia, that he was, for purposes of
sentencing, subject to &quot;high exposure . . . due to the scoring of over=
 1.5
kilograms of crack cocaine.&quot; Thomas claimed that &quot;[t]his penalty =
is
grossly disproportionate to the offenses&quot; of which he had been convict=
ed,
and he noted that the Guideline ratio of 100 to 1 between crack and cocaine=
 had
been &quot;the subject of criticism by courts, legal commentators and the
Sentencing Commission on the grounds that the disparity lacks any persuasive
penal or scientific justification, and it has a racially disparate impact in
federal sentencing.&quot; Thomas further argued that the &quot;legislative
history . . . contains &nbsp;[**67]&nbsp;no rationale for the 100:1 ratio, =
and
the Sentencing Commission has studied the issue in depth since and found no
data to support Congress'[s] assumptions in passing the legislation.&quot;
Thomas accordingly urged the district court to impose a non-Guidelines sent=
ence
or in the alternative to grant him a downward departure from the Guidelines=
.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal39 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[*84]&nbsp;
<a name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BDJ0010000400"></a>At the May 23, 2007 sente=
ncing
hearing for Thomas, his counsel again raised the issue of the crack and pow=
der
cocaine disparity and noted the Sentencing Commission's then-ongoing review=
 of
the &quot;crack versus powder differential.&quot; Specifically, counsel sta=
ted
that the &quot;new Commission Guidelines . . . will affect [Thomas's]
calculations if the court adheres strictly to a Guidelines determination.&q=
uot;
In response, the district court stated: &quot;Well, this, I know there's a =
lot
of talk about the discrepancy between cocaine versus &#8212; cocaine powder
versus crack, and at this point in time, though, the law has not changed. So
you may have an exception there also.&quot; The district court went on to
impose a term of imprisonment of 360 months, a term of supervised release o=
f 5
years, and a special assessment of $100. For its part, the government's
sentencing memorandum &nbsp;[**68]&nbsp;submitted in the district court cit=
ed
to </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BDG0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4KNN-BD20-0038-X3D2-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
 v.
Castillo</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4KNN-BD20-0038-X3D2-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 460 F.3d 33=
7,
361 (2d Cir. 2006)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, for the general proposition th=
at a
district court may not deviate from a Guidelines sentence based upon a poli=
cy
disagreement with the disparity between the Guidelines; however, the govern=
ment
did not discuss in its sentencing memorandum the disparate treatment of cra=
ck
versus powder cocaine offenses.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal39 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BDJ0030000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BDM0020000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Although Thomas did not move in =
the
district court, pursuant to </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8TV4-SJH2-D6RV-H3S9-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
3582(c)(2)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-farea=
st-font-family:
Times;color:black'>, for a sentencing reduction based upon the crack-cocaine
amendment, at the time of Thomas's sentencing, on May 23, 2007, the law of =
this
Circuit &quot;did not acknowledge a district court's so-called 'variance
discretion' with respect to whether&quot; the 100-to-1 crack-powder ratio
&quot;results in an unfair measure of the seriousness of the offense.&quot;=
 </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BDJ0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4T70-C2D0-TX4N-G0BN-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
 v.
Keller</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4T70-C2D0-TX4N-G0BN-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 539 F.3d 97=
, 99
(2d Cir. 2008)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'>; <u>see </u></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BDJ0040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4KNN-BD20-0038-X3D2-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Castillo</spa=
n></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4KNN-BD20-0038-X3D2-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 460 F.3d at=
 361</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(holding that district court erred when it substituted its own crack-powder
ratio for the ratio set forth in the Guidelines). <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I82R1BM9W4V000077XR0000W"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BDM0040000400"></a>Moreover, because the record=
 does
not &quot;unambiguously demonstrate&quot; that the district court was aware=
 of
its discretion to vary from the Guidelines if it found &nbsp;[**69]&nbsp;th=
at
the disparity in the crack-powder ratio resulted in a greater sentence than
necessary, remand is appropriate. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG7B0N0BDP0010000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BDM0010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4T70-C2D0-TX4N-G0BN-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Keller</span>=
</i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4T70-C2D0-TX4N-G0BN-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 539 F.3d at
101-02</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-f=
ont-family:
Times;color:black'>. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG7B0N0BDP0010000400_2"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BDM0040000400_2"></a>Because the record also cl=
early
demonstrates that Thomas preserved this issue by raising it in his sentenci=
ng
memorandum and at the sentencing hearing, we remand to the district court f=
or
plenary resentencing consistent with </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BDM0040000400_3"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BDM0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4RB0-9510-TXFX-12KY-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Kimbrough</sp=
an></i></a><u><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
United States v. Jones</span></u><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG790N0BDM0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4SV1-1VB0-TXFX-41VW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>531 F.3d 163,
180-83 (2d Cir. 2008)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",seri=
f;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>; <u>cf. </u></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52FCG7B0N0BDP0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4S07-F370-TXFX-43D5-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
 v.
Regalado</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4S07-F370-TXFX-43D5-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 518 F.3d 143
(2d Cir. 2008)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'> (remanding, under plain error review, to the district c=
ourt
to allow the court to determine whether resentencing was required where the
defendant failed to preserve an argument that the district court should have
exercised its authority under 3553(a) to consider the disparity between the
crack and powder-cocaine Guidelines).</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal39 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>We
have considered all of appellants' remaining arguments and find them to be
without merit.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal39 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>CONCLUSION</span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal39 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
