113,
117, 559 N.Y.S.2d 704 (N.Y., 1st Dept. 1990)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4XFDYHJ0K1MNJ1440000400"></a>&quot;To prevail on a claim =
for
unjust enrichment in New York, a plaintiff must establish (1) that the
defendant benefitted; (2) at the plaintiff's expense; &nbsp;[**24]&nbsp;and=
 (3)
that equity and good conscience require restitution.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4XFDYHJ0K1MNJ13N0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3YG9-B2K0-0038-X4CT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
