<p class=3DNormal41 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",=
serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Interstate Commerce</span></i></=
p>

<p class=3DNormal41 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4XFDYHJ0K1MNJ1MF0000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Klotsman defendants' contention =
that
plaintiff's RICO claims fail because the Amended Complaint lacks specificity
concerning the effect of the enterprise on interstate commerce is similarly
without merit. <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc27_3"></a>Only a &quot;<u>de
minimis</u>&quot; effect on interstate commerce need be shown. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4XFDYHJ0K1MNJ1MK0000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4XFDYHJ0K1MNJ1M70000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4TMC-HT30-TX4N-G0JT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
 v.
Mejia</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4TMC-HT30-TX4N-G0JT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 545 F.3d 17=
9,
203 (2d Cir. 2008)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4XFDYHJ0K1MNJ1MG0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:42PH-01G0-0038-X2BT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>De Falco v.
Bernas</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:42PH-01G0-0038-X2BT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 244 F.3d 28=
6,
309 (2d Cir. 2001)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4XFDYHJ0K1MNJ1MK0000400_2"></a>It is the enterprise, not =
the
individual defendant, that must engage in or affect interstate commerce. <u=
>See
</u></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4XFDYHJ0K1MNJ1MJ0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4N-C890-003B-614W-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Khaimi v.
Schonberger</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4N-C890-003B-614W-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 664 F. Supp.
54, 60 (E.D.N.Y. 1987)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4XFDYHJ0K1MNJ1PT0000400"></a>Here, plaintiff alleges that
defendants submitted fraudulent medical claims to, and affected
&nbsp;[**49]&nbsp;the business of, plaintiff, a national insurance company,=
 an
Illinois corporation, with its principal place of business in Bloomington,
Illinois. This alleged fact is sufficient to provide the required interstate
nexus. <u>See </u></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4XFDYHJ0K1MNJ1PS0000400"></a>=
<a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4DDR-B9V0-0038-X2CF-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>First Capital
Asset Mgmt., Inc. v. Satinwood, Inc</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4DDR-B9V0-0038-X2CF-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>., 385 F.3d 1=
59,
173 n.12 (2d Cir. 2004)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",se=
rif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal41 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[*231]&nbsp;
Accordingly, plaintiff has properly pleaded its RICO violations against the
Klotsman defendants and defendant Kagan.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal41 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Other Arguments</span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal41 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Any
arguments by defendants, for example, the role of <u>res judicata</u> or
collateral estoppel, as to specific invoices submitted to plaintiff, are
premature at this time. Defendants have failed to identify anything in the
pleadings or the public record which is properly considered at this stage of
the proceedings.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal41 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Conclusion</span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal41 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>For
the reasons set forth above, the court denies the motions to dismiss of the
Laufer defendants, the Klotsman defendants and defendant Kagan in their
entirety.</span></p>

