mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1</spa=
n></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> of
the Sherman Act. Whether or not the district court correctly viewed the
allegations of the Complaint itself as too conclusory, we conclude that the
court &nbsp;[**44]&nbsp;erred in ruling that the additional factual allegat=
ions
in the PAC were equally conclusory and provided no plausible basis for an
inference of conspiracy. In light of the PAC's allegations, we have difficu=
lty
with the court's antitrust analysis &nbsp;[*182]&nbsp; and its application =
of <u>Twombly's</u>
plausibility test.</span></p>

