:contentItem:44R3-71P0-0038-X4HD-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>., 275 F.3d 1=
91,
203 (2d Cir. 2001)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (&quot;<u>Todd</u>&quot;). A co=
urt
ruling on such a motion may not properly dismiss a complaint that states a
plausible version of the events &nbsp;[**53]&nbsp;merely because the court
finds a different version more plausible.</span></p>

