<p class=3DNormal43 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>One
of the potential bases for liability under &sect;&sect; 11 and 12(a)(2) is =
an
omission in contravention of an affirmative legal disclosure obligation. <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id</i>. In this case, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dadministrative-cod=
es&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:61RX-V8M3-GXJ9-324R-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Item 303</spa=
n></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> of
SEC Regulation S-K provides &nbsp;[**16]&nbsp;the basis for Ikanos's alleged
disclosure obligation. <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc4_40"></a>The Regula=
tion,
as we have seen, requires registrants to &quot;[d]escribe any known trends =
or
uncertainties . . . that the registrant reasonably expects will have a mate=
rial
. . . unfavorable impact on . . . revenues or income from continuing
operations.&quot; Instruction 3 to paragraph 303(a) provides that &quot;[t]=
he
discussion and analysis shall focus specifically on material events and
uncertainties known to management that would cause reported financial
information not to be necessarily indicative of future operating results or=
 of
future financial condition.&quot; </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dadministrative-cod=
es&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:61RX-V8M3-GXJ9-324R-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>17 C.F.R. &se=
ct;
229.303(a)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-farea=
st-font-family:
Times;color:black'> instruction 3. According to the SEC's interpretive rele=
ase
regarding </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dadministrative-cod=
es&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:61RX-V8M3-GXJ9-324R-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Item 303</spa=
n></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
the Regulation imposes a disclosure duty &quot;where a trend, demand,
commitment, event or uncertainty is both [1] presently known to management =
and
[2] reasonably likely to have material effects on the registrant's financial
condition or results of operations.&quot; Management's Discussion and Analy=
sis
of Financial Condition and Results of Operations, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dadministrative-mat=
erials&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:3T1N-Y6D0-000Y-43D4-00000-00&amp;context=3D=
"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Securities Act
Release No. 6835, Exchange Act Release No. 26,831, Investment Company Act
Release No. 16,961, 43 SEC Docket 1330, 1989 SEC LEXIS 1011 (May 18, 1989)<=
/span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
&nbsp;[**17]&nbsp;We believe that, viewed in the context of </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dadministrative-cod=
es&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:61RX-V8M3-GXJ9-324R-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Item 303</spa=
n></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>'s
disclosure obligations, the defect rate, in a vacuum, is not what is at iss=
ue.
Rather, it is the manner in which uncertainty surrounding that defect rate,
generated by an increasing flow of highly negative information from key
customers, might reasonably be expected to have a material impact on future
revenues.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal43 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Litwin v. Blackstone Group, L.P<=
/span></i><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.,
decided after the district court denied Panther leave to file the 2PSAC, is
instructive on this point. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I13MHHRHRGT0007952T0025D"></=
a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I55X6FF32N1PSV0050000400"></a>There, investors sued Blacks=
tone,
an asset management company, under &sect;&sect; 11 and 12(a)(2) for omitting
&nbsp;[*121]&nbsp; from a registration statement and prospectus information
regarding negative trends in the real estate market. Blackstone's real esta=
te
investments accounted for approximately 22.6% of its assets under managemen=
t.
Reversing the district court's dismissal of the complaint, we held that
plaintiffs adequately alleged that Blackstone was required by </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dadministrative-cod=
es&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:61RX-V8M3-GXJ9-324R-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Item 303</spa=
n></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> to
disclose the trend, &quot;already known and existing at the time of the
IPO,&quot; because it &quot;was reasonably likely to have a material impact=
 on
Blackstone's financial condition.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I55X6FF32N1PSV0040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5254-JR11-652R-01XX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>634 F.3d at 7=
16</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
In so holding, we emphasized that</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal43 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bott=
om:0in;
margin-left:20.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:15.=
0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>the
key information &nbsp;[**18]&nbsp;that plaintiffs assert should have been
disclosed is whether, and to what extent, the particular known trend, event=
, or
uncertainty might have been reasonably expected to materially affect
Blackstone's investments. . . . <a name=3D"Bookmark_I55X6FF328T4PK002000040=
0"></a>Again,
the focus of plaintiffs' claims is the required disclosures under </span><a
