Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>RICO's legislative history fully
supports our analysis.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>Indeed,
illegal gambling appears to have been a primary concern of Congress when
enacting RICO, </span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn478' href=3D"#_ftn478"
name=3D"_ftnref478" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",seri=
f;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>4</span></sup></a><span style=3D'font-family=
:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>&nbsp;[**12]&nbsp; and there is =
no
language in the legislative history to indicate that the alleged enterprise
must engage in activities separate and distinct from illicit gambling to co=
me
within the purview of RICO.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>In
fact, the legislative history consistently speaks of the broad scope and
important remedial purposes to be served by the Act. </span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn479' href=3D"#_ftn479" name=3D"_ftnref479" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>5</span><=
/sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
The Supreme Court has honored this legislative intent by giving the term
&quot;enterprise&quot; a broad scope.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4FPXWCR0K1MNJ4BG0000400"></a><a
