name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4T2D6NCX0030000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Importantly, the <u>Holmes</u> C=
ourt
also provided three functional factors with which &nbsp;[*36]&nbsp; to asse=
ss
whether proximate cause exists under RICO. First, the Court noted concerns
about proof, reasoning that &quot;the less direct an injury is, the more
difficult it becomes to ascertain the amount of a plaintiff's damages
attributable to the violation, as distinct from other, independent,
factors.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4T28T51W0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>503 U.S. at 2=
69</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Second were concerns about administrability and the avoidance of multiple
&nbsp;[**32]&nbsp;recoveries: &quot;[R]ecognizing claims of the indirectly
injured would force courts to adopt complicated rules apportioning damages
among plaintiffs removed at different levels of injury from the violative a=
cts,
to obviate the risk of multiple recoveries.&quot; <u>Id</u>. Third, the Cou=
rt
focused on the societal interest in deterring illegal conduct and whether t=
hat
interest would be served in a particular case: &quot;[T]he need to grapple =
with
[the previous two] problems [may be] simply unjustified by the general inte=
rest
in deterring injurious conduct, since directly injured victims can generall=
y be
counted on to vindicate the law as private attorneys general, without any of
the problems attendant upon suits by plaintiffs injured more remotely.&quot=
; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4T2D6NCX0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id</span></i>=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>. at 269-70</=
span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.</span></p>

