k'>
also supports the conclusion that Kaiser meets the proximate cause requirem=
ent
for several additional reasons. First, <u>Bridge</u> held that the plaintif=
fs
there &quot;clearly were injured by [defendants'] scheme,&quot; as they lost
valuable property they would not otherwise have lost. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4T2HM68Y0050000400"></a><a
