<p class=3DNormal45 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4V2HM6960020000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Pfizer's argument is a repetitio=
n of
its assertion that there is an intervening cause -- individual physicians'
independent medical judgment -- which precludes a finding of causation base=
d on
aggregate evidence. But &quot;the burden of proving an 'intervening cause' =
--
something which snaps the 'causal chain' (that is, operates as a 'supersedi=
ng
cause,' wiping out the defendant's liability) that connects the wrongful ac=
t to
the defendant's injury -- is on the defendant.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4V2HM6960010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:52FW-1VM1-F04K-R033-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id</span></i>=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:52FW-1VM1-F04K-R033-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>. at 757</spa=
n></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(citation omitted). Pfizer did offer the testimony of doctors who said that
their decisions to prescribe Neurontin were not influenced by Pfizer's
fraudulent marketing, and the jury and district court, within their powers,
rejected the argument.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal45 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Pfizer
also argues that its testimony from doctors who stated that they prescribed
Neurontin for off-label uses without relying on Pfizer's misrepresentations
&quot;falsified&quot; Kaiser's statistical analysis. Not so. The existence =
of
some doctors who purportedly were not influenced by Pfizer's misinformation
would not defeat the inference that this misinformation had a significant
influence on prescribing decisions &nbsp;[**62]&nbsp;which injured Kaiser.
Indeed, Dr. Rosenthal noted the scientific invalidity of looking to physici=
an-by-physician
accounts of their prescribing decisions. Weighing the individual testimony
presented by Pfizer &nbsp;[*46]&nbsp; against the aggregate evidence presen=
ted
by Kaiser was a task for the jury and district court.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal45 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4V2HM6960040000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Pfizer next argues that the
Rosenthal report merely demonstrated &quot;correlation&quot; and not
&quot;causation.&quot; But if Pfizer's information could not be expected to
affect a single doctor's decision making, the company's choice to undertake=
 the
marketing campaign would be inexplicable. <u>Cf</u>. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4V2HM6960030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:52FW-1VM1-F04K-R033-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>id</span></i>=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:52FW-1VM1-F04K-R033-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>. at 758</spa=
n></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(&quot;The object of [the defendants'] conspiracies was to obtain liens that
would otherwise go to [the plaintiffs and other] bidders -- there could be =
no
other reason for wanting to pack the room in violation of the County's rule=
. .
. . How likely is it that [plaintiffs] lost <u>no</u> bids to bidders who h=
ad
13 arms in the room but should have had only three?&quot;).</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal45 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4V2D6ND70010000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>More generally, Pfizer argues th=
at
Kaiser's use of aggregate evidence is precluded by the decisions of other
courts in pharmaceutical marketing RICO fraud cases. Pfizer relies on a ser=
ies
of cases that it argues have rejected evidence like Kaiser's. <u>See,
&nbsp;[**63]&nbsp;e.g., </u></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4V2HM696005000=
0400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:55N7-0PB1-F04K-K0CW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>In re Schering
Plough Corp. Intron/Temodar Consumer Class Action</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:55N7-0PB1-F04K-K0CW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 678 F.3d 235
(3d Cir. 2012)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'>; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4V2D6ND70020000400"><=
/a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:52CP-JM01-JCNJ-6038-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Ironworkers L=
ocal
Union 68 v. Astra Zeneca Pharm., LP</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:52CP-JM01-JCNJ-6038-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 634 F.3d 13=
52
(11th Cir. 2011)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4V2D6ND70040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5109-4R71-652R-0000-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>UFCW Local 17=
76
v. Eli Lilly &amp; Co</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5109-4R71-652R-0000-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>., 620 F.3d 1=
21
(2d Cir. 2010)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'>; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4V2SF8C50010000400"><=
/a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4X06-XCR0-TXFP-K277-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
