name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc11_26"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",=
serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The burden of proof as to damage=
s is
lower than that for causation, &nbsp;[**74]&nbsp;and the fact finder is
afforded a greater deal of freedom to estimate damages where the defendant,=
 as
here, has created the risk of uncertainty. <u>See </u></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4V2D6NDB0010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3V4J-TT00-0038-X0NB-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
