the
possibility of holding a bellwether trial as to one TPP's claims against the
defendants. The court stated on September 18, 2009, that it favored holding=
 a
trial on Kaiser's claims, a view joined by plaintiffs on October 2, 2009.</=
span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn503' href=3D"#_ftn503" name=3D"_ftnref503" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>23</span>=
</sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
Defendants opposed, saying that any bellwether trial should not be on Kaise=
r's
claims because &quot;Kaiser is the most atypical of the named TPPs.&quot;
During none of these discussions did Pfizer suggest that venue should be
transferred to California.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal45 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4V2HM6980030000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>On November 12, 2009, the distri=
ct
court ordered that &quot;[t]he trial in the action brought by coordinated
plaintiff Kaiser will begin [before it] on February 22, 2010.&quot; About a
month later, Pfizer moved to transfer &nbsp;[**76]&nbsp;venue pursuant to <=
/span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5HW2-D6RV-H0J2-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
