if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Coady v. Ashc=
raft
&amp; Gerel</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:40XP-H270-0038-X0YK-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 223 F.3d 1,=
 11
(1st Cir. 2000)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. Kaiser opposed defendants' mot=
ion
to transfer, and coordinated plaintiffs Aetna and Guardian were domiciled in
New York and Connecticut, respectively. The Massachusetts district court had
considerable experience with complex claims against defendants arising out =
of
the fraudulent marketing of Neurontin, and coordinated plaintiffs' claims w=
ere
national in scope, not localized to California.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal45 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>B. <u>Denial
of Pfizer's Motion for New Trial Based on Purportedly New Evidence Regarding
the Cochrane Review of Neuropathic Pain</u></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal45 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4V28T5280010000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4V28T5280030000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>There was no abuse of discretion=
 in
the district &nbsp;[**78]&nbsp;court's denial of defendants' March 22, 2011
motion for new trial. At trial, Pfizer had presented expert testimony that
Neurontin was effective for the broad treatment of neuropathic pain, which
relied in part on a 2005 review by the Cochrane Collaboration, an independe=
nt
organization, that concluded that adequate evidence supported Neurontin's
efficacy for neuropathic pain. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4V2N1RHD0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:8332-2RB1-652H-V13D-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Kaiser Findin=
gs</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:8332-2RB1-652H-V13D-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 2011 U.S. D=
ist.
LEXIS 99593, 2011 WL 3852254, at *42</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-fami=
ly:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. The district cou=
rt
discounted this testimony because the 2005 Cochrane Review was based on
incomplete information, given defendants' suppression of negative informati=
on
about Neurontin's efficacy for the broad treatment of neuropathic pain. </s=
pan><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5889J4V28T5280020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:8332-2RB1-652H-V13D-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>2011 U.S. Dis=
t.
LEXIS 99593, [WL] at *42-43</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times=
",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal45 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
2011, the Cochrane Collaboration published another review of the effects of
gabapentin in treating chronic neuropathic pain. This revised review was
&quot;updated with the inclusion of unpublished information made available
through litigation&quot; and concluded that &quot;[g]abapentin provides pain
relief of a high level in about a third of people who take [it] for painful
neuropathic pain.&quot;</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal45 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
district court denied defendants' motion for a new trial, explaining that a
credible meta-analysis from the Cochrane Collaboration based on
&nbsp;[**79]&nbsp;the entirety of the scientific evidence concerning
Neurontin's use in treating broad neuropathic pain was unavailable to
defendants at the time of trial only because &quot;Pfizer itself did not
provide the Cochrane Group with all available studies prior to the trial
because it fraudulently suppressed these studies.&quot; That reason was suf=
ficient.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal45 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>VII.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal45 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
judgment of the district court is <u>affirmed</u>.</span></p>

