miss
are denied to the extent that they argue lack of standing.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal47 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>b) <u>RICO Conspiracy Claim</u><=
/span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal47 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I521F27C0PXTX20040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Section 1962(=
d)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
makes it &quot;unlawful for any person to conspire to violate&quot; any of =
the
substantive provisions of RICO. </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
1962(d)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>. Thus, a RICO conspiracy is &quot;an agreement to condu=
ct
or to participate in the conduct of a charged enterprise's affairs through a
pattern of racketeering.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I521F27C0PXTX20030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4X1S-WS40-TXFX-42C8-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
 v.
Pizzonia</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4X1S-WS40-TXFX-42C8-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 577 F.3d 45=
5,
464 (2d Cir. 2009)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (citing </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I521F27C0PXTX20050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-63B0-001B-K0HX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
 v.
Persico</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-63B0-001B-K0HX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 832 F.2d at
705, 713 (2d Cir. 1987))</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",s=
erif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. Defendants claim that plaintif=
fs
have neither pleaded a substantive RICO violation nor established an agreem=
ent
among the defendants. Here, the pleadings sufficiently allege substantive R=
ICO
violations and plausibly establish an agreement among the defendants, as
discussed <u>supra</u>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal47 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I521F27C0PXTX40030000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>In addition, while a defendant m=
ay
not be liable under the &quot;operation or management&quot; test for
substantive RICO violations, he may be liable of a RICO conspiracy where he
&quot;'know[s] the general nature of the conspiracy and that the conspiracy
extends beyond this] individual &nbsp;[**32]&nbsp;role[].'&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I521F27C0PXTX40020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3YXR-FVF0-0038-X2Y8-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
 v.
Zichettello</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3YXR-FVF0-0038-X2Y8-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 208 F.3d 72=
, 99
(2d Cir. 2000)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'> (quoting </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I521F27C0PXTX400400=
00400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CRN0-003B-5347-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
 v.
Rastelli</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CRN0-003B-5347-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 870 F.2d 82=
2,
828 (2d Cir. 1989))</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>; <u>see also </u></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I521F27C0PXTX60010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RHK-1090-004C-300F-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Salinas v. Un=
ited
States</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RHK-1090-004C-300F-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 522 U.S. 52,
64, 118 S. Ct. 469, 139 L. Ed. 2d 352 (1997)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(&quot;A person . . . may be liable for </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>[&sect; 1962(=
d)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>]
conspiracy even though he was incapable of committing the substantive
offense.&quot;). For the above reasons, I deny the Samserv defendants' moti=
ons
to dismiss the RICO conspiracy claims with respect to all Samserv employees,
including the five individual process server defendants. Conversely, becaus=
e of
the insufficiency of the pleadings with respect to Waldman, Orlando, and
Canella, I also dismiss all RICO conspiracy claims against them. The Compla=
int
has sufficiently pleaded facts, however, that would establish the liability=
 of
all other defendants for the RICO conspiracy claim, and thus this prong of
their motions to dismiss is denied.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal47 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
