&para;&para; 58, 60.) According to the complaint, these &quot;litigation
activities,&quot; constitute mail fraud. (Compl. &para;&para; 58, 60.)
Specifically, in order to advance the &quot;scheme to litigate&quot;
DeGregorio's alleged &quot;fee obligation&quot; to the Curtis Law Firm, the
Bushman defendants allegedly committed mail fraud by mailing to the court,
other parties, witnesses, or counsel: (1) a Reply to the Counterclaims asse=
rted
by the Curtis Law Firm on February 9, 2007; (2) a Notice for Discovery on
