name=3D"Bookmark_fnpara_15"></a><span style=3D'font-size:9.0pt;mso-bidi-fon=
t-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'=
>We
do not determine whether the state-court proceedings here constitute predic=
ate
acts under RICO, as the parties do not address that issue, and it is not
necessary for us to reach. That said, we briefly address some general points
relevant to that issue. This Court held in <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:=
normal'>Kim
v. Kimm</i> that &quot;allegations of frivolous, fraudulent, or baseless
litigation activities&#8212;without more&#8212;cannot constitute a RICO
predicate act.&quot; <b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>884 F.3d 98, 104 (2d Cir. 2018)</i></b=
>.
Because the plaintiff there had alleged that the defendant &quot;engaged in=
 a <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>single</i> frivolous, fraudulent, or
baseless lawsuit,&quot; we determined that &quot;such litigation activity <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>alone</i> cannot constitute a viable R=
ICO
predicate act.&quot; <b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id. at 105</i></b> (emphases added). We
declined, however, &quot;to reach the issue of whether all RICO actions bas=
ed
on litigation activity are categorically meritless.&quot; <i style=3D'mso-b=
idi-font-style:
normal'>Id.</i> The instant action is distinguishable from <i style=3D'mso-=
bidi-font-style:
normal'>Kim</i>. State Farm does not appear to contend that the state-court
proceedings here are predicate acts under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-size:9.0pt;mso-bid=
i-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077C=
C;
background:white'>18 U.S.C. &sect; 1961(1)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-size:9.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Times",seri=
f;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, but instead that they help fur=
ther
the RICO violation, which consists of a pattern of racketeering activity un=
der
the mail fraud statute through other fraudulent activities alleged in the
complaint. In other words, the issue is not whether the state-court proceed=
ings
are <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>themselves</i> predicate acts, =
but
rather that they are allegedly designed to perpetuate and monetize the RICO
scheme for the reasons described above. Thus, we need not consider whether =
the
state-court proceedings are themselves predicate acts.</span></p>

