<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Richard
J. Holwell, District Judge:</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
this case plaintiff DDR Construction Services, Inc. (&quot;DDR&quot;) sues
several of its former associates in the construction, electrical
subcontracting, and consulting industries in New York for violations of the
Racketeer Influenced and Corrupt Organizations Act, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U.S.C.
&sect;&sect; 1961 </span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>et seq.</span=
></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(&quot;RICO&quot;), as well as for fraud, breach of fiduciary duty, and sev=
eral
other state law claims. Currently pending are four motions to dismiss filed=
 by
different groups of defendants; DDR's cross-motions to strike, to dismiss
counterclaims, and for sanctions; and DDR's cross-motion for leave to seek
sanctions. DDR has also submitted a letter application seeking leave to fil=
e an
amended complaint. For the reasons that follow, defendants' motions are
GRANTED; DDR's cross-motion to strike and to dismiss, and for sanctions, is
GRANTED IN PART and is DENIED IN PART; DDR's cross-motion for leave to seek
sanctions is DENIED; and, DDR's letter application is DENIED.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>I. FACTUAL SETTING</span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_II08GN4RDBSD003RSXSB003C4"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M38YB0K3NNW0020000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M38YB0K3NNW0040000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>For &nbsp;[**3]&nbsp;the purpose=
s of
the present motions, the following facts, drawn from the complaint and the
documents incorporated by reference therein, are taken as true. Because the
complaint incorporates by reference a litigation involving many of the same
parties and factual issues ongoing in the Supreme Court of the State of New
York, County of Queens, <a name=3D"Bookmark_I52M38YB0K3NNW0010000400"></a><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>First Keystone Consultants, Inc. v. DDR
Constr. Servs., 25 Misc. 3d 1217A, 901 N.Y.S.2d 906 (N.Y. Sup. Ct.)</i>
(hereinafter the &quot;Queens Action&quot;), the pleadings and decisions in
that matter are also described and considered. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-st=
yle:
normal'>See </i></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52M38YB0K3NNW0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4CF1-6070-0038-X0VC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Blue Tree Hot=
els
Inv. (Canada), Ltd. v. Starwood Hotels &amp; Resorts Worldwide, Inc.</span>=
</i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4CF1-6070-0038-X0VC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 369 F.3d 21=
2,
217 (2d Cir. 2004)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (<a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFcls=
cc1"></a>&quot;Our
review is generally limited to the facts and allegations that are contained=
 in
the complaint and in any documents that are [] incorporated into the compla=
int
by reference. . . . But we may also look to public records, including
complaints filed in state court, in deciding a motion to dismiss.&quot;
(internal citations omitted)).</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>A. The Parties</span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Plaintiff
DDR is a New Jersey corporation that provides consulting and other services=
 to
entities in the construction industry. (Compl. &para;&para; 8, 33.)
Specifically, DDR brings together other construction &nbsp;[**4]&nbsp;indus=
try
entities in order to facilitate bidding, assists in arranging bids, and man=
ages
construction projects. (<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i>
&para;&para; 21, 25-26, 33-34.) As of 2001, DDR's vice president, Clifford
Weiner (&quot;Weiner&quot;), had affiliations with several
construction-industry entities operating in the New York area, including de=
fendants
Schlesinger Electrical Contractors, Inc. (&quot;Schlesinger&quot;), and Fir=
st
Keystone Consultants, Inc. (&quot;First Keystone&quot;). (<i style=3D'mso-b=
idi-font-style:
normal'>Id.</i> &para; 21.) In 2004, Weiner was also vice president of
Schlesinger. (<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i> &para; 32.)</=
span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Defendants
Siemens Energy &amp; Automation, Inc. (&quot;SEA&quot;), and Siemens Indust=
ry,
Inc. (&quot;SII&quot;), (collectively &quot;Siemens&quot;), are Delaware
corporations that provide electrical, engineering, and automation solutions
&nbsp;[*636]&nbsp; in the construction industry. (<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font=
-style:
normal'>Id.</i> &para; 9; Siemens' Defs.' Mem. at 4.) </span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn1' href=3D"#_ftn1" name=3D"_ftnref1" title=3D""=
><sup><span
