<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>C. SSE's Alleged Criminal Acts</=
span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
2005, SSE won bids for at least three NYCDEP projects including the &quot;2=
6th
Ward Project,&quot; the &quot;Wards Island Project,&quot; and the &quot;Cro=
ton
Facility Project.&quot; (Compl. &para;&para; 80-83, 85.) However,
&nbsp;[**17]&nbsp;in preparing its bids and performing the contracts, SSE
allegedly engaged in broad-scale fraudulent activity &quot;caus[ing] enormo=
us
harm to the profitability of the [projects].&quot; (<i style=3D'mso-bidi-fo=
nt-style:
normal'>Id.</i> &para; 179.) For example, DDR alleges that SSE manipulated =
New
York City's Minority Business Entity (&quot;MBE&quot;) program, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6KPN-CW63-RW53-154J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>New York City
Administrative Code &sect; 6-129</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, &nbsp;[*640]&nbsp; by creating
sham transactions in order to claim MBE credit. According to DDR, Siemens a=
nd
Schlesinger </span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn11' href=3D"#_ftn11"
name=3D"_ftnref11" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>11</span></sup></a><span style=3D'font-famil=
y:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> caused an electri=
cal
subcontractor, J&amp;R Rey Electrical (&quot;JR&quot;), to accept funds from
Schlesinger and use those funds to purchase electrical equipment from Sieme=
ns.
(Compl. &para;&para; 152-155.) SSE then counted JR's costs in those purchas=
es
against its MBE requirements. (<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.<=
/i>)
SSE thus charged at least $320,000 of fraudulent expenses incurred by JR in
equipment purchases against the 26th Ward Project, along with at least $100=
,000
in legal fees in preparation for litigation with JR and &quot;enormous&quot;
amounts in preparation for investigations by &quot;several&quot; State
agencies. (<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i> &para;&para; 150=
(a),
158, 159.) In order to secure JR's cooperation, Siemens, Schlesinger, Deurl=
ein,
and Levita allegedly put financial pressure on JR and forced JR to hire SSE=
's
accountant Guddemi, nominally &nbsp;[**18]&nbsp;as an electrician, but in r=
eality
as a &quot;fox guarding the henhouse.&quot; (<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-styl=
e:
normal'>Id.</i> &para;&para; 188-192.) The over $86,000 paid to Guddemi was
also charged against the 26th Ward Project between January 2006 and January
2008. (<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i> &para; 194.) Additio=
nally,
through his position Guddemi was able to secure &quot;enormous&quot; profits
for his company, Alison, which were all hidden from the Internal Revenue
Service. (<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i> &para; 195).</spa=
n></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>DDR
also alleges that SSE, Siemens, Schlesinger, and First Keystone defrauded
NYCDEP by forging documents in order to meet NYCDEP's requirement that SSE
employ a &quot;Master Electrician&quot; full time. (<i style=3D'mso-bidi-fo=
nt-style:
normal'>Id.</i> &para;&para; 160-163.) Allegedly, between July of 2006 and
April of 2008, SSE paid one Bronislav Ostrovsky (&quot;Ostrovsky&quot;) at
least $36,000 to serve as SSE's Master Electrician, but Ostrovsky was actua=
lly
employed by another contractor, Five Star Electric, Inc., during that perio=
d. (<i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i> &para;&para; 163-170.) Not onl=
y were
SSE's payments to Ostrovsky charged to the 26th Ward Project so as to dimin=
ish
the Project's value, but, as with the MBE scheme, SSE has incurred
&quot;extraordinary costs and fees&quot; due to State &nbsp;[**19]&nbsp;inv=
estigations
of the Ostrovsky payments. (<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i>
&para;&para; 150(c), 166.) Finally, DDR makes several more general allegati=
ons
including that SSE management along with Schlesinger and First Keystone (1)
wrongfully diverted SSE funds to themselves; (2) intentionally falsified and
confused SSE records; and (3) engaged in widespread nepotism. <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>(See id.</i> &para;&para; 182A-F.)</sp=
an></p>

