<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>All
moving defendants argue that the &quot;<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:norm=
al'>Colorado
River</i> abstention doctrine&quot; requires this Court to dismiss the pres=
ent
action because &nbsp;[**26]&nbsp;DDR is litigating its entitlement to the
anticipated profits from SSE's NYCDEP contracts in the Queens Action.
Defendants argue, &quot;[a] ruling in the Queens Action that DDR is not
