suit
since DDR would be unable to sustain a claim for damages.&quot; (Siemens De=
fs.'
Mem. at 12.)</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M398F0K3S7Y0030000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M398F0K3S7Y0050000400"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFc=
lscc3"></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&quot;The
doctrine of abstention, under which a District Court may decline to exercis=
e or
postpone the exercise of its jurisdiction, is an extraordinary and narrow
exception to the duty of a District Court to adjudicate a controversy prope=
rly
before it.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52M398F0K3S7Y0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-9YH0-003B-S3H5-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Colorado River
Water Conservation Dist. v. United States</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-9YH0-003B-S3H5-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 424 U.S. 80=
0,
813, 96 S. Ct. 1236, 47 L. Ed. 2d 483 (1976)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M39KR0K3VHD0020000400"></a>Unlike other abstention doct=
rines
related to &quot;considerations of proper constitutional adjudication and
regard for federal-state &nbsp;[*644]&nbsp; relations,&quot; <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Colorado River</i> abstention &quot;re=
st[s]
on considerations of wise judicial administration, giving regard to
conservation of judicial resources and comprehensive disposition of
litigation.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52M398F0K3S7Y0040000400"></a>=
<a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-9YH0-003B-S3H5-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-9YH0-003B-S3H5-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> at 817</span=
></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
However, &quot;[a]lthough duplicative litigation as between federal courts =
is
ordinarily to be avoided, . . . the pendency of an action in [] state court=
 is
no bar to proceedings concerning &nbsp;[**27]&nbsp;the same matter in []
Federal court . . . <a name=3D"Bookmark_I52M39KR0K3VHD0020000400_2"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_II08GN4RDBSD003RSXSB003C6"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M39M00K3VJP0010000400"></a>[due to] the virtually unfla=
gging
obligation of the federal courts to exercise the jurisdiction given them.&q=
uot;
</span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52M39KR0K3VHD0010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:42CM-SY00-0038-X2ST-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Woodford v. C=
mty.
Action Agency of Greene Cnty., Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:42CM-SY00-0038-X2ST-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 239 F.3d 51=
7,
522 (2d Cir. 2001)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (citing </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M39KR0K3VHD0030000400"></a><a
