Times;color:black'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M39SD0K3WGB0010000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>These &nbsp;[**42]&nbsp;rulings =
now
preclude DDR from claiming status as a partner, member, or joint venturer in
SSE. Whether DDR was a member or partner in SSE for the purposes of its
fiduciary duty claim against SSE in state court is identical to whether DDR=
 was
a member or partner is SSE for the purposes of its claims here. <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See</i> 18 Wright et al., Federal Prac=
tice
and Procedure &sect; 4421 (2d ed. 2002) (when the controlling legal princip=
als
and the facts involved are the same, the issues are identical for purposes =
of
claim preclusion). Resolution of the issue was also necessary to Justice Ha=
rt's
dismissal of DDR's fiduciary duty claim.<a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc14"=
></a> <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M39SD0K3WGB0030000400"></a>&quot;An issue is necessary =
to a
prior judgment for issue preclusion purposes if its disposition was the bas=
is
for the holding with respect to the issue and not mere dictum.&quot; </span=
><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M39S10K3WF40050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4N-C720-001T-530B-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>MTS, Inc. v. =
200
East 87th Street Assocs.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4N-C720-001T-530B-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 899 F. Supp.
1180, 1184 (S.D.N.Y. 1995)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-styl=
e:
normal'>see also</i> 18 Wright et al. &sect; 4421 (invoked issue need not be
but-for element supporting prior court's decision; instead issue must be
independently sufficient ground carefully considered by the prior court). <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M39SD0K3WGB0030000400_2"></a>The reasoning behind Justi=
ce
Hart's decision was (1) that the documentary evidence established that DDR =
was
neither a member &nbsp;[**43]&nbsp;in SSE as an LLC nor a partner in SSE as=
 an
alleged joint venture; and (2) that therefore SSE and DDR were not in a
fiduciary relationship. </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52M39SD0K3WGB0020000400=
"></a><a
