k'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_II08GN4RDBSD003RSXSB003D4"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3C6W0K45290010000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>DDR's &nbsp;[**54]&nbsp;argument=
s on
proximate cause fail because (1) the Supreme Court in </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3C6M0K450S0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:7XMP-8RB0-YB0V-912G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Hemi Group</s=
pan></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
explicitly rejected all three of the measures of proximate causation DDR
invokes; and (2) DDR's injury is insufficiently direct for the two reasons
explained in that case. First, DDR's injuries caused by defendants' conduct
were, at best, harm in the fourth step. DDR can claim its injury only as a
partner in SFD and not as a member or partner in SSE; for the reasons discu=
ssed
<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>supra</i>, DDR is collaterally esto=
pped
from alleging partnership or membership in SSE. And any harm to the value of
SSE's NYCDEP contracts caused by payments to JR, Ostrovsky, or Guddemi was =
felt
first by SSE, not by DDR. Before DDR can claim injury, the harm must flow
through SSE; then to Schlesinger as a member in SSE; then to SFD pursuant to
Schlesinger's relationship with SFD; and finally to DDR as a partner in SFD=
. As
in <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Hemi Group</i>, &quot;[b]ecause
[DDR's] theory of causation requires [the Court] to move well beyond the fi=
rst
step,&quot; and indeed to the fourth step of the harm, &quot;that theory ca=
nnot
meet RICO's direct relationship requirement.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3C6W0K45290020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:7XMP-8RB0-YB0V-912G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>130 S. Ct. at=
 989</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_II08GN4RDBSD003RSXSB003D5"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_II08GN4RDBSD003RSXSB003D6"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3C6W0K45290050000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Second, DDR's proximate cause th=
eory
fails because defendants' RICO violations were &nbsp;[**55]&nbsp;not
&quot;directly responsible&quot; for DDR's injury. First, to the extent that
the injury's value equals amounts SSE has charged against the NYCDEP contra=
cts
in fighting investigations or litigation pursued by JR, these charges are of
the type precisely rejected as a basis for proximate causation in </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3C6W0K45290040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4K41-DS80-004C-200J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Anza</span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4K41-DS80-004C-200J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> </span></i><=
/a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>and
</span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3C720K45380010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:7XMP-8RB0-YB0V-912G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Hemi Group</s=
pan></i></a><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.</span></i><span style=3D'font-=
family:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> The alleged predi=
cate
acts, defrauding New York City concerning MBE and Master Electrician
requirements and extorting JR, were not directly responsible for the
investigation and litigation expenses. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3C720K45380040000400"></a>Instead the decisions of the=
 City
and JR to pursue those avenues are the acts directly responsible for SSE's
incurring of the related expenses. As &quot;the cause of [DDR's] harm was a=
 set
of actions [(charging expenses against the contract accounts)] entirely
distinct from the alleged RICO violation (defrauding the [City and extorting
JR]) [t]he alleged violation . . . [did] not le[a]d directly to the plainti=
ff's
injuries.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3C720K45380030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:7XMP-8RB0-YB0V-912G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Hemi Group</s=
pan></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:7XMP-8RB0-YB0V-912G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 130 S. Ct. =
at
990</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font=
-family:
Times;color:black'> (internal quotation marks and citation omitted). The sa=
me
is true regarding the direct costs of the activities. For DDR to have felt =
any
injury, several intervening acts share responsibility with defendants' purs=
uit
of the JR and Ostrovsky &nbsp;[**56]&nbsp;schemes. For example, SSE-not fac=
ing
a RICO claim from DDR-must have decided to charge the costs of its members'
RICO-violating schemes against the NYCDEP contracts as opposed to elsewhere.
Again, merely because defendants' predicate acts created a situation in whi=
ch
DDR sustained injury does not satisfy RICO's standing requirement; defendan=
ts'
acts must instead have <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>direct
responsibility</i> for the injury. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>=
Id.</i></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Finally,
there are several other parties with an incentive to sue for the violations
described. As the direct target of the predicate schemes, the City seems to
have such an incentive. Moreover, as any harm felt by DDR would be felt equ=
ally
by Schlesinger and First Keystone as co-partners in SFD, those parties would
have incentive to sue Siemens and its officers as well. Indeed, the only
difference between DDR's position and that of Schlesinger and First Keyston=
e is
that DDR was, allegedly, forced out of SFD. But DDR's expulsion, or withdra=
wal,
from SFD <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>is not</i> claimed as a
predicate act, nor does it seem it could be. Any extra injury to DDR, not f=
elt
by Schlesinger or First Keystone, was caused by <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-s=
tyle:
normal'>that act</i>-its expulsion &nbsp;[*654]&nbsp; from SFD-<i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>and not</i> by the predicate acts DDR =
relies
on to support &nbsp;[**57]&nbsp;its RICO claim. Thus, DDR's injury is not
caused by the predicate RICO acts, but instead of by facts &quot;entirely
distinct&quot; from those violations.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
