lscc30"></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&quot;Under
New York law, the elements of a negligence claim are: (i) a duty owed to the
plaintiff by the defendant; (ii) breach of that duty; and (iii) injury
substantially caused by that breach.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3GVT0K521J0010000400"></a><a
