:contentItem:4535-CJ50-0038-X31T-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 280 F.3d 20=
9,
215 (2d Cir. 2002)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. The duty invoked may take the =
form
of a fiduciary duty. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See </i></span=
><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3GVT0K521J0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4FB2-HTV0-TVW3-P2FP-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Moscato v. TIE
Techs., Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4FB2-HTV0-TVW3-P2FP-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, No. 04 Civ.
2487, 2005 U.S. Dist. LEXIS 867, 2005 WL 146806, *6 (S.D.N.Y. Jan. 21, 2005=
)</span></i></a><span
