<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
Siemens Defendants argue that DDR cannot establish that Siemens owed any du=
ty
to it. They are correct. DDR's complaint is vague and conclusory regarding =
the
first element of a negligence claim-the duty, if any, owed it by Siemens. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3HCN0K56KX0010000400"></a>The complaint states: &quot;=
[b]y
virtue of the relationship of trust and confidence between DDR and [Siemens]
which existed under the parties' arrangement, [Siemens] owed a duty of
care&quot; to DDR. (Compl. &para; 274.) The complaint says nothing else; &n=
bsp;[**84]&nbsp;and
DDR's brief is unhelpful as it does not address the issue. The Court,
interpreting the complaint's language as broadly as possible, reads the duty
alleged as sounding in fiduciary duty. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:norm=
al'>See
</i></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3H3J0K546K0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:7XN4-SRW0-YB0N-V0X0-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>DirecTV Latin
America, LLC v. Park 610, LLC</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:7XN4-SRW0-YB0N-V0X0-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 691 F. Supp=
. 2d
405, 439 (S.D.N.Y. 2010)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",s=
erif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (fiduciary duty owed between
partners or LLC members encompassing traditional duties of loyalty and <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>of care</i>). However, as discussed <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>supra</i>, DDR was not a joint venture=
r with
Siemens and Siemens had no duty, fiduciary or otherwise, to DDR. Therefore =
DDR
cannot make out the first element of a negligence claim, and that claim is
dismissed.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3HCN0K56KX0030000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>To the extent that DDR has inten=
ded
to assert a negligent entrustment claim, it appears that DDR has misunderst=
ood
the doctrine. Negligent entrustment requires that the owner of a dangerous
instrumentality not entrust that instrumentality to some whose use of it
creates an unreasonable risk of harm to other persons. <i style=3D'mso-bidi=
-font-style:
normal'>See </i></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3HCN0K56KX0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:42C6-30G0-0039-4320-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Rios v. Smith=
</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:42C6-30G0-0039-4320-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 95 N.Y.2d 6=
47,
744 N.E.2d 1156, 1158, 722 N.Y.S.2d 220 (N.Y. 2001)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(parents liable for negligent entrustment after allowing minor son to opera=
te
all-terrain-vehicle); </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3HCN0K56KX0040000400">=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4JH1-PTF0-0039-40JS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Kelly</span><=
/i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4JH1-PTF0-0039-40JS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 27 A.D.3d at
1082</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-fon=
t-family:
Times;color:black'> (same with motorboat). The claim here is that Siemens
managed SSE's funds in a negligent &nbsp;[**85]&nbsp;manner. (Compl. &para;
279-280 (&quot;[Siemens] is also negligent for its negligent entrustment of
funds to [other defendants]. . . . [This] created an unreasonable risk of h=
arm
to DDR's property interests.&quot;).) In other words, DDR does not allege t=
hat
there was a dangerous instrumentality, that there was any entrustment at al=
l,
or that there was a risk of harm to any person. Accordingly any negligent
entrustment claim is dismissed.</span></p>

