and must be dismissed.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
First &nbsp;[**86]&nbsp;Keystone Defendants respond that their counterclaim=
 is
not for fraud but for breach of fiduciary duty. (First Keystone Defs.' Opp'=
n at
2.) But as demonstrated <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>supra</i>, =
since
DDR was not a joint venturer in SSE, it had no fiduciary relationship to SS=
E or
the SSE partners, including First Keystone. Thus, even if First Keystone's
second counterclaim &nbsp;[*664]&nbsp; sounds in breach of fiduciary duty, =
it
would still be dismissed.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>First
Keystone's first counterclaim is not for fraud but for breach of contract. =
(<i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See id.</i> &para; 201.) DDR offers no
argument as to why this first counterclaim should be dismissed; therefore t=
he
claim survives.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3HCS0K56N00020000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Finally, First Keystone's third
counterclaim is for the costs and litigation fees spent in defending this
action. However,<a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc32"></a> &quot;[i]n New Yor=
k, the
issue of attorneys fees is not the proper subject for an independent cause =
of
action.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3HCS0K56N00010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4X9N-WPP0-TXFR-J34M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Merit Grp., L=
LC
v. Sint Maarten Int'l Telecomm. Servs. NV</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4X9N-WPP0-TXFR-J34M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, No. 08 Civ.
3496, 2009 U.S. Dist. LEXIS 88142, 2009 WL 3053739, at *3 (S.D.N.Y. Sept. 2=
4,
2009)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-fo=
nt-family:
Times;color:black'> (quoting <a name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3HCS0K56N00030000400">=
</a><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Terry v. Inc. Village of Patchogue, 886
N.Y.S.2d 72, 23 Misc. 3d 1118A, 2009 WL 1141599, at *8 (N.Y. Sup. Ct. 2009)=
)</i>.
Instead, &quot;attorney's fees are incidents of litigation and a prevailing
party may not collect them from the loser unless &nbsp;[**87]&nbsp;an award=
 is
authorized by agreement between the parties, statute or court rule.&quot; <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i> Thus First Keystone's third
counterclaim is dismissed.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>2. DDR's Cross-Motion to Strike =
is
Denied</span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
