<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Having
reviewed the First Keystone Defendants' Answer, the Court finds that DDR has
not met the required high standard. Indeed, DDR's own memorandum of law in
support of the motion undermines any &nbsp;[**89]&nbsp;argument that the An=
swer
is &quot;so unrelated to [DDR's] claims as to be unworthy of any
consideration.&quot; 5C Wright et al. &sect; 1380. For example, DDR points =
to
the First Keystone Defendants' allegation that Weiner was himself involved =
in
kickback schemes which resulted in his resignation from SSE's board. (Pl.'s
&nbsp;[*665]&nbsp; Mem. at 7.) But this allegation is directly related to t=
he
factual issues involved in this case. In addition, DDR makes no argument th=
at
allowing the Answer's allegations to remain in the proceeding will be
prejudicial. Accordingly, DDR's motion to strike the First Keystone Defenda=
nts'
Answer is denied.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>3. DDR's Cross-Motions for Sanct=
ions
Are Denied</span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3HK90K58R00030000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3HK90K58R00050000400"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFc=
lscc34"></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>A
pleading or motion violates </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5GYC-1WP1-6N19-F0YT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Rule 11</span=
></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
when it &quot;has been interposed for any improper purpose, or where, after
reasonable inquiry, a competent attorney could not form a reasonable belief
that the pleading is well-grounded in fact and warranted by existing law or=
 a
good faith argument for the extension, modification or reversal of existing
law.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3HK90K58R00020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4P9T-DXN0-TXFR-J23V-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Abdelhamid v.
Altria Grp., Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4P9T-DXN0-TXFR-J23V-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 515 F. Supp=
. 2d
384, 391 (S.D.N.Y. 2007)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",s=
erif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-styl=
e:
normal'>see also</i> </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5GYC-1WP1-6N19-F0YT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Fed. R. Civ. =
P.
11(b)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-fo=
nt-family:
Times;color:black'>. The rule &quot;establishes an objective standard, inte=
nded
to eliminate any 'empty-head pure-heart' &nbsp;[**90]&nbsp;justification for
patently frivolous arguments.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52M3HK90K58R00040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3X29-DTB0-0038-X2RY-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Simon DeBarto=
lo
Grp., L.P. v. Richard E. Jacobs Grp., Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3X29-DTB0-0038-X2RY-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 186 F.3d 15=
7,
166 (2d Cir. 1999)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. &quot;The extent to which a
litigant has researched the issues and found some support for its theories =
even
in minority opinions, in law review articles, or through consultation with
other attorneys should certainly be taken into account.&quot; <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal0 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>DDR
seeks sanctions against the First Keystone Defendants concerning their answ=
er
and counterclaims, and seeks leave to pursue sanctions against the Schlesin=
ger
Defendants concerning their time-bar argument regarding DDR's RICO claims.
Having reviewed the parties' submissions, the Court is prepared to give the
First Keystone and Schlesinger Defendants, and their counsel, the benefit of
the doubt. First, concerning the Schlesinger Defendants' statute of limitat=
ions
argument, Schlesinger counsel appears simply to have misunderstood what DDR
alleged as RICO predicate acts. (<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Se=
e</i>
Schlesinger Defs.' Mem. at 20.) Second, concerning the First Keystone
Defendants' answer and counterclaims, the Court neither finds that pleading=
 so
frivolous as to warrant sanctioning nor finds DDR's conclusory argument on =
the
point compelling. &nbsp;[**91]&nbsp;Thus the Court denies DDR's cross-motion
for sanctions against the First Keystone Defendants and DDR's cross-motion =
for
leave to seek sanctions against the Schlesinger Defendants.</span></p>

