<p class=3DNormal1 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4G85C52D4H00079JF400172"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52MT75V0K45DM0020000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The Court set forth the details =
of
the Plaintiffs' allegations in this matter in its previous decision in this
case, </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52MT75V0K45DM0010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4V8B-1FD0-TXFR-J1V2-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Allstate
Insurance Co. v. Rozenberg</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4V8B-1FD0-TXFR-J1V2-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 590 F. Supp=
. 2d
384 (E.D.N.Y. 2008)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. Although familiarity with the
factual background and procedural history of this case is assumed, a brief
review is in order.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal1 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>On
February 12, 2008, the Plaintiffs, a group of nine insurers, commenced this
action against Inna Polack, Alexander Polack, Natalya Shvartsman (&quot;the
Initial Management Defendants&quot;), Mighty Management Group, Inc., Mighty
Management LLC, and Blue Wave Management, Inc. (&quot;the Initial Management
Companies&quot;), Dr. Alexander Rozenberg (&quot;Rozenberg&quot;), and A.R.
Medical Rehabilitation, P.C. (&quot;AR&quot;), A.R. Medical Art, P.C.
(&quot;ARMA&quot;), and Yonkers Medical Art, P.C. (&quot;YMA&quot; and toge=
ther
with AR and ARMA &quot;the PC Defendants&quot; and collectively with the
Initial Management Defendants, the Initial Management Companies, and Rozenb=
erg
&quot;the Initial Defendants&quot;), alleging that they conspired to abuse =
New
York's No-Fault Insurance regime, </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5CT3-11P1-6RDJ-84H4-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>N.Y. Ins. Law
&sect; 5101 et seq.</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, in order to obtain
&nbsp;[**5]&nbsp;payment for medical services and diagnostic tests that were
not medically necessary, or in some cases, never performed at all (the
&quot;Initial Complaint&quot;). With the exception of ARMA and YMA, all of =
the
Initial Defendants were also subject to a criminal indictment with respect =
to
their participation in the allegedly fraudulent scheme.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal1 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>As
stated in previous decisions, the basics of the alleged scheme are as follo=
ws.
The PC Defendants are medical professional corporations that billed the
Plaintiffs for consultations and medical procedures performed upon patients
insured by the Plaintiffs. According to the Plaintiffs, Rozenberg, a licens=
ed
neurologist, was listed as the owner of the PC Defendants, but played no ro=
le
in the actual operation or management of the PC Defendants. Rather, in the
Initial Complaint, the Plaintiffs asserted that the PC Defendants were owned
and operated by the Initial Management Companies; namely, New York corporat=
ions
that are owned and controlled by Yuliy Goldman, Inna Polack and Alexander
Polack. The Plaintiffs alleged that the sole purpose of the relationship be=
tween
the PC Defendants and the Initial Management Companies was to facilitate a
scheme to defraud the &nbsp;[**6]&nbsp;Plaintiffs by creating and submitting
fraudulent medical reports and invoices for medical services in
&nbsp;[*259]&nbsp; support of hundreds of No-Fault insurance claims. The
Plaintiffs also alleged that Inna Polack, Alexander Polack, and Rozenberg
created the PC Defendants with different names, addresses, and taxpayer
identification numbers to reduce the likelihood that insurers would uncover
their scheme.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal1 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
particular, the Plaintiffs asserted that the Initial Defendants submitted b=
ills
for services not rendered; charged excessive fees for unnecessary medical
treatment; and induced Allstate and the other insurers to pay No-Fault
insurance claims to professional medical corporations that were owned by
non-licensed individuals. The Plaintiffs further alleged that checks were d=
rawn
from the accounts of the Initial Management Companies and made payable to
corporations owned or controlled by Emmanuel Kucherovsky (the &quot;money
laundering entities&quot;) who, for a transaction fee, transferred these mo=
nies
to Inna Polack.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal1 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
the Initial Complaint, the Plaintiffs alleged that the Initial Defendants (=
i)
violated RICO,</span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
1962(c)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>; (ii) engaged in a RICO conspiracy in violation of </sp=
an><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
1962(d)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>; (iii) committed &nbsp;[**7]&nbsp;common law fraud and
unjust enrichment; and (iv) were liable under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6HKK-NR83-SHV7-X0WS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>N.Y. Gen. Bus=
. L.
&sect; 349</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-farea=
st-font-family:
Times;color:black'> for deceptive business practices. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52MT75V0K45DM0040000400"></a>The Initial Defendants filed
motions to dismiss the Initial Complaint in April and June of 2008. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4G85C559S700079JF40017R"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52MT75X0K45F70010000400"></a>By order dated December 29, =
2008,
this Court denied the motions as to all counts with the exception of the ca=
use
of action alleging a RICO conspiracy under the Innocent Enterprise Theory. =
<u>See
generally </u></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I52MT75V0K45DM0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4V8B-1FD0-TXFR-J1V2-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Allstate
Insurance Co. v. Rozenberg</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4V8B-1FD0-TXFR-J1V2-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 590 F. Supp=
. 2d
384 (E.D.N.Y. 2008)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I52MT75X0K45F70010000400_2"></a>In addition, by order dated
January 26, 2009, <a name=3D"Bookmark_I52MT75V0K45DM0050000400"></a><u>Alls=
tate
Ins. Co v. Rozenberg</u>, No. 08-CV-565, Docket No. 119 (E.D.N.Y. Jan. 26,
2009) (the &quot;January 26, 2009 Order&quot;) and subsequent amendments, t=
he
Court granted the Plaintiffs' requests for prejudgment attachments on the
assets of the Initial Defendants based upon a showing of a likelihood of
success on the merits and the existence of one or more of the enumerated
statutory grounds for attachment under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5CT3-08C1-6RDJ-8508-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>N.Y. C.P.L.R.
&sect; 6201</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fare=
ast-font-family:
Times;color:black'> (&quot;</span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5CT3-08C1-6RDJ-8508-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>CPLR &sect; 6=
201</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&quot;).</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal1 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
