6201(3)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>. Contrary to what has been provided for every other
Management Company, including First Neptune who was also an alleged owner a=
nd
manager of YMA (<u>Id.</u> at Ex. 7), in the Amended Complaint the Plaintif=
fs
have not specifically alleged, nor have they provided any evidence that
Sheynkman or Artek transferred any of the money they received from YMA to a=
ny
of the money laundering entities. Accordingly, the Court denies the Plainti=
ffs'
request for prejudgment attachment as to Sheynkman and Artek, without
prejudice.</span></p>

