<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>As
noted above, DiVittorio's complaint is framed almost entirely upon informat=
ion
and belief, with one irrelevant exception. Further, at least with respect to
the federal claims, derelictions are pleaded against the defendants general=
ly,
with little or no specification as to individual roles. For the reasons
discussed below, we conclude that these defects are not fatal with respect =
to
plaintiff's claims against certain of the &nbsp;[*1248]&nbsp; Equidyne
defendants; with respect to the remaining&nbsp;[**16]&nbsp; defendants, how=
ever,
we hold that the complaint was properly dismissed. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
