if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Rule 9(b)</sp=
an></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
where they assert, for example, that although offering memorandum represent=
ed
that general partners would make capital contributions of $ 385,000 to
partnership, they actually contributed $ 80,000; and although memorandum
represented that cost of renovation project would be $ 4.5 million, liabili=
ties
for incomplete project exceeded $ 10.2 million at time of appeal). </span><=
/p>

<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FKGBJP0K1MNJ4YG0000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FKGBJP0K1MNJ4YJ0000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>We wish to stress, however, that=
 <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Luce</i> does not stand for the propos=
ition
that mere reliance on an offering memorandum or similar document satisfies a
pleader's burden under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5GYC-1WP1-6N19-F0YN-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Rule 9(b)</sp=
an></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>;
even there, we noted that &quot;many&quot; -- and thus not all -- claims
grounded on the offering memorandum were sufficiently pleaded. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FKGBJP0K1MNJ4YF0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-0JJ0-0039-P06C-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Luce</span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-0JJ0-0039-P06C-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 802 F.2d at=
 55</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
We noted that on remand, amendments of Luce's complaint &quot;relating to
projections or expectations offered to induce investments [whether or not t=
he
representations were contained in the offering memorandum] must allege
particular facts demonstrating the knowledge of defendants at the time that
such statements were false.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FKGBJP0K1MNJ4YH0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-0JJ0-0039-P06C-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Luce</span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-0JJ0-0039-P06C-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 802 F.2d at=
 57</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FKGBJP0K1MNJ5000000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>We turn next to the application =
of
these principles to specific Equidyne defendants. &nbsp;[**19]&nbsp; As not=
ed
earlier, </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4FKGBJP0K1MNJ4YY0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-0JJ0-0039-P06C-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Luce</span></=
i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-0JJ0-0039-P06C-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 802 F.2d at=
 55</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
does not require a specific connection between insiders or affiliates and
fraudulent representations in an offering memorandum. Even with the aid of =
this
rule, however, the amended complaint here is not adequate with respect to m=
ost
of the Equidyne defendants. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
amended complaint identifies Eastern only as an &quot;affiliate of the Gene=
ral
Partner, and the Contract Miner for the Partnership's coal properties,&quot;
para. 7; EDC as &nbsp;[*1249]&nbsp; &quot;an affiliate of the General Partn=
er,
and the [sic] co-contracting driller . . . for the development of the
Partnership's oil properties,&quot; para. 8; Eastland as &quot;an affiliate=
 of
the General Partner, which . . . sublet coal properties to the
Partnership,&quot; para. 9; and Properties as &quot;a subsidiary of Equidyn=
e .
. . [which] serves as a manager and syndicator of Equidyne real estate
investments,&quot; para. 11. These allegations are inadequate to charge the=
se
defendants with liability for misrepresentations in the Offering Memorandum=
. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>None
of the individual Equidyne defendants, Ross, Beeler, Rock and Liebmann, is =
tied
to the Offering Memorandum in any specific way, or even alleged to have bee=
n an
officer or director of any non-individual&nbsp;[**20]&nbsp; Equidyne defend=
ant
when the Offering Memorandum was issued or the specified class of plaintiffs
bought their limited partnership interests. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style=
:normal'>See</i>
Amended Complaint, paras. 12-15. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Some
of these defects might be curable. As stated earlier, however, we have
jurisdiction only because plaintiff made an irrevocable election, in the fa=
ce
of leave given below to amend the complaint further, to stand or fall on the
amended complaint in its present form. Accordingly, that complaint can stand
only against the Partnership, the General Partner, and Equidyne. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>2) <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>The Lawyer Defendant, the Accountant
Defendants and Inland</i>. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
district court correctly dismissed the complaint under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5GYC-1WP1-6N19-F0YN-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Rule 9(b)</sp=
an></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> as
to these defendants. No allegations in the amended complaint are sufficient=
 to
describe any of them as insiders or affiliates, and there is no allegation
linking any of them in any specific way to any fraudulent misrepresentation=
 or
omission. </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>III.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>CONCLUSION </span></p>

<p class=3DNormal5 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
order of the district court dismissing the complaint is affirmed as to all
defendants except the Partnership, the General Partner and Equidyne, as to =
whom
we reverse and remand for further proceedings consistent herewith. Plaintiff
should be allowed no&nbsp;[**21]&nbsp; further opportunity to amend his
complaint (except as necessary to conform hereto), in view of his election =
to
stand upon the present amended complaint.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&=
