<p class=3DNormal7 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc6_5"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",se=
rif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The Act defines
&quot;enterprise&quot; to &quot;include[] any individual, partnership,
corporation, association, or other legal entity, and any union or group of
individuals associated in fact although not a legal entity.&quot; </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
1961(4)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>. Although the statute does &nbsp;[**10]&nbsp;not define=
 the
outer boundaries of &nbsp;[*368]&nbsp; what constitutes an enterprise, it is
clear that partnerships, corporations, and &quot;other legal entit[ies],&qu=
ot;
as well as associations-in-fact, may be RICO enterprises. In this case,
Allstate alleges that, in each cluster, the PC, a legal entity, constituted=
 the
relevant enterprise under RICO. Compl. &para;&para; 550, 575, 600, 625, 650,
675, 700, 725.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal7 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
moving defendants argue that Allstate has failed to adequately plead an
&quot;enterprise&quot; for three reasons. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF7528T42K0040000400"></a>First, defendants charge tha=
t an
entity whose sole function is fraud may not be an enterprise under RICO, and
defendants argue that the PCs' only alleged function was fraud. They appear=
 to
suggest that when the sole function of an enterprise is fraud, the
&quot;enterprise&quot; element and &quot;pattern of racketeering activity&q=
uot;
element impermissibly merge. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752N1RCP0010000400">=
</a>This
objection is easily dispensed with; the Supreme Court has made clear that <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc7_4"></a>a wholly illegitimate enterprise, jus=
t like
a legitimate enterprise, may constitute an enterprise under RICO. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF7528T42K0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Turkette</spa=
n></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 452 U.S. 57=
6,
101 S. Ct. 2524, 69 L. Ed. 2d 246</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:=
"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752N1RCP0010000400_2"></a>The elements of
&quot;enterprise&quot; and &quot;pattern of racketeering activity&quot; rem=
ain
distinct elements under RICO, even when the allegations and proof of those
elements &nbsp;[**11]&nbsp;overlap. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF7528T42K0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id</span></i>=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-69X0-003B-S0DS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>. at 583</spa=
n></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal7 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752N1RCP0030000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Second, defendants contend that =
the
Complaint fails to appropriately plead an association-in-fact enterprise.</=
span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn125' href=3D"#_ftn125" name=3D"_ftnref125" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>4</span><=
/sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
However, Allstate has not alleged an association-in-fact enterprise. The
alleged enterprises are the PCs, and <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc8_4"><=
/a>corporations
are expressly included in the definition of enterprise. <i style=3D'mso-bid=
i-font-style:
normal'>See</i> </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:65TD-2HT3-GXF6-804J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
1961(4)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>see also </i><=
/span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752N1RCP0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4DDR-B9V0-0038-X2CF-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>First Capital
Asset Mgmt., Inc. v. Satinwood, Inc</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4DDR-B9V0-0038-X2CF-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
