Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Finally, defendants maintain that
the Complaint &nbsp;[**12]&nbsp;runs afoul of the rule that a RICO enterpri=
se
be distinct from the person(s) charged with conducting the affairs of the
enterprise under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 1962(c=
)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See </i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752HM6T30010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4DDR-B9V0-0038-X2CF-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Satinwood</sp=
an></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4DDR-B9V0-0038-X2CF-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 385 F.3d at=
 173</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
They suggest because the defendants charged with the RICO violations (<i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>i.e</i>., the paper owners, the actual
owners, and Lyons) are all employees of the charged RICO enterprises (<i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>i.e</i>., the PCs), the defendants are=
 not
distinct from the enterprises.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal7 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>This
argument misapprehends either the state of the law or the allegations of the
Complaint. For each of the RICO claims, the Complaint alleges that, within =
each
cluster, the PC constitutes the relevant enterprise. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752HM6T30040000400"></a>The paper owners, the actual
owners, and Lyons are the named defendants; in other words, they are allege=
d to
be the persons who conducted the affairs of the enterprises. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc10_4"></a>That a RICO defendant is employed by=
 the
alleged corporate enterprise does not violate the distinctness rule because=
 an
employee of a corporation and the corporation are not the same entity. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752D6MYC0010000400"></a>Rather, a &quot;corporate
owner/employee, a natural person, is distinct from the corporation itself, a
legally different entity with different rights and responsibilities due to =
its
different legal status.&quot; &nbsp;[**13]&nbsp;</span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752HM6T30030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:437X-B220-004C-0032-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Cedric Kushner
Promotions, Ltd. v. King</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:437X-B220-004C-0032-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 533 U.S. 15=
8,
163, 121 S. Ct. 2087, 150 L. Ed. 2d 198 (2001)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752D6MYC0010000400_2"></a>RICO's distinctness rule i=
s thus
satisfied &quot;when a &nbsp;[*369]&nbsp; corporate employee [the RICO
defendant] unlawfully conducts the affairs of the corporation&quot; alleged=
 to
constitute the RICO enterprise. </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752HM6T30050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:437X-B220-004C-0032-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id</span></i>=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:437X-B220-004C-0032-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>. at 166</spa=
n></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal7 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752D6MYC0030000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>It is true that the situation mi=
ght
be different if the Complaint named a corporation as the RICO <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>defendant</i> and then alleged that the
corporation together with its own employees constituted an association-in-f=
act
enterprise. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See </i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752D6MYC0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:437X-B220-004C-0032-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>id</span></i>=
</a><a
