<p class=3DNormal7 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752N1RCT0010000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The case before me is easily
distinguishable. Allstate is not seeking redress for an uncollectible debt;
rather, &nbsp;[**30]&nbsp;it seeks damages for paying millions of dollars to
defendants based upon their allegedly fraudulent claims for no-fault benefi=
ts.
In such a case, I find that Allstate's damages are clear and definite, and
defendants have directed me to no authority that leads me to believe otherw=
ise.</span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn129' href=3D"#_ftn129" name=3D"_ftnref129" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>8</span><=
/sup></a></p>

<p class=3DNormal7 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>e. <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>RICO Conspiracy</i></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal7 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Defendants
suggest that I must dismiss Allstate's RICO conspiracy claims because the
substantive RICO claims are defective. Because I find that the substantive =
RICO
claims are legally sufficient, defendants' argument fails. Defendants make =
no
other attack on Allstate's RICO conspiracy claims.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal7 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>3. <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Common Law Fraud</i></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal7 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc23_2"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752N1RCT00=
30000400"></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
order to plead a claim for New York common law fraud, a plaintiff must alle=
ge
that the defendant made a material misrepresentation of a fact, with knowle=
dge
of its falsity and an intent to induce reliance, that the plaintiff justifi=
ably
&nbsp;[**31]&nbsp;relied on defendant's misrepresentation, and that the
plaintiff suffered damages. </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752N1RCT002000=
0400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:7VW0-M8Y1-2R6J-246H-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Eurycleia
Partners, LP v. Seward &amp; Kissel, LLP</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:7VW0-M8Y1-2R6J-246H-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 12 N.Y.3d 5=
53,
559, 910 N.E.2d 976, 883 N.Y.S.2d 147 (2009)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
In this case, the Complaint alleges that the defendants defrauded Allstate =
by
misrepresenting in their no-fault claims (1) that they were eligible to rec=
eive
reimbursement under the no-fault &nbsp;[*375]&nbsp; law and (2) that they w=
ere
requesting reimbursement for services that were medically necessary and
compensable. Compl. &para;&para; 739-42. Allstate alleges that defendants m=
ade
these representations with knowledge of their falsity and with the purpose =
of
inducing Allstate to pay those claims, that Allstate reasonably relied on
defendants' misrepresentations, and that Allstate incurred damages as a res=
ult.
<i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id</i>. &para;&para; 743-45.</span>=
</p>

<p class=3DNormal7 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Defendants
claim that Allstate has failed to plead fraud because it has not properly
alleged justifiable reliance. According to defendants, because Allstate is a
&quot;sophisticated insurer,&quot; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>=
see</i>
Defs.' Mem. Supp. Mot. Dismiss 21, ECF No. 80, it had the ability to detect
defendants' alleged fraud and is therefore precluded from arguing that it
justifiably relied on their alleged misrepresentations.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal7 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752N1RCT0050000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>I emphatically reject this notio=
n. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc24_2"></a>Reliance &nbsp;[**32]&nbsp;is unjust=
ified
if &quot;the misrepresentation allegedly relied upon was not a matter within
the peculiar knowledge of the party against whom the fraud is asserted, and
could have been discovered by the party allegedly defrauded through the
exercise of due diligence.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752N1RCT0040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RH6-S1X0-0039-4287-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Cohen v. Ceri=
er</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RH6-S1X0-0039-4287-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 243 A.D.2d =
670,
663 N.Y.S. 2d 643, 644 (App. Div. 1997)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-f=
amily:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. Even assuming th=
at
this is the kind of case in which due diligence was required by Allstate
&#8212; a dubious assumption &#8212; the defendants' fraud in this case was
sophisticated and deep and could not have been discovered with such diligen=
ce.
The suggestion that Allstate bore the responsibility to discover that
defendants had covertly allotted ownership and control of the PCs to
non-physicians is absurd. Allstate was entitled to rely on the representati=
ons
that defendants made to it and to the New York Department of State regarding
the ownership of the PCs. It is similarly incorrect to claim that Allstate =
was
remiss in relying on defendants' facially reasonable diagnoses and claims f=
or
payment and failing to uncover their falsity. In short, regardless of the s=
trength
of Allstate's investigatory capabilities, it is not barred from asserting f=
raud
claims solely for failing to &nbsp;[**33]&nbsp;detect &#8212; within the
no-fault law's 30-day window, no less &#8212; the complex fraudulent schemes
attributed to defendants here. Allstate has adequately pled the element of
justifiable reliance.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal7 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>For
the reasons addressed elsewhere in this order, I further conclude that
Allstate's claims for fraud are pled with the requisite specificity and are
otherwise sufficient.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal7 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>4. <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Consumer Protection Claims</i></span><=
/p>

<p class=3DNormal7 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc25_2"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752HM6T600=
20000400"></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Under
</span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6HKK-NR83-SHV7-X0WS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 349 of=
 the
New York General Business Law</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Tim=
es",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, it is unlawful to engage in
&quot;[d]eceptive acts or practice in the conduct of any business, trade or
commerce or in the furnishing of any service&quot; in New York. </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6HKK-NR83-SHV7-X0WS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>N.Y. Gen. Bus=
. L.
&sect; 349(a)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fa=
reast-font-family:
Times;color:black'>. Although similar to fraud claims in many ways, </span>=
<a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6HKK-NR83-SHV7-X0WS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>&sect; 349</s=
pan></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
claims are unique in that they &quot;must be predicated on a deceptive act =
or
practice that is 'consumer oriented.'&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752HM6T60010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3Y52-5JC0-0039-455G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Gaidon v.
Guardian Life Ins. Co. of Am</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3Y52-5JC0-0039-455G-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>., 94 N.Y.2d =
330,
344, 725 N.E.2d 598, 704 N.Y.S.2d 177 (1999)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(quoting </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I554PF752HM6T60030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S2R-6F40-003V-B43S-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Oswego Labore=
rs'
Local 214 Pension Fund v. Marine Midland Bank</span></i></a><a
