if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Schmuck v. Un=
ited
States</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-BVS0-003B-4333-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 489 U.S. 70=
5,
57 U.S.L.W. 4362, 103 L. Ed. 2d 734, 109 S. Ct. 1443 (1989)</span></i></a><=
span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,&nbsp;[**34]&nbsp;
the defendant purchased used cars, rolled back their odometers, and then so=
ld
the cars to retail dealers at inflated prices. <a
