<p class=3DNormal13 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
appeal in this Title VII suit challenges the denial of a motion to vacate t=
he
judgment of dismissal and to file a first amended complaint. After the
complaint was dismissed for failure to state a claim, plaintiffs pursued a
hotly contested appeal, which resulted in a split panel decision in this Co=
urt
affirming the dismissal, and an <u>in banc</u> petition that was ultimately
denied over the dissent of five judges. Plaintiffs then asked the district
court to vacate the judgment of dismissal so they could (attempt to) cure t=
he
pleading deficiencies.</span></p>

