<p class=3DNormal13 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I69VS1PF2SF89S0040000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The district court seemingly gav=
e no
weight to the viability of Plaintiffs' proposed amendment because it was ba=
sed
on information that was publicly available for years prior to the filing of=
 the
Complaint. Even assuming the information was obtainable, standing alone tha=
t is
not a basis for depriving Plaintiffs of a first opportunity to add allegati=
ons
that render their claim plausible. <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc13_7"></=
a>As
the Supreme Court has explained, when &quot;the underlying facts or
circumstances relied upon by a plaintiff may be a proper subject of relief,=
 he
ought to be afforded an opportunity to test his claim on the merits.&quot; =
</span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I69VS1PF2SF89S0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-H6D0-003B-S3WS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Foman</span><=
/i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-H6D0-003B-S3WS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 371 U.S. at=
 182</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>; <u>see
also </u></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I69VS1PF2SF89S0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-FMC0-008H-V0D1-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
