at 425-26</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareas=
t-font-family:
Times;color:black'>. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I5RY2WC628T4S50050000400_2"></a>Th=
erefore,
Kim's claims &quot;were not foreclosed a priori by binding precedent even if
they were unlikely to succeed&quot; and Kim's position &quot;was not
unsupported by case law even though the cases he cited were not binding on =
the
court adjudicating his claims.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5RY2WC628T4S50040000400"></a><a
