427
(NGG)(RML), 2014 U.S. Dist. LEXIS 135758, 2014 WL 4773991, at *8 (E.D.N.Y. =
Sep.
24, 2014)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareas=
t-font-family:
Times;color:black'>, and therefore Trilegiant may have perpetrated a fraud
despite the presence of disclosures on its enrollment page. But <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc3_14"></a>to show that customers may have been
misled, the plaintiff must produce evidence that particular statements are
deceptive when considered in context. <u>Cf. </u></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5SCRJDP2HM61T0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4PCS-P8M0-TXFX-42DR-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
