:contentItem:5JV8-2DW1-F04K-J034-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 822 F.3d at=
 657</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
That is so notwithstanding characterization of the alleged frauds as predic=
ate
acts of a racketeering conspiracy.</span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn260'
href=3D"#_ftn260" name=3D"_ftnref260" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-f=
amily:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>6</span></sup></a><span style=3D'font-family=
:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> The complaint here lacks the
particularized allegation of an underlying &quot;scheme to defraud&quot;
animated by a material misrepresentation.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>For
example, the complaint alleges that consumers were &quot;duped into
believing&quot; that the membership programs were being offered by an
e-merchant, rather than Trilegiant, App'x at 282, but identifies no
misrepresentation that induced such a belief. Similarly, the complaint labe=
ls
datapass a &quot;fraudulent tactic,&quot; <u>id.</u>, and alleges that each
time an e-merchant shared a customer's billing information with Trilegiant,
both the e-merchant and Trilegiant &quot;committed an act of wire fraud,&qu=
ot; <u>id.</u>
at 308. But the transfer of billing information from one merchant to anothe=
r is
not inherently fraudulent, and the plaintiffs do not identify any
misrepresentation regarding such transfers by Trilegiant or any other
defendant.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&nbsp;[*126]&nbsp;
<a name=3D"Bookmark_I5SCRJDP2N1RG50030000400"></a>Neither the complaint's
specific discussion of Trilegiant's allegedly deceptive
tactics,&nbsp;[**17]&nbsp; nor its conclusory references to Trilegiant's
fraudulent scheme, set forth a material misrepresentation with the requisite
particularity.</span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn261' href=3D"#_ftn261"
name=3D"_ftnref261" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",seri=
f;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>7</span></sup></a><span style=3D'font-family=
:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> <u>Cf. </u></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5SCRJDP2N1RG50020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5MF7-XJ31-F04K-J0FJ-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Webloyalty.co=
m</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5MF7-XJ31-F04K-J0FJ-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 673 F. App'=
x at
104</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font=
-family:
Times;color:black'> (concluding that Trilegiant's practices at issue in that
case not &quot;sufficient to ground [a] fraud claim&quot;). The complaint
therefore fails to plead a scheme to defraud. Without an underlying scheme =
to
defraud, the plaintiffs have not alleged a pattern of racketeering.</span><=
/p>

<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5SCRJDP28T44Y0030000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The plaintiffs' RICO conspiracy
claim fails as well. The alleged conspiracy involved an agreement to commit=
 the
same substantive RICO violations we have deemed insufficiently pled, and the
plaintiffs have not alleged any further acts that, if carried out, would ha=
ve
satisfied RICO's requirement of a pattern of racketeering. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5SCRJDP28T44Y0050000400"></a><u>See generally </u></span>=
<a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5SCRJDP28T44Y0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RHK-1090-004C-300F-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Salinas v. Un=
ited
States</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RHK-1090-004C-300F-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 522 U.S. 52,
118 S. Ct. 469, 139 L. Ed. 2d 352 (1997)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-=
family:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. The plaintiffs
therefore failed to plead the necessary agreement to violate RICO's substan=
tive
provisions. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I5SCRJDP28T44Y0050000400_2"></a><u>See </u>=
</span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5SCRJDP28T44Y0040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3X3J-CFS0-0038-X33R-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Cofacredit S.=
A.
v. Windsor Plumbing Supply Co.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3X3J-CFS0-0038-X33R-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 187 F.3d 22=
9,
245 (2d Cir. 1999)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>IV</span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Finally,
we affirm the grant of summary judgment on the CUTPA and unjust enrichment
claims substantially for the reasons set forth by the district court.</span=
></p>

<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc11_11"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",=
serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>CUTPA prohibits &quot;unfair or
deceptive acts or practices in the conduct of any trade or commerce.&quot; =
</span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:56C1-2X71-648C-K4N3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Conn. Gen. St=
at.
Sec. 42-110b(a)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. The plaintiffs allege that
Trilegiant's&nbsp;[**18]&nbsp; refund mitigation strategy caused them to lo=
se a
portion of a possible refund of membership fees. But the plaintiffs, who
consented to their original enrollment, have not shown that they are entitl=
ed
to any such refund. The fact that some plaintiffs were offered less than a =
full
refund to which they would not have been entitled at law cannot constitute =
an
&quot;unfair or deceptive&quot; act.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
district court was likewise correct in granting summary judgment on the unj=
ust
enrichment claim. An unjust enrichment claim for membership fees does not l=
ie
if the plaintiff freely entered into the membership agreement. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5SCRJDP2D6NB20020000400"></a>The plaintiffs further claim=
 that
the refund mitigation technique caused Trilegiant to retain an unfair benef=
it
by offering only partial refunds. But as with their failed CUTPA claim, they
cannot argue that Trilegiant was unjustly enriched by not refunding additio=
nal,
legitimate past membership fees to which its customers were not entitled. <=
u>See,
e.g., </u></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5SCRJDP2D6NB20010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5BF4-YPY1-F04K-V4T7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Berger v. Home
Depot USA, Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5BF4-YPY1-F04K-V4T7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 741 F.3d 10=
61,
1070 (9th Cir. 2014)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (requiring &quot;unjust retenti=
on
of [a] benefit&quot; as an element of an unjust enrichment claim).</span></=
p>

<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>CONCLUSION</span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal15 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>For
the foregoing reasons, we hereby <b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>A=
FFIRM</b>
the judgment of the district court.</span></p>

