shoes, was the only defendant.</span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn351'
href=3D"#_ftn351" name=3D"_ftnref351" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-f=
amily:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>88</span></sup></a><span style=3D'font-famil=
y:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> In answering that
question, the district court found that although &quot;the level of involve=
ment
and seriousness with which several Committee members treated their fiduciary
duty [was] troubling, [the court] does not find that this rose to a level o=
f failure
to fulfill fiduciary obligations. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I63DBHNP2HM66D0010000=
400_2"></a>Between
[the investment advisor firm's] advice and the guidance of the more
well-equipped Committee members . . . , the Court is persuaded that the
Committee performed its role adequately.&quot;</span><a style=3D'mso-footno=
te-id:
ftn352' href=3D"#_ftn352" name=3D"_ftnref352" title=3D""><sup><span style=
=3D'font-family:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>89</span></sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> In
our view, this passage means only that, while certain constituent members of
