<p class=3DNormal16 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>We
therefore vacate the denial of leave to amend and remand for consideration
under the correct legal standard. We also vacate the denial of plaintiffs' =
</span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5GYC-22N1-6N19-F032-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Rule 52(b)</s=
pan></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
and </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:5GYC-2421-6N19-F16C-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>59(e)</span><=
/i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
post-trial motions; those motions sought findings specific to Meagher and
Sanchez, and so, depending on how the motion to amend is disposed of on rem=
and,
those motions may require further consideration as well.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal16 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>III. Plaintiffs waived their jury
demand</span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal16 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I63DBHNP2HM66D0050000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Plaintiffs argue that they had a=
 </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8T9R-T4S2-D6RV-H37V-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Seventh Amend=
ment</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
right to a trial by jury, and therefore&nbsp;[**39]&nbsp; that the district
court erred in striking their jury demand. We disagree. The record of
proceedings before the district court makes clear that plaintiffs waived th=
eir
jury demand.</span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn354' href=3D"#_ftn354"
name=3D"_ftnref354" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",seri=
f;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>91</span></sup></a><span style=3D'font-famil=
y:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> Accordingly, we n=
eed
not address the substance of their </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8T9R-T4S2-D6RV-H37V-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Seventh Amend=
ment</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
argument.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal16 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>On
December 4, 2017, NYU moved to strike plaintiffs' jury demand. Under the
Southern District of New York's local rules, plaintiffs' opposition to NYU =
's
motion was due within fourteen days.</span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn3=
55'
href=3D"#_ftn355" name=3D"_ftnref355" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-f=
amily:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>92</span></sup></a><span style=3D'font-famil=
y:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> On December 19, o=
ne
day after the deadline for plaintiffs to file a response had expired, the
district court granted NYU's motion to strike. Plaintiffs now argue that we
should excuse their failure to respond to NYU's motion as &quot;inadvertent=
[].&quot;</span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn356' href=3D"#_ftn356" name=3D"_ftnref356" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>93</span>=
</sup></a><span
