ct;
1962(b)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>; and (5) she has adequately pleaded that all six defend=
ants
violated </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>18 U.S.C. &se=
ct;
1962(c)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>. Accordingly, we VACATE the District Court's judgment
dismissing in full Virginia's RICO claim and related state law claims both =
as
brought on her own behalf and as Executrix, and we REMAND the cause for fur=
ther
proceedings in accordance with this opinion.</span></p>

