<p class=3DNormal17 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>DISCUSSION</span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal17 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Virginia
contends that several aspects of the District Court's ruling are flawed. She
identifies error in the court's determination that her lost debt damages we=
re
not yet ripe. She also argues that, contrary to the District Court's
conclusion, the facts set forth in&nbsp;[**23]&nbsp; the Complaint are
sufficient to establish that she suffered an &quot;acquisition or maintenan=
ce
injury&quot; as required by </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>section 1962(=
b)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
and that Defendants were associated with an &quot;enterprise&quot; as requi=
red
to pursue recovery under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>section 1962(=
c)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Defendants, for their part, defend the District Court's ruling on ripeness =
as
to the lost debt injury, and, predictably, if cursorily, attack it as to
collection expense damages. They further adopt the District Court's analysi=
s of
the Complaint's insufficiency with respect to claims based on </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>sections 1962=
(b)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
and </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>(c)</span></i=
></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
and they maintain in addition, in a ground rejected by the District Court, =
that
Virginia's asserted injuries were not proximately caused by their actions,
making dismissal correct in their view for several independent reasons.</sp=
an></p>

<p class=3DNormal17 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H52D6NW60050000400"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFc=
lscc3_15"></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>We
review the District Court's ruling de novo, construing the facts alleged in=
 the
Complaint in the light most favorable to Virginia, and drawing all reasonab=
le
inferences in her favor. </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H52D6NW6004000040=
0"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:58P9-74D1-F04K-J00C-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Cruz v.
FXDirectDealer, LLC</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:58P9-74D1-F04K-J00C-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 720 F.3d 11=
5,
118 (2d Cir. 2013)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. On such review, we conclude th=
at
the District Court correctly determined that Virginia's claim for her share=
 of
the Estate's assets is unripe and that her claim for collection expenses is
ripe. We also determine that Virginia has sufficiently alleged that her
collection expense&nbsp;[**24]&nbsp; injuries were proximately caused by the
claimed RICO violations. In contrast to the District Court, we rule that
Virginia has sufficiently identified a distinct acquisition and maintenance
injury under </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>section 1962(=
b)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'> to
support her collection expenses claim with regard to David, Gregory Garvey,
&nbsp;[*93]&nbsp; and Red Knot, but not with regard to the other defendants=
. We
further conclude that Virginia has also sufficiently alleged a </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>section 1962(=
c)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
&quot;enterprise&quot; with regard to all six defendants, supporting her cl=
aim
for collection expenses on this theory of recovery as well. For these reaso=
ns,
we vacate the District Court's dismissal as to Virginia's RICO claim on her=
 own
behalf and on behalf of her mother's estate for collection expenses and rem=
and
that claim and her state law claims for further proceedings consistent with
this opinion.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal17 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times"=
,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>I. Ripeness of private actions
brought under RICO</span></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal17 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H528T4NS0020000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6GBJN4WXX600005X060000G"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H52N1PRJ0010000400"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFc=
lscc4_15"></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Our
Circuit's statutory ripeness jurisprudence in the RICO context grows from t=
he
Supreme Court's decision in </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H528T4NS001000=
0400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-DRC0-003B-S48H-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Zenith Radio
Corp. v. Hazeltine Research, Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-DRC0-003B-S48H-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 401 U.S. 32=
1,
91 S. Ct. 795, 28 L. Ed. 2d 77 (1971)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-fam=
ily:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, in which the Cou=
rt
ruled&#8212;in the context of a private action for treble damages recovery
under the </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8S9D-W4V2-8T6X-74X3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Sherman Act</=
span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>&#8212;that
a cause of action has not accrued when &quot;the fact of [future damages] is
speculative or their amount and nature unprovable.&quot;&nbsp;[**25]&nbsp; =
</span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H528T4NS0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-DRC0-003B-S48H-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-DRC0-003B-S48H-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> at 339</span=
></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>; <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>see also</i> David B. Smith &amp; Terr=
ance
G. Reed, <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Civil RICO</i>, &para;
6.04[5][a] (Matthew Bender 2017). We have concluded that no civil RICO caus=
e of
action for treble damages accrues &quot;until the amount of damages becomes
clear and definite.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H528T4NS00500004=
00"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-5FN0-003B-P0RW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>First Nationw=
ide
Bank v. Gelt Funding Corp.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-5FN0-003B-P0RW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
