<p class=3DNormal17 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>A. <u>Distribution
of Estate assets: claim for &quot;lost debt&quot; injuries</u></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal17 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H52N1PRJ0050000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>We agree with the District Court
that Virginia's RICO claim for her rightful share of the Estate is not yet
ripe. <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc5_14"></a>Our Circuit has consistently
ruled in the RICO context that claims for &quot;lost debt&quot;
injuries&#8212;that is, for damages in the form of an owed, but
as-yet-uncollected, amount&#8212;are unripe when parallel proceedings to
collect the amount owed are ongoing in another forum. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6GBJN4X09200005X060000H"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H52SF7PN0020000400"></a>We have reasoned that, since
&quot;RICO [treble] damages are netted against recovery obtained from
collateral and other sources,&quot; the outcome of the parallel proceedings
could significantly affect the total amount owed in the case at bar, and th=
at this
fundamental uncertainty renders the claim not ready for adjudication. </spa=
n><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6GBJN4YDWJ00005X060000R"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6GBJN4Y9XG00005X060000N"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6GBJN4X3G600005X060000K"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H52SF7PN0040000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H52N1PRJ0040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4835-WTN0-0038-X47T-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Motorola Cred=
it
Corp. v. Uzan</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4835-WTN0-0038-X47T-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 322 F.3d 13=
0,
135-36 (2d Cir. 2003)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",seri=
f;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (finding unripe plaintiffs' RICO
claim for injury based&nbsp;[**26]&nbsp; on unpaid loans where plaintiffs h=
ad
not yet foreclosed on loan security and related arbitrations were pending).=
 <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H52SF7PN0040000400_2"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H52SF7PN0020000400_2"></a>Although some other courts=
 have
taken a different approach, <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>see, e.=
g., </i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H52SF7PN0010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-5400-006F-M065-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Grimmett v. B=
rown</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-5400-006F-M065-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 75 F.3d 506
(9th Cir. 1996)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>, our jurisprudence on this poin=
t is
long- and well-established. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See, e.=
g., </i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H52SF7PN0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-5FN0-003B-P0RW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>First Nationw=
ide
Bank</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-5FN0-003B-P0RW-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 27 F.3d at =
769</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(finding unripe RICO claims for injury arising from plaintiffs' loans to
defendant where, though information from defendants provided as a basis for=
 the
loans was alleged to be false, no default had yet occurred); </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H52SF7PN0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-FY30-003B-P52C-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Stochastic
Decisions, Inc. v. DiDomenico</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-FY30-003B-P52C-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 995 F.2d 11=
58,
1165-66 (2d Cir. 1993)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (finding unripe a RICO claim for
injury in amount of two state court judgments entered against defendant whe=
re
(1) one judgment was satisfied after initiation of RICO suit, and (2) second
judgment was &quot;likely to be fully satisfied&quot;); </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5T6X5H52HM5PK0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4W-Y060-001B-K0GT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Bankers Trust=
 Co.
v. Rhoades</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4W-Y060-001B-K0GT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 859 F.2d 10=
96,
1105-06 (2d Cir. 1988)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (RICO claim for lost debt injury
unripe because fraudulently transferred assets might yet be recovered during
