Influenced and Corrupt Organizations Act (&quot;RICO&quot;), 18 U.S.C. &sec=
t;
1961 et seq.</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-far=
east-font-family:
Times;color:black'>, alleging that they smuggled liquor into New York State,
depriving Empire of sales it would have otherwise made. The district court
granted defendants' </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:6CHH-WBV3-SCV7-1000-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Fed. R. Civ. =
P.
12(b)(6)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast=
-font-family:
Times;color:black'>&nbsp;[**1]&nbsp; motion to dismiss because, inter alia,=
 the
smuggling operation, as alleged, did not directly cause Empire to lose sale=
s,
and therefore Empire did not adequately allege proximate cause under RICO. =
We
hold that Empire's Amended Complaint did not adequately allege proximate ca=
use.
Accordingly, the judgment of the district court is AFFIRMED.</span></p>

