CHIN, <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Circuit Judge</i>:</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal20 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
this case, plaintiff-appellant John Kowalchuck sued his former employer,
defendant-appellee Metropolitan Transportation Authority (the &quot;MTA&quo=
t;),
under the </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SDD-0JP2-8T6X-73F9-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Federal
Employers' Liability Act (&quot;FELA&quot;), 45 U.S.C. &sect; 51 </span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SDD-0JP2-8T6X-73F9-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>et seq.</span=
></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
for injuries sustained while clearing snow at an MTA property. The MTA
requested a pre-motion conference to discuss its anticipated motion for sum=
mary
judgment. The district court granted the request. At the pre-motion confere=
nce,
the district court deemed the MTA's motion as having been made and denied i=
t.
Two years later, and only four days before trial was set to begin and witho=
ut
notice to either party, the district court reconsidered its previous denial=
 of
the motion and granted summary judgment in favor of the MTA, dismissing the
complaint. Kowalchuck was not given an opportunity to submit papers in
opposition to the motion.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal20 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>On
appeal, Kowalchuck argues that the district court erred when it <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>sua sponte</i> reconsidered its denial=
 of
summary judgment and granted summary judgment to the MTA, without giving him
notice or an opportunity to be heard. We agree. For the reasons set forth
below, we VACATE and REMAND.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal20 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>BACKGROUND</span></i></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal20 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>I.
The Facts</span></i></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal20 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>As
alleged in the complaint,&nbsp;[**3]&nbsp;</span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-i=
d:
ftn442' href=3D"#_ftn442" name=3D"_ftnref442" title=3D""><sup><span style=
=3D'font-family:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>1</span></sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
the facts may be summarized as follows: Kowalchuck was employed as a police
officer by the MTA. On January 27, 2015, during a shift, Kowalchuck shoveled
snow from an accessibility ramp at an MTA building. While pushing a shovel =
on
the ramp to clear the snow, he hit a raised edge of a wooden plank. Kowalch=
uck
felt a jolt, and sustained injuries to his shoulder, neck, and cervical spi=
ne.
On August 26, 2016, Kowalchuck retired from the MTA.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal20 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><br>
<b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>II.
Procedural History</span></i></b></p>

<p class=3DNormal20 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>On
April 8, 2017, Kowalchuck filed the complaint below. He alleged that the MT=
A's
