or
district courts to require parties to request a conference before filing a
motion and submit letters describing the grounds for the proposed motion. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6BFKS0N28T4K90030000400"></a><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-st=
yle:
normal'>See, e.g., </i></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I6BFKS0M2D6MY30050000400"=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-8JJ0-001B-K0PD-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Richardson
Greenshields Sec., Inc. v. Lau</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-8JJ0-001B-K0PD-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
