proceedings here is particularly troubling because Kowalchuck brings this c=
ase
under FELA, a statute that seeks to provide broad protection for workers
employed by railroads engaged in interstate commerce. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc11_13"></a>Indeed, the Supreme Court has relax=
ed the
standards for proving negligence in FELA cases. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I6BFKS0S2SF8RS0050000400"></a><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-st=
yle:
normal'>See </i></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I6BFKS0S2HM6YJ0030000400"></a><a
