k'>,
construing the complaint liberally, accepting all factual allegations in the
complaint as true, and drawing all reasonable inferences in the plaintiff[s=
']
favor.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J42D6NHJ0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:456H-9WR0-0038-X4H7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Chambers v. T=
ime
Warner, Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:456H-9WR0-0038-X4H7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 282 F.3d 14=
7,
152 (2d Cir. 2002)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. &quot;We review the district
court's denial of leave to amend the complaint for abuse of discretion.&quo=
t; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J42SF8760020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5GHD-XPY1-F04K-J085-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Loreley Fin.
(Jersey) No. 3 Ltd. v. Wells Fargo Secs., LLC</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5GHD-XPY1-F04K-J085-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 797 F.3d 16=
0,
169 (2d Cir. 2015)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal21 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>A.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal21 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J42SF8760050000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J52HM6TV0010000400"></a><a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFc=
lscc3_19"></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Under
New York law, &quot;[i]t is well settled that, if the parties to an agreeme=
nt
do not intend it to be binding upon them until it is reduced to writing and=
 <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>signed by both of them</i>, they are n=
ot
bound and may not be held liable until it has been written out and
signed.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J42SF8760040000400"></a><a
