:contentItem:3RRS-VX20-003C-C48N-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Scheck v. Fra=
ncis</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RRS-VX20-003C-C48N-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 26 N.Y.2d 4=
66,
260 N.E.2d 493, 494, 311 N.Y.S.2d 841 (N.Y. 1970)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(emphasis&nbsp;[**10]&nbsp; added); <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'=
>see </i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J528T4W50010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-5JJ0-003B-50P7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Jim Bouton Co=
rp.
v. Wm. Wrigley Jr. Co.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-5JJ0-003B-50P7-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 902 F.2d 10=
74,
1081 (2d Cir. 1990)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (&quot;New York follows the
generally accepted rule that when parties negotiating a proposed contract
express an intent not to be bound until their negotiations have culminated =
in
the execution of a formal contract, they cannot be held bound until that ev=
ent
has occurred.&quot;) (collecting cases, including </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J528T4W50030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RRS-VX20-003C-C48N-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Scheck</span>=
</i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>).
&quot;The point of these rules is to give parties the power to contract as =
they
please, so that they may, if they like, bind themselves orally or by inform=
al
letters, or that they may maintain 'complete immunity from all obligation'
until a written agreement is executed.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J528T4W50050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4W-TSM0-003B-G0RV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>R.G. Grp., In=
c v.
Horn &amp; Hardart Co.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4W-TSM0-003B-G0RV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 751 F.2d 69=
, 74
(2d Cir. 1984)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'> (quoting 1 A. Corbin, <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:n=
ormal'>Corbin
on Contracts</i> &sect; 30, at 98 (1963)).</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal21 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc4_19"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",s=
erif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>This Court has set out four fact=
ors</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal21 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bott=
om:0in;
margin-left:20.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:15.=
0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I1HPPHX39DJ00003HJ50003Y"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J52HM6TV0030000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>that help determine whether the
parties intended to be bound in the absence of a document executed by both
sides. The court is to consider (1) whether there has been an express
reservation of the right not to be bound in the absence of a writing; (2) w=
hether
there has been partial performance of the contract; (3) whether all of the
terms of the alleged contract have been agreed upon; and (4) whether the
agreement at issue is the type of contract that is usually committed to
writing.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal21 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J52HM6TV0030000400_2"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J52HM6TV0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CNX0-0039-P2M3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Winston v.
Mediafare Entm't Corp.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CNX0-0039-P2M3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 777 F.2d 78=
, 80
(2d Cir. 1985)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-f=
areast-font-family:
Times;color:black'>. In the present case, each of these factors
weighs&nbsp;[**11]&nbsp; in the Republic's favor.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal21 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J52HM6TV0050000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>First, &quot;indications in the
proposed settlement agreement that the parties did not intend to bind
themselves until the settlement had been signed&quot; must be given
&quot;considerable weight.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J52HM6TV0040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RJX-J6G0-0038-X089-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Ciaramella v.
Reader's Digest Ass'n</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RJX-J6G0-0038-X089-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 131 F.3d 32=
0,
324 (2d Cir. 1997)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. The text of the Instructions,
Master Settlement Agreement, and Agreement Schedule unambiguously require t=
he
Republic's countersignature and exchange of executed copies of an Agreement
Schedule before either party is bound.</span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ft=
n449'
href=3D"#_ftn449" name=3D"_ftnref449" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-f=
amily:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>2</span></sup></a><span style=3D'font-family=
:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> The Instructions &nbsp;[*831]&n=
bsp;
state that &quot;[h]olders may become a party to a Settlement Agreement by
executing and exchanging with the Republic a completed Agreement Schedule. =
. .
. [An] Agreement Schedule, when countersigned by the Republic, shall consti=
tute
a binding agreement between the parties . . . .&quot; Joint App. 90-91. The
Agreement Schedule states that &quot;[b]y executing counterparts of this
Agreement Schedule in the space provided below and exchanging those
counterparts, the parties agree to be bound by the terms of the Settlement
Agreement . . . .&quot; Joint App. 99. An Agreement Schedule must be signed=
 by
the Republic to identify the parties to any Master Settlement Agreement, wh=
ich
is &quot;made . . . between [the Republic] and the Holder identified in item
(i) of the Agreement&nbsp;[**12]&nbsp; Schedule signed by the parties in
connection with this Agreement (such Agreement Schedule, when executed and
exchanged by the Republic and the Holder, being an integral part of this
Settlement Agreement).&quot; Joint App. 92. By their own express terms, the
unexecuted agreements between the Republic and plaintiffs were not binding
contracts.</span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn450' href=3D"#_ftn450"
name=3D"_ftnref450" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",seri=
f;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>3</span></sup></a></p>

<p class=3DNormal21 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62N1RHC0040000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The second </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62N1RHC0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CNX0-0039-P2M3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Winston</span=
></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CNX0-0039-P2M3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> </span></i><=
/a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>factor
concerns &quot;whether there has been partial performance of the
contract.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62N1RHC0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CNX0-0039-P2M3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Winston</span=
></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CNX0-0039-P2M3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 777 F.2d at=
 80</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Plaintiffs argue that they partially performed the contract by representing=
 to
the district court that they had reached agreements in principle with the
Republic and that the Republic partially performed the contract by represen=
ting
to the district court that it had settled with other parties and seeking
vacatur of the <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>pari passu</i>
injunctions. These actions do not amount to partial performance of the
settlement agreements. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I1HPPHX81YD00003HJ50006K"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62SF87J0030000400"></a>Regardless of their
representations to the district court, plaintiffs did not withdraw their cl=
aims
against the Republic. The Republic did not make any payments to plaintiffs,=
 and
neither its settlements with other bondholders nor its efforts to vacate th=
e <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>pari passi</i> injunctions bear on its
intentions with respect to plaintiffs.&nbsp;[**13]&nbsp; The second </span>=
<a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62SF87J0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CNX0-0039-P2M3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Winston</span=
></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
factor thus weighs against plaintiffs.</span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ft=
n451'
href=3D"#_ftn451" name=3D"_ftnref451" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-f=
amily:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>4</span></sup></a></p>

<p class=3DNormal21 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62SF87M0020000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>We have framed the third </span>=
<a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62SF87M0010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CNX0-0039-P2M3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Winston</span=
></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
factor as &quot;whether there was 'literally nothing left to negotiate.'&qu=
ot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62SF87M0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CNX0-0039-P2M3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Winston</span=
></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CNX0-0039-P2M3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 777 F.2d at=
 82</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(quoting </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62SF87M0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4W-TSM0-003B-G0RV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>R.G. Grp.</sp=
an></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4W-TSM0-003B-G0RV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 751 F.2d at=
 76</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>).
Plaintiffs argue that there was nothing left to negotiate because the terms=
 of
the settlement were already set in the Proposal and were never open to
negotiation. However, before plaintiffs emailed their &nbsp;[*832]&nbsp;
Agreement Schedules, the Republic was not aware of how much money plaintiffs
believed they should be paid or which bonds would be covered by any agreeme=
nt.
Once the Republic did see plaintiffs' submissions, it disagreed with them a=
bout
these essential terms. Accordingly, there was still much left to negotiate.=
</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal21 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62N1RHG0030000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The fourth </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62N1RHG0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CNX0-0039-P2M3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Winston</span=
></i></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62HM6V30020000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> factor asks &quot;whether the
agreement at issue here was the type of contract that was usually put in
writing.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62N1RHG0040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CNX0-0039-P2M3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Winston</span=
></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-CNX0-0039-P2M3-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 777 F.2d at=
 83</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Plaintiffs concede that settlement agreements are the type of contract that=
 is
usually put into writing. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62HM6V30020000400_2"><=
/a><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See, e.g., </i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62HM6V30010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RJX-J6G0-0038-X089-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Ciaramella</s=
pan></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3RJX-J6G0-0038-X089-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 131 F.3d at=
 326</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(&quot;Settlements of any claim are generally required to be in writing or,=
 at
a minimum, made on the record in open court.&quot;). However, plaintiffs in=
sist
that the alleged settlement agreements here were put into writing. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62HM6V30040000400"></a>Plaintiffs ignore the fact t=
hat
the&nbsp;[**14]&nbsp; written agreements were not signed by the Republic.
Because the agreements required countersignatures to be effective, there we=
re
no complete written agreements. As we have observed, &quot;[w]ith [millions=
 of
dollars] at stake, a requirement that [an] agreement be in writing and sign=
ed
simply cannot be a surprise to anyone.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5X9X1J62HM6V30030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4W-TSM0-003B-G0RV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>R.G. Grp.</sp=
an></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4W-TSM0-003B-G0RV-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 751 F.2d at=
 77</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal21 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
sum, the parties intended not to bind themselves to any settlement agreement
until the relevant documents were executed by both parties and exchanged.
Because the Republic did not countersign the agreements, there were no bind=
ing
settlement agreements between plaintiffs and the Republic.</span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn452' href=3D"#_ftn452" name=3D"_ftnref452" titl=
e=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>5</span><=
/sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
The district court was correct to dismiss plaintiffs' Amended Complaint on
