ng
physicians serve as <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>intermediaries<=
/i>
between Defendants' fraudulent omission of Actos's risk of causing bladder
cancer and Plaintiffs' payments for Actos, prescribing physicians do not
constitute an <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>intervening cause</i>=
 to
cut off the chain of proximate cause. <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc6_19"=
></a>An
intervening cause is &quot;a later cause of independent origin that was not
foreseeable.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5XNGX7H2D6N7K0050000400"></a=
><a
