if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
 v.
Porcelli,</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-DGT0-003B-5237-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> 865 F.2d 135=
2</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(2d Cir.), <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>cert. denied,</i> <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FHBSR40K1MNJ1WF0000400"></a><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-st=
yle:
normal'>493 U.S. 810, 107 L. Ed. 2d 22, 110 S. Ct. 53 (1989)</i> (upholding
conviction for mail fraud against <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>M=
cNally</i>
challenge where defendant was charged with defrauding state government of i=
ts
right to sue for sales tax he failed to collect); </span><a
