:contentItem:3S4X-64F0-003B-53D0-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>United States=
 v.
Aiello,</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-64F0-003B-53D0-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> 900 F.2d 528,
530-31 (2d Cir. 1990)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",seri=
f;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>.&nbsp;[**50]&nbsp; <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I1K033T390C000KB5YH0056K"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FHBSR40K1MNJ28M0000400"></a>Upon a showing of such a con=
flict,
a defendant need not demonstrate prejudice because a conflict inhibiting a
lawyer's performance is such an affront to the right to effective assistanc=
e of
counsel that we have found that such a circumstance demonstrates a denial of
that right. <a name=3D"Bookmark_I4FHBSR40K1MNJ28M0000400_2"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I1K033T3JMN000KB5YH0056N"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FHBSR40K1MNJ28P0000400"></a><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-st=
yle:
normal'>Id.</i> We have found a <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>per=
 se</i>
</span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8T9R-T4F2-D6RV-H37N-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
