397-98</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-f=
ont-family:
Times;color:black'>. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>National Mortg=
age</i>
applied this antitrust rule in the RICO context against a defendant who sou=
ght
the benefit of another party's pretrial settlement.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FH5Y1T0K1MNJ0R50000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4N-BCX0-0039-R00P-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>630 F. Supp. =
1149
at 1151</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-=
font-family:
Times;color:black'>. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Cianfrani</i>
involved a withholding from retirement funds payable to a retired legislato=
r of
amounts equal to funds that he had embezzled by placing fictitious employee=
s on
the legislative payroll; the withholding was held not to bar a subsequent R=
ICO
award of treble damages (reduced by the prior withholding) in behalf of the
state against the legislator.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span=
></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FH5Y1T0K1MNJ0R70000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4N-GV70-0039-R2TR-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>600 F. Supp. =
at
1367</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-fon=
t-family:
Times;color:black'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal26 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>None
of these cases involved, as did <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Ban=
kers
Trust</i>, a RICO violation whose central purpose was to prevent the collec=
tion
of a claim or judgment. Accordingly, they do not provide reliable guidance =
for
the resolution of the &quot;lost &nbsp;[**23]&nbsp; debt&quot; issue presen=
ted
by this appeal. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Bankers Trust</i> m=
akes
clear that such a RICO claim does not accrue until it is established that
collection of the claim or judgment has been successfully frustrated. In ot=
her
words, to the extent of a successful collection, the RICO claim is abated <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>pro tanto</i>, prior to any applicatio=
n of
trebling.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal26 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>2. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FH5Y1T0K1MNJ0RB0000400"></a><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-st=
yle:
normal'>Attorney Fees as RICO Damages.</i></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal26><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DNormal26 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>Stochastic contends that <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Bankers Trust</i> &quot;makes it clear=
 that
plaintiff is . . . entitled to recover as [trebled] RICO damages the . . .
legal fees which plaintiff incurred in obtaining the two New Jersey judgmen=
ts .
. . . <a name=3D"Bookmark_I4FH5Y1T0K1MNJ0RD0000400"></a>[</span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FH5Y1T0K1MNJ0R90000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4W-Y060-001B-K0GT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Bankers Trust=
</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4W-Y060-001B-K0GT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 859 F.2d at
1105</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-fon=
t-family:
Times;color:black'>.]&quot; We disagree. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FH5Y1T0K1MNJ0RD0000400_2"></a>Stochastic's argument woul=
d be
equivalent to a ruling in <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Bankers T=
rust</i>
that the attorney fees incurred by the bank during the debtor's initial
bankruptcy proceedings constituted RICO injury. However, Bankers Trust soug=
ht
only past legal fees incurred in (1) fighting the debtor's frivolous satell=
ite
lawsuits; (2) overcoming bribe-induced decisions in South Carolina; and (3)
obtaining a revocation of the initial reorganization plan.<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FH5Y1T0K1MNJ0RC0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4W-Y060-001B-K0GT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>859 F.2d at 1=
105</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
We allowed recovery of such &nbsp;[**24]&nbsp; fees, to the extent not barr=
ed
by the statute of limitations. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id</=
i>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal26 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>This
ruling provides no basis to allow Stochastic to recover the legal fees
initially expended in obtaining the New Jersey judgments. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FH5Y1T0K1MNJ0RG0000400"></a>The asserted RICO violations=
 in
this case are defendants' illegal actions in impeding Stochastic's collecti=
on
of those judgments. The Supreme Court has &nbsp;[*1167]&nbsp; made it clear
that <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc1_24"></a>a RICO injury must stem from=
 and
be proximately caused by a RICO violation. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:=
normal'>See
</i></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4FH5Y1T0K1MNJ0RF0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-9Y60-0039-N48C-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Sedima, S.P.R=
.L.
v. Imrex Co.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4X-9Y60-0039-N48C-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 473 U.S. 47=
9,
496-97, 87 L. Ed. 2d 346, 105 S. Ct. 3275 (1985)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(&quot;plaintiff . . . can only recover to the extent that . . . he has been
injured in his business or property <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'=
>by
the conduct constituting the violation</i>&quot; (emphasis added)); <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>see also </i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FH5Y1T0K1MNJ0RH0000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Holmes v.
Securities Investor Protection Corp.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S65-KJ40-003B-R4CC-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 117 L. Ed. =
2d
532, 112 S. Ct. 1311, 1318-21 (1992)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-fami=
ly:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (articulating
proximate cause requirement for RICO). In the instant case, it cannot plaus=
ibly
be contended that efforts to impede the <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:nor=
mal'>collection</i>
of the New Jersey judgments proximately caused Stochastic's prior expenditu=
re
of legal fees in <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>obtaining</i> the
judgments. Additionally, we perceive no abuse of discretion by the district
court in reducing the legal&nbsp;[**25]&nbsp; fees claimed by Stochastic to
have been spent in its collection efforts from $ 71,976.26 to $ 50,000.</sp=
an></p>

<p class=3DNormal26 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
ht:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I1NKYW806MK00079X8P005WH"></a><a
