Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The district court in <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Capasso</i> immediately proceeded to p=
oint
out, however, that no predicate RICO act of mail or wire fraud had been
established, and to cite cases in which litigation expenses in a prior
litigation were allowed as RICO damages when a RICO violation was proved. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FH5Y1T0K1MNJ0SD0000400"></a><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span></span><a
