href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4N-CP10-001T-7412-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id</span></i>=
</a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4N-CP10-001T-7412-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>. at 842-43</=
span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Further, as discussed <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>supra</i> her=
ein,
we explicitly ruled in <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Bankers Trus=
t</i>
that <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc2_24"></a>legal fees may constitute RI=
CO
damages when they are proximately caused by a RICO violation. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I4FH5Y1T0K1MNJ0SD0000400_2"></a><i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-=
style:
normal'>See </i></span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I4FH5Y1T0K1MNJ0S60000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:3S4W-Y060-001B-K0GT-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Bankers Trust=
</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
