on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5042-D6RV-H0PX-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Section 1964(=
c)</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
also requires a RICO plaintiff to be awarded &nbsp;[**27]&nbsp; &quot;the c=
ost
of the [RICO] suit, including a reasonable attorney's fee.&quot; As describ=
ed <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>supra</i>, Stochastic claimed an attor=
ney's
fee of $ 497,477.24. The district court disallowed $ 80,000 for
&quot;unreasonably excessive litigation,&quot; allocated $ 100,000 to
Stochastic's pursuit of its state law claims, and awarded a fee of $
317,477.24.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal26 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heig=
