<p class=3DNormal18 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:12.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_fnpara_10_8"></a><span style=3D'font-size:9.0pt;mso-bidi-f=
ont-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'=
>A
rational retailer would buy Reliable Johnnie Walker over the other two opti=
ons.
But if the defendants had not smuggled Maryland liquor to New York, the
retailer would have purchased smuggled Johnnie Walker from New Hampshire, n=
ot
Empire's legal Johnnie Walker. In this scenario, Empire would have lost Joh=
nnie
Walker sales no matter what the defendants did, which means that the smuggl=
ing
did not necessarily cause its injuries.</span></p>

