<p class=3DNormal1 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>Moreover,
Kopchik alleges additional facts to plausibly suggest why the Town may have
waited nine months. He alleges that the 90-day period within which he could
file suit as to his 2014 EEOC complaint expired just two months before the =
Town
Board passed its resolution. He claims that the Town may have waited until =
this
time to pass its resolution&nbsp;[**8]&nbsp; so that he could no longer bri=
ng
suit as to those claims. The district court considered this argument and he=
ld
that, if the Town were waiting until the 90-day period expired, it would ha=
ve
been implausible for the Town to wait another two months to retaliate again=
st
Kopchik. We disagree. Assuming the truth of Kopchik's allegations, it would=
 be
plausible for the Town to let some further time pass, so as to conceal its
motivation.</span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn7' href=3D"#_ftn7" name=3D=
"_ftnref7"
title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-f=
amily:
Times'>5</span></sup></a></p>

<p class=3DNormal1 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>In
any event, Kopchik does not rely on temporal proximity alone. Rather, drawi=
ng
all reasonable inferences from the complaint, Kopchik plausibly alleges that
after he filed his EEOC age-discrimination charge, the Town essentially reh=
ired
into similar positions all its ground-and building-maintenance workers exce=
pt
Kopchik, as a pretextual means to terminate his employment. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5V2SRRN28T4C20040000400"></a>It is plausible that the Tow=
n did
so in response to the EEOC charge. These allegations of discriminatory
treatment are thus sufficient to state the causation element of an </span><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dstatutes-legislati=
on&amp;id=3Durn:contentItem:8SG9-5TK2-8T6X-7066-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>ADEA</span></=
i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
retaliation claim. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>See </i></span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5V2SRRN28T4C20030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5GKJ-MJF1-F04K-J09J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Littlejohn</s=
pan></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5GKJ-MJF1-F04K-J09J-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 795 F.3d at=
 319</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal1 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5V2SRRN2N1R9H0010000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>The district court also held tha=
t,
in the absence of indirect evidence of discriminatory treatment based on
temporal proximity, and of other evidence of retaliatory animus, Kopchik was
