similarly situated employee who did not engage in a protected activity,&quo=
t;
and that he failed to do so. App'x 133. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5V2SRRN2N1R9H0030000400"></a>The district court found tha=
t the
&quot;complaint implies . . . that plaintiff was not similarly situated&quo=
t;
to the other Town workers whose maintenance positions were eliminated becau=
se
Kopchik was the only supervisor. <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id=
.</i>
The district court cited to our decision in </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5V2SRRN28T4C20050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:54CC-R7P1-F04K-J045-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Richards-Byer=
s v.
New York City Dep't of Fin.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:54CC-R7P1-F04K-J045-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 449 Fed. Ap=
px.
55, 57 (2d Cir. 2011)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",seri=
f;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5V2SRRN2N1R9H0030000400_2"></a>There, invoking the famili=
ar <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>McDonnell Douglas</i> framework, we st=
ated
that <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc3_0"></a>one of the ways the plaintiff=
 might
have made out a <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>prima facie</i>
retaliation case at summary judgment was to provide &quot;circumstantial
evidence that she was treated differently from any similarly-situated
