<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5NKV27S2D6NKS0050000400"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I13MHJ0W2730007952T003VD"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5NKV27S2HM6T90020000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>F5 asks us to conclude that the
Pappas, Oaktree, and Monarch defendants collectively constitute a control g=
roup
for purposes of the Oceanbulk Merger and Excel transactions.</span><a
style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn19' href=3D"#_ftn19" name=3D"_ftnref19" title=
=3D""><sup><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>10</span>=
</sup></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
That is, F5 contends that we may combine those defendants' individual inter=
ests
in Star Bulk in considering whether there was a controlling shareholder. In
general, defendants' holdings may not be aggregated &quot;to satisfy the
control test absent a voting agreement among the group or a blood pact to a=
ct
together.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5NKV27S2D6NKS0040000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4PDM-7SG0-TXFP-21WB-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Feldman I</sp=
an></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4PDM-7SG0-TXFP-21WB-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 956 A.2d at=
 657</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(internal quotation marks omitted). In other words, a direct action may lie
&quot;if the complaint pleads that a number of shareholders, each of whom
individually cannot exert control over the corporation collectively form a
control group and are connected in some legally significant way&#8212;<i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>e.g.</i>, by contract, common ownershi=
p,
agreement, or some other arrangement&#8212;to work together toward a shared
goal.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5NKV27S2HM6T90010000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:57YW-8781-F04C-G03M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Carsanaro v.
Bloodhound Techs., Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:57YW-8781-F04C-G03M-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 65 A.3d 618,
659 (Del. Ch. 2013)</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> (internal quotation marks and
