Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Importantly, <a
name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc13"></a>the Supreme Court held in <i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Exxon</i> that the &quot;contamination
theory&quot; applies only to the complete diversity requirement and &quot;m=
akes
little sense with respect to the amount-in-controversy
requirement,&nbsp;[**29]&nbsp; which is meant to ensure that a dispute is
sufficiently important to warrant federal-court attention.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5NKV27S2SF8BB0050000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4GG1-N9X0-004B-Y027-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Exxon</span><=
/i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4GG1-N9X0-004B-Y027-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 545 U.S. at=
 562</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
In other words, the amount-in-controversy requirement is claim-specific, but
the complete diversity requirement applies to the entire action. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5NKV27S2HM6TF0030000400"></a>Wright &amp; Miller &sect; 3=
567.2.
<a name=3D"Bookmark_I5NKV27S2HM6TF0030000400_2"></a>To put it yet another w=
ay,
adding a non-diverse party to a case in which federal jurisdiction is
predicated on diversity defeats federal jurisdiction over the entire case, =
but
adding a claim seeking less than the jurisdictional amount in controversy t=
o a
diversity claim that does satisfy the amount-in-controversy requirement does
not. We have explained that the distinction makes sense in light of the
different purposes of each requirement. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5NKV27S2HM6TF0050000400"></a>&quot;The purpose of the
amount-in-controversy requirement . . . is fulfilled by a single claim of
sufficient importance to warrant a federal forum and is not negated by
additional, smaller claims.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5NKV27S2HM6TF0020000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5DGP-NS71-F04K-J0ND-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Pa. Pub. Sch.
Emps</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5DGP-NS71-F04K-J0ND-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>.' Ret. Sys.<=
/span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5DGP-NS71-F04K-J0ND-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 772 F.3d at=
 118</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>
(internal quotation marks omitted). <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5NKV27S2HM6TF0050000400_2"></a>&quot;A failure of diversi=
ty, on
the other hand, . . . takes away any justification for providing a federal
forum.&quot; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>Id.</i> (internal quot=
ation
marks omitted). Ultimately, therefore, &quot;while the amount-in-controversy
requirement is somewhat malleable,&nbsp;[**30]&nbsp; complete diversity of =
all
parties is an absolute, bright-line prerequisite to federal subject matter =
jurisdiction.&quot;
