mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Id.</span></i=
></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4V89-BXS0-TXFX-83BN-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'> at 408</span=
></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>,
quoting S. Rep. No. 109-14, at 4 (2005), <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:no=
rmal'>as
reprinted in</i> 2005 U.S.C.C.A.N. 3, 5. CAFA thus made &quot;it harder for
plaintiffs' counsel to . . . try[] to defeat diversity&quot; to stay in sta=
te
