<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>At
the time that F5's complaint was filed, there were nine members of Star Bul=
k's
board: Petros Pappas, Roger Schmitz, Tom Softeland, Spyros Capralos, Koert
Erhardt, Renee Kemp, Rajath Sourie, Stelios Zavvos, and Emily Stephens. In
order to plead demand futility because of the board's interestedness in the
each challenged transaction, therefore, F5 must allege particularized facts
that raise a reasonable doubt concerning the impartiality of five of the bo=
ard
members. We assume that Pappas was conflicted&nbsp;[**39]&nbsp; with respec=
t to
each transaction. We conclude, however, that, at a minimum, Zavvos, Kemp,
Sourie, Stephens, and Capralos would have been able to consider a pre-suit
demand impartially.</span><a style=3D'mso-footnote-id:ftn26' href=3D"#_ftn2=
6"
name=3D"_ftnref26" title=3D""><sup><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times'>17</span></sup></a><span style=3D'font-famil=
y:
"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'> Thus, F5 has fail=
ed
to plead that demand would have been futile.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;line-height:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>1. <u>Oceanbulk
Merger</u></span></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>The
Oceanbulk Merger is the complaint's principal focus. As explained, the
Oceanbulk Merger was a complex transaction in which Star Bulk acquired
Oceanbulk and its fleet of dry bulk vessels. According to F5, Oceanbulk lost
almost $20 million in the 18 months prior to the merger, making it a poor
investment for Star Bulk that did not have a legitimate business purpose.
Although not directly relevant to discerning the five board members'
impartiality, we note that the Oceanbulk Merger was evaluated and approved =
by a
special committee. That two-person committee included defendants Softeland =
and
Schmitz, and F5 alleges that Schmitz was &quot;hopelessly conflicted&quot;
because of &quot;his relationship with Monarch, a large shareholder, and the
fact that the Oceanbulk Merger was his idea.&quot; Compl. &para; 79 (emphas=
is
omitted). That committee retained Evercore Group LLC (&quot;Evercore&quot;)=
 to
issue a fairness opinion concerning the merger. According to&nbsp;[**40]&nb=
sp;
F5, Evercore's opinion was inadequate because it failed to analyze various
costs and potential pitfalls of the merger in sufficient detail. F5 further
claims that the Evercore opinion was compromised because Evercore would rec=
eive
$2.95 million if the merger was successful, but only $800,000 if the
transaction failed.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>F5's
allegations against the five directors who, in our view, would be impartial=
 in
considering a pre-suit demand are as follows. <a
name=3D"Bookmark_I13MHJ0XSP70007952T003VT"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5NKV27S2SF8BD0020000400"></a>First, F5 alleges that Zavvos
served on the board of Zeus Capital Partners, L.P., a private equity real
estate fund, with Pappas. Zavvos and Pappas also serve together on the boar=
d of
West Invest AG, another private equity fund. According to F5, Zavvos's
&quot;substantial business entanglements with Pappas&quot; mean that he can=
not
&quot;impartially consider a demand on the Board.&quot; App. Reply Br. 10. =
Its
allegations concerning the Zavvos-Pappas relationship are plainly insuffici=
ent,
especially &nbsp;[*85]&nbsp; in light of the requirement to plead
particularized facts, because <a name=3D"Bookmark_LNHNREFclscc20"></a>under
Delaware law a &quot;mere personal friendship or . . . outside business
relationship&quot; does not &quot;raise a reasonable doubt about a director=
's
independence.&quot; </span><a name=3D"Bookmark_I5NKV27S2SF8BD0010000400"></=
a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4C3V-D4M0-0039-41FS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Beam ex rel.
Martha Stewart Living Omnimedia, Inc.</span></i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:4C3V-D4M0-0039-41FS-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 845 A.2d at
1050</span></i></a><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-fon=
t-family:
Times;color:black'>.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I13MHJ0XXHC0007952T003VV"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5NKV27S2SF8BD0040000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:black'>Zavvos's alleged business
relationship with&nbsp;[**41]&nbsp; Pappas is entirely unlike relationships
that the Delaware courts have found sufficiently close to raise a reasonable
doubt concerning director independence. For example, the Delaware Supreme C=
ourt
recently held that co-ownership of a private plane with an admittedly
conflicted director was sufficient to raise a reasonable doubt concerning t=
he
independence of a director. Co-ownership of the plane was an &quot;unusual
fact&quot; that &quot;signaled an extremely close, personal bond between&qu=
ot;
the two directors &quot;and between their families.&quot; </span><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5NKV27S2SF8BD0030000400"></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5MB8-4Y61-F04C-K00W-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>Sandys</span>=
</i></a><a
href=3D"https://plus.lexis.com/api/document?collection=3Dcases&amp;id=3Durn=
:contentItem:5MB8-4Y61-F04C-K00W-00000-00&amp;context=3D"><i
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Times",ser=
if;
mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:#0077CC;background:white'>, 152 A.3d at=
 130</span></i></a><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times",serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Times;color:blac=
k'>.
Those circumstances were &quot;suggestive of the type of very close personal
relationship that, like family ties, one would expect to heavily influence a
human's ability to exercise impartial judgment.&quot; <i style=3D'mso-bidi-=
font-style:
normal'>Id.</i> F5 does not allege such a bond between Zavvos and Pappas he=
re;
it merely pleads that they served together on two other boards of directors=
 and
includes no particularized allegations concerning the details of their busi=
ness
or personal relationship. F5 has therefore failed to raise a reasonable dou=
bt
concerning Zavvos's independence.</span></p>

<p class=3DNormal2 style=3D'margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-heigh=
t:15.0pt'><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I13MHJ0Y2BH0007952T003VW"></a><a
name=3D"Bookmark_I5NKV27S2SF8BF0010000400"></a><span style=3D'font-family:"=
Times",serif;
